// Words: Jonathan's canonical commentary txt. Structure: his Notion pages.
import type { V205BookData } from '../types';

export const DATA: V205BookData = {
  book: "Psalms",
  display: "Psalms",
  chapters: {
    "1": {"chapter":1,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a lot to talk about in these amazing parts of scripture. Psalms is one of those books of the Bible that may seem tedious, and sometimes repetitive, but there is a much grander purpose behind their placement, as well as their overarching theme to scripture. I would consider the book of Psalms as the backbone of scripture. It holds the Bible together and connect EVERYTHING."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will cover pain, testing, trials, joy, salvation, longing, patience, peace, safety... The list goes on forever, but it will also cover prophecy, dedication, purpose, and it will do it all through a mode in which God has taken very serious importance to... worship."},{"kind":"para","text":"God cares very much about worship. It's a theme that is constantly harped on through scripture. In fact, one of the first things that Moses did when he travelled with the Israelites in the wilderness was sing a song of worship."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now therefore write ye this song for you, and teach it the children of Israel: put it in their mouths, that this song may be a witness for me against the children of Israel.","ref":"Deuteronomy 31:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"It's the major theme of David, and it's passed down to his sons as well, particularly Solomon (the author of Song of Solomon). It's also something that the Apostles spoke very highly of as being a pleasing sound to the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Speaking to yourselves in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing and making melody in your heart to the Lord;","ref":"Ephesians 5:19"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let the word of Christ dwell in you richly in all wisdom; teaching and admonishing one another in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing with grace in your hearts to the Lord.","ref":"Colossians 3:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"And it's something that all the saints of the Lord will be doing for all of eternity..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they sung as it were a new song before the throne, and before the four beasts, and the elders: and no man could learn that song but the hundred and forty and four thousand, which were redeemed from the earth.","ref":"Revelation 14:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"Worship is something special to the Lord, and it's something we should get use to at this moment if we are going to be spending an eternity in it. God loves our worship, and the Psalmists show us just how that is done. Each Psalm has a unique perspective, but they all lead to the same exact thing. Glorifying the Lord and pointing to Jesus Christ. The book of Psalms is the glue that holds all of scripture together, and I believe that is why it's one of the longest books, and why it's right in the middle of the Bible..."}],"previously":[],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"A Poor or Blessed Perspective","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Right off the batt, David gives us the differences between a blessed (or happy) man, and a miserable (or nonblessed) man and what that looks like."},{"kind":"para","text":"The blessed man is someone that knows the right people to talk to."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows who would give him good advice, and would be able to lift him up for the right reasons."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's someone who doesn't try and be like the rest of the world in going after ungodly things, or purposely trying to reject the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's someone who doesn't try and look for problems and try and make enemies with everyone around him."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a great deal of people today who do not feel blessed."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some of those people are even Christians."},{"kind":"para","text":"They say, \"I am a Christian. I know who God is, and I know what Christ has done for me.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"But, really, the question is, \"Do you take unwise counsel from ungodly people? Do you walk after the world and stand in the way of sinners? Do you sit in the seat of the scornful and make issues with those who are righteous and good?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Many times the issue is not that we are in the world, but rather the issue is we are too much LIKE the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"We become so use to being in the world that we don't realize how much it has affected our walk with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not blessed, because we are not in the right place spiritually."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is what a blessed person would do..."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You say, \"God's law doesn't seem like something that would really bring me joy.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"This isn't just speaking about God's law specifically."},{"kind":"para","text":"At that time, the only word they had from the Lord was God's law."},{"kind":"para","text":"They meditated on God's WORD, not just the law."},{"kind":"para","text":"They didn't just pick apart Leviticus and leave out Exodus, and Genesis and Deuteronomy."},{"kind":"para","text":"No, they delighted in every part of God's Word, and seeing as all they had was God's law at the time, their delight was found in that alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"They had less of a Bible than we do today, and they had great blessings by delighting in what little they had."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have far more to soak in and be thankful for, and yet many of us feel that we are not blessed."},{"kind":"para","text":"You are blessed to be living in a time when you have much more of God's Word to meditate on."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have more than just the Ten Commandments to contemplate on."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's law is not just the Ten Commandments to a believer today."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's law is Christ's commandments."},{"kind":"para","text":"He tells us multiple commands through His ministry, but I think it's wise for us to meditate on at least 10 of them (if you don't know the ten commandments too, I highly suggest you look into them and find a form of memorizing them)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ's ten commands are:"},{"kind":"para","text":"1) Repent"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"From that time Jesus began to preach, and to say, Repent: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.","ref":"Matthew 4:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"2) Love God"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he answering said, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy strength, and with all thy mind; and thy neighbour as thyself.","ref":"Luke 10:27"},{"kind":"para","text":"3) Love Others"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A new commandment I give unto you, That ye love one another; as I have loved you, that ye also love one another.","ref":"John 13:34"},{"kind":"para","text":"4) Seek the Kingdom"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you.","ref":"Matthew 6:33"},{"kind":"para","text":"5) Minister"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But it shall not be so among you: but whosoever will be great among you, let him be your minister; And whosoever will be chief among you, let him be your servant: Even as the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.","ref":"Matthew 20:26-28"},{"kind":"para","text":"6) Be Examples"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.","ref":"Matthew 5:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"7) Pray"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore I say unto you, What things soever ye desire, when ye pray, believe that ye receive them, and ye shall have them.","ref":"Mark 11:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"8) Preach"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said unto them, Go ye into all the world, and preach the gospel to every creature.","ref":"Mark 16:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"9) Baptise"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Go ye therefore, and teach all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Ghost:","ref":"Matthew 28:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"10) Wait On His Return"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Watch therefore: for ye know not what hour your Lord doth come.","ref":"Matthew 24:42"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is just to name a few."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's law is worth meditating on, absolutely, but we should not just be limited to the law of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be doing as David really implies here and meditate on God's WORD."},{"kind":"para","text":"All of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is only His Word that provides us with blessing and \"delight.\""}]}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"title":"A Blessed Man Is Sustained","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When we fully encompass ourselves with God's Word, we become FRUITFUL."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is amazing, because we are told that Jesus IS God's Word in the flesh. \"And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.\" John 1:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"And then Jesus says we cannot produce any fruit without Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Abide in me, and I in you. As the branch cannot bear fruit of itself, except it abide in the vine; no more can ye, except ye abide in me. I am the vine, ye are the branches: He that abideth in me, and I in him, the same bringeth forth much fruit: for without me ye can do nothing.","ref":"John 15:4-5"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus uses this example of a tree planted by the rivers of water to describe the life of a born again believer."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are abiding in God's Word (that doesn't mean we just visit it, it means we LIVE in it), then we will be blessed, and we will be able to produce some amazing works that would benefit not just ourselves, but anyone else that we are around."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everything we do (if we are living in His Word) will prosper, because we will not be doing it out of a selfish ambition to just simply get things done and make ourselves look good."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will be doing it with the ultimate response of seeing God get the glory."},{"kind":"para","text":"We want to raise Him up, not ourselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are not abiding in God's Word, we will never be able to do that."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"Being Rooted or Uprooted","entries":[{"start":4,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are not sustained by the Word of God and the faith of Christ will not be able to stand through any judgement or trials."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will be easily carried away."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have nothing firm to give them hope."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have no hope to cling onto."},{"kind":"para","text":"A chaff is a seed that's been separated from threshing."},{"kind":"para","text":"You could think of it like a dandelion."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our front yard has some dandelions growing in it, and my daughter likes to pluck them up and blow the little dandelion seeds all over the lawn, so then they grow more and more until there are so many dandelions that I can't keep up with them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those plants are popping up in other people's yards because of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are, ultimately, weeds, and they are not very pleasant things to have."},{"kind":"para","text":"The ungodly people are just like the dandelions."},{"kind":"para","text":"They think they are special, and outwardly they seem like a significant thing, but they are not really good for anything except spreading into other people's yards and ruining people's gardens."},{"kind":"para","text":"The righteous are like fruit trees, useful for sustainability."},{"kind":"para","text":"The unrighteous are like dandelions, useful to ruin people's hard work."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only way to get rid of dandelions is to cut them, and kill them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Plucking them out by the root is helpful, but spraying them with weed killer is even better."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are not benefiting the world and the cause of Christ will not be able to stand in the day of judgement."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will not be able to say \"Well I was just doing my job. That's what I was taught to do. I was taught to destroy other people's lawns.\" especially because they had the option to become useful, fruitful trees planted in assurance and righteousness."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Does this mean that God does not know the way of the unrighteous?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't believe so."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe that God knows the way of both, but He is only able to bless ONE."},{"kind":"para","text":"The ungodly will be punished for what they do that is ungodly."},{"kind":"para","text":"The righteous will be blessed for what they do in righteousness."},{"kind":"para","text":"These are really the only two options."},{"kind":"para","text":"You cannot stay stagnant and say \"Well I did neither, so therefore what will God do with me now?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"If you do nothing, that is unrighteous."},{"kind":"para","text":"Dandelions don't have to walk to the lawn nextdoor."},{"kind":"para","text":"The wind blows them there."},{"kind":"para","text":"The wind directs and guides them, and they just allow it to happen."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether the unrighteous know it or not, God takes them to their next steps."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is opportunity for them to become new creatures in every step they take in this life, but God also knows that they won't."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the end, God will have no choice but to punish the unjust, and ungodly things of this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Two options for the people of Earth are given here."},{"kind":"para","text":"One leads to righteousness and security."},{"kind":"para","text":"The other leads to wandering, confusion, and punishment."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":6}]},
    "2": {"chapter":2,"intro":[],"previously":["In our first chapter of this book, we got a look at the purpose for these writings of the Psalms, and how they will ultimately be dealt with throughout each chapter. Each psalm has it's own theme, yet with one over-arching theme throughout all of them. The theme is upon Jesus, but the different Psalms have different stages of our walk in life with Christ. Much of our perspective of the world today should be viewed through the eyes of the Psalms. There will be several things addressed through Psalm 1 like the fact that there will be prophesy, songs, and acts of worship, as well as valuable lessons for us to grasp and utilize as we read.","This chapter is no exception. There is a lot of learn and take from this, but there is a very important message that must be ministered to in our lives that David looks at here. Whether we are in a position of leadership or not, we must take account of how we are leading, and if we are leading with the proper motives/perspective."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"The Leaders Defiled","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David starts this Psalm off with a question."},{"kind":"para","text":"A good question at that."},{"kind":"para","text":"His focus here is on issues with the Gentiles and Hebrews."},{"kind":"para","text":"The \"heathen\" were gentile people."},{"kind":"para","text":"They were people who usually worshipped their traditions and fake gods rather than the God of Israel."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is assumed that the \"people\" mentioned here are the Israelites."},{"kind":"para","text":"So we have Gentiles who are angry, and Israelites who are distracted."},{"kind":"para","text":"What could make them be this way?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well David answers it in the next verse..."}]},{"start":2,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We have a very big problem when there are people who are in leadership that desire to hurt, inflict pain, or destroy anything and anyone that the Lord has anointed or set up."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm not even just talking about political leadership either."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have leaders in the church (since the time of David and beyond) that have abused their position and have devised plans against the Lord and His anointed."},{"kind":"para","text":"The word \"anointed\" here actually comes from the Hebrew Word which means \"Messiah.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Worse than attacking Christians (or God's children) is that they are seeking to attack Christ specifically."},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course that is all they did when Jesus had His ministry."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at this..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The man departed, and told the Jews that it was Jesus, which had made him whole. And therefore did the Jews persecute Jesus, and sought to slay him, because he had done these things on the sabbath day.","ref":"John 5:15-16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus did a lot of amazing things."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some of His first miracles were mistreated by the religious leaders of His day."},{"kind":"para","text":"Ultimately, when He is brought to the cross, it is by the authority of the religious rulers that take Him there."},{"kind":"para","text":"The politicians of that day were no better."},{"kind":"para","text":"They had the ultimate say so, but they conspired with the religious rulers to do the most heinous things to the Messiah."},{"kind":"para","text":"David is questioning their ethics and decisions."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why would they feel this way?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Why do they hate the Lord that much?"},{"kind":"para","text":"What makes them so angry about God and His people?"}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"God's Perspective","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Even with all their hate, and their plans of torment to the anointed of the Lord, God just laughs at their foolishness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Does God think that their anger and evil is funny?"},{"kind":"para","text":"No."},{"kind":"para","text":"He thinks that their anger and evil is pitiful."},{"kind":"para","text":"The bigger they puff themselves up to be, the smaller they are to the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But he giveth more grace. Wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble.","ref":"James 4:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"Proverbs is a book full of insight on the life of a proud fool."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously (seeing as Proverbs is written by David's own son) he learned a thing or two from his father's perspective on terrible leadership (possibly as well as Solomon's own leadership)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Battling against the Lord in this age is a foolish and hilarious thing."},{"kind":"para","text":"You can do whatever you want on this Earth, and you can hurt whomever you want, but in the end it will be God who has the say so."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The atheist may think a very small thing about the wrath of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"They may think it's okay to play games with God, and live in a fairytale world trying to convince themselves (against their own conscience mind you) that there is no God."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many religions who have gone against the Lord and His anointed."},{"kind":"para","text":"Many of which have added works to their religion instead of simply accepting Christ as the final end all be all of our faith."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those people, those are the ones that God laughs at."},{"kind":"para","text":"They think they are clever (and most are doing it for money, or for some sort of recognition) but in the end, God has nothing but wrath stored up for them."},{"kind":"para","text":"You can deny God's wrath all you want, but that will not remove His wrath from being poured upon those that hate Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the wrath of God is revealed from heaven against all ungodliness and unrighteousness of men, who hold the truth in unrighteousness;","ref":"Romans 1:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"You might ask, \"If they hold the truth, then how can they still live in unrighteousness?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no one that is without excuse."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Christian has done a decent job at sharing the truth of God's Word around the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are not many places today (there are still some) who have not hurt the gospel in one form or another."},{"kind":"para","text":"These people hold the truth of God's Word, and yet they still reject it and live their lives as if it doesn't really matter."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Atheist is a prime example of this."},{"kind":"para","text":"They hold the truth, but they refuse to listen to it, and both David and Paul say that God's wrath is revealed to them."},{"kind":"para","text":"How has it been revealed?"},{"kind":"para","text":"It's been revealed in a threefold way."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is revealed by their own conscience (they know that what they say and believe is completely wrong they just don't want to admit it)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Which shew the work of the law written in their hearts, their conscience also bearing witness, and their thoughts the mean while accusing or else excusing one another;)","ref":"Romans 2:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"God's wrath is revealed in their life as they try to live it ignoring the obvious signs that God is seeking their attention."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that believeth on the Son hath everlasting life: and he that believeth not the Son shall not see life; but the wrath of God abideth on him.","ref":"John 3:36"},{"kind":"para","text":"These people will be literally living in God's wrath."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's more terrifying than trying to pretend like it doesn't exist and living in a fairytale land."},{"kind":"para","text":"But God's wrath was also revealed through His own Son."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Yet it pleased the LORD to bruise him; he hath put him to grief: when thou shalt make his soul an offering for sin, he shall see his seed, he shall prolong his days, and the pleasure of the LORD shall prosper in his hand. He shall see of the travail of his soul, and shall be satisfied: by his knowledge shall my righteous servant justify many; for he shall bear their iniquities.","ref":"Isaiah 53:10-11"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us. Much more then, being now justified by his blood, we shall be saved from wrath through him.","ref":"Romans 5:8-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"The wrath of God is satisfied through the sacrifice of His perfect Son who did no sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus fulfilled God's wrath by living a perfectly sinless life and dying on the cross for our sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that reject Christ, will dwell in God's wrath."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that sear their conscience will dwell in God's wrath."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that hide their life from the Lord will dwell in God's wrath."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether they want to believe it or not, God's wrath dwells with those that desire to have it."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is on the throne."},{"kind":"para","text":"David understands this all too well."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites wanted a king just like the rest of the world had, because they were too scared to rely on the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They wanted someone they could tangibly see, and someone who would have to be physically there with them."},{"kind":"para","text":"There was too much trust to be had in an invisible and mighty God that they were too afraid to actually talk too."},{"kind":"para","text":"So God let them do it."},{"kind":"para","text":"And it didn't work out for them."},{"kind":"para","text":"David becomes a great king, and it's not because David was a perfect or great man."},{"kind":"para","text":"Saul's kingdom falls apart because he never placed God in His proper place."},{"kind":"para","text":"He abused people, and he abused his position of power, and the people were hurt from that (including David)."},{"kind":"para","text":"David puts the Lord on the kings throne."},{"kind":"para","text":"Above all earthly kings, the Lord must sit and dictate, and David was wise enough to see and use that."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":9,"title":"The Lord Is Alive","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a lot of speculation and assumptions about what this verse means, and the best way we can identify the meaning of a questionable verse is to back it up with scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"Surely this is used somewhere else in the Bible."},{"kind":"para","text":"If it is not, then we take the best representation based on the rest of the context of this chapter to illustrate what it truly means."},{"kind":"para","text":"Thankfully, we have an accurate description of what is being talked about here because Paul uses this verse in a sermon that he preaches in the book of Acts"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"God hath fulfilled the same unto us their children, in that he hath raised up Jesus again; as it is also written in the second psalm, Thou art my Son, this day have I begotten thee.","ref":"Acts 13:33"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is not talking about the birth of Jesus (as some religions might try and assume)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ has no beginning, so it can't be talking about that (especially because He had no bodily form until well after David was past and gone)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Paul says that Christ was born from Joseph's tomb."},{"kind":"para","text":"The day that the Lord speaks of in this verse about begetting His Son is the day He rose again from the dead."},{"kind":"para","text":"How do we know that God means this here?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well (other than the fact that Paul gives us further clarity) David continues to explain in the next verses..."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Through Christ's resurrection, Christ rules and reigns."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has always ruled, but His kingdom was established the moment He rose again from the dead."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus answered, My kingdom is not of this world: if my kingdom were of this world, then would my servants fight, that I should not be delivered to the Jews: but now is my kingdom not from hence.","ref":"John 18:36"},{"kind":"para","text":"The moment He rises again He sits down next to His Father."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"To him that overcometh will I grant to sit with me in my throne, even as I also overcame, and am set down with my Father in his throne.","ref":"Revelation 3:21"},{"kind":"para","text":"He can do what He pleases."},{"kind":"para","text":"When David wrote this, I don't believe he understood the death of the Lord quite yet."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe he understood there would be a Savior, that had been promised over and over again, but I don't think he fully understood what he was writing here."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Holy Spirit had other plans for it though, far beyond what David could ever understand."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This further proves the fact that this is speaking about Christ's second coming."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ came and preached a message of grace and truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"It was a message of salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"He did not come and \"break them with a rod of iron...\" and \"dash them in pieces...\""},{"kind":"para","text":"No, He will do that when He comes back."},{"kind":"para","text":"His first coming was to set up the kingdom and establish it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It was to prepare the people for what was to come next."},{"kind":"para","text":"His second coming is to reign forever."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":12,"title":"Kiss The Son","entries":[{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is only one way to lead correctly, and sadly we will continue to see leaders miss this over and over again."},{"kind":"para","text":"Politicians, and religious leaders, and all sorts of corporate heads all have this in common."},{"kind":"para","text":"They look for ways to build their image, rather than displaying the image of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"We see this with even the most Godly of corporations."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have seen this happen with Chick-Fil-A a few times."},{"kind":"para","text":"Hobby Lobby has lost it's focus on God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sears is nearly nonexistent at this point."},{"kind":"para","text":"Forever 21 has fallen and rotten away."},{"kind":"para","text":"Walmart will eventually become a distant memory."},{"kind":"para","text":"The list goes on."},{"kind":"para","text":"The more we try and make ourselves look good and drive our motives on money and fame, the less grace God will deliver to us, and the more we will live in agony and defeat."},{"kind":"para","text":"Wisdom is not found in your own personal goals and beliefs."},{"kind":"para","text":"Wisdom is found in Christ and moving forward in God's Will with whatever direction He deems worthy to go."},{"kind":"para","text":"Here's what they must do..."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is quite an interesting verse given to us here."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Kiss the Son...\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We know of at least one person who kissed the Son (capital \"S\" mind you), and we know that did not work out very well for him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe the reason he betrays him with a kiss is because this scripture is a prophecy."},{"kind":"para","text":"Judas (unknowingly) fulfilled a prophecy by giving Christ a kiss."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, I know there are a lot of arguments about God's sovereignty and predestination and all that from the Hyper- Calvinists today."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many who would say, \"God did not give Judas a choice.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"But I believe God did."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe Christ did too."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moment Christ was kissed He called Judas \"friend.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"He reminded Judas who He was."},{"kind":"para","text":"Judas didn't take the hint however, and instead ends up hanging himself."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe that Judas could have turned that kiss around and used it to be blessed."},{"kind":"para","text":"He could have trusted in Christ as that moment, but he chooses not to."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that kiss the Lord, must kiss Him for who He actually is, and for no other reason at all."},{"kind":"para","text":"May we not be like Judas with the motive to betray God and try and inflict pain on the Lord's anointed."},{"kind":"para","text":"This Psalm should be very close to our hearts."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":12}]},
    "3": {"chapter":3,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last chapter, we read about the leaders being defiled by ungodly people in the world, what God's perspective is on the issue, and the fact that the Lord lives (Christ is risen). We also talked about \"kissing the son\" which was an interesting take on the betrayal of Christ (worth going back and reading).","In this chapter we continue to read about the thoughts of David, and how the Lord uses him during times of great turmoil and trouble. It seems everything is against David, and there is no way to move forward with the help of others around him. In fact, it seems that everyone around him doesn't want him to move forward at all."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Discouraged From All Sides","entries":[{"start":1,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are a couple things to address right of the batt here in this Psalm."},{"kind":"para","text":"David seems to be in a place in life where he is feeling quite discouraged."},{"kind":"para","text":"There would be many people would tell him that he was lost and forsaken."},{"kind":"para","text":"He would feel as if the whole world were against him, as well as the Lord Himself."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've been to churches that preach this kind of message."},{"kind":"para","text":"They make you feel alone, forgotten, and altogether invaluable."},{"kind":"para","text":"They make you feel like you are nothing more than redeemed trash."},{"kind":"para","text":"David is feeling like trash, and maybe he is, but the Lord found value in him, and had made him something far more useful than trash could ever be."},{"kind":"para","text":"This should be a reminder to the reader as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are ever feeling like trash, or you are ever feeling invaluable, think about how much value the Lord has given to you through His sacrifice for you on the cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"He literally DIED because He found so much value in you that it was worth dying for."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For ye are bought with a price: therefore glorify God in your body, and in your spirit, which are God's.","ref":"1 Corinthians 6:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"No matter what a preacher might tell you about your value, the Bible is extremely clear that Christs say on the matter is far heavier."},{"kind":"para","text":"The second thing we notice in this Psalm is the word \"Selah.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"This is the first time we are introduced to it in this book."},{"kind":"para","text":"There has been a lot of debate about what the word means, but I have come to understand it as a \"Musicians Pause.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"When I was teaching the youth in Texas, I preached a short sermon series on \"Being Still,\" or \"Pausing for God.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The premise being that we should learn how to wait in a world that is so busy trying to get to the top or trying to be noticed about every little thing."},{"kind":"para","text":"This was for a camp week, and one of the nights we had an arts night."},{"kind":"para","text":"One of the teens painted a picture about this word \"Selah,\" and in the picture she wrote the word, and then added a heart with it that formed the shape of the word and a \"semi- colon.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"\"What's the semi-colon?\" I asked."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Well,\" she said, \"When you explained the word as a 'musicians pause' I thought of it as a semi-colon. It tells you to stop, pause, and think about what you just read.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"I couldn't give a clearer picture if I tried."},{"kind":"para","text":"These Selah's will be good for us to utilize so we can stop, pause, and think about what you just read."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every time we see one it would be wise of us to stop, and think."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"title":"God Listens","entries":[{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think these verses give us an appropriate understanding as to why the pauses are there now."},{"kind":"para","text":"The first two verses read as if David is downcast, and would never see a good day again after the amount of torment he has received from those around him (including from the people he loves)."},{"kind":"para","text":"But in these two verses it seems his countenance is lifted higher than the heavens."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well because he took a moment to stop, pause, and think about what he had just said."},{"kind":"para","text":"He understands that it doesn't matter what the world may say about him."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world has a lot to say about Christians who are living for the Lord and who are completely sold out for the cross and cause of Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will always hear about how disgusting we are as humans because we choose to love people rather than hate people, but does our strength come from the hurtful things that people say?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course not."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our strength comes from the Lord in which we serve."},{"kind":"para","text":"They can throw all sorts of accusations our way, but the Lord is our shield."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord will lift up our heads."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will be glorified."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will be our rejoicing."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we ever feel like we are overburdened, or discouraged in our ministry and lives, may we go to the Lord and cry to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've spent a great deal of nights crying to the Lord for a new Spirit to be lifted in me, and often it takes longer than I desire."},{"kind":"para","text":"Through those times, however, I find that sitting in my depressed state, or sitting with the pain is the only way for me to understand how needful I am of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I cannot do anything without Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am a lost puppy in need of a good master who would take care of my needs."},{"kind":"para","text":"Without Him, I am undone."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Casting all your care upon him; for he careth for you.","ref":"1 Peter 5:7"}]}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"title":"A New Morning","entries":[{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Every morning is a fresh look at life."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be renewed every morning."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"It is of the LORD's mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not. They are new every morning: great is thy faithfulness.","ref":"Lamentations 3:22-23"},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't matter what people said yesterday."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't matter what you did yesterday."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't matter how you fell yesterday."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a new morning, and God has given you fresh breath in your lungs."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's time to start fresh, and new, and it's time to be zealous for the Lord and His love for you."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't matter what the day looks like ahead, as long as God grants you another new day tomorrow, you could face a thousand people who are ready to (literally) fight you, and it wouldn't matter because you have the Lord on your side."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not lost."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not incapable."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not without."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not encumbered."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not destroyed."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even if we are, we have one that seeks us, who desires to be present with us, who gives us strength, who gives us sustenance, who takes our burdens, and brings us to safety."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"title":"Salvation Given","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I've had my fair share of fights in the day."},{"kind":"para","text":"The last place you want to get hit is in the face."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, in both karate, and kick-boxing (probably others as well, I have not done anything other than those two) they tell you to guard your face more than anything else."},{"kind":"para","text":"Your reflexes (actually) are pretty good at making sure your face stays protected."},{"kind":"para","text":"David probably knew a thing or two about being punched in the face as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is okay with his enemies being punched in the face, but not through his own will, but rather through the will of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He desires that God would take care of those that are ungodly, and unruly, and are out to get the people that God has chosen for himself."},{"kind":"para","text":"God chose David, we must make that clear."},{"kind":"para","text":"There were kings and authorities all around the land that were out to make sure David failed."},{"kind":"para","text":"They didn't want to see the Lord succeed."},{"kind":"para","text":"God, however, has the bigger plan and purpose."},{"kind":"para","text":"God greatly used David, and that might have been a few hits to the face here and there, but the ultimate punches were thrown from the Lord, taking people down where they needed to be."},{"kind":"para","text":"A punch to the face is a pretty quick way to take someone down."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This verse is extremely important."},{"kind":"para","text":"You think to our modern church age where there are many religions who have this idea that Salvation is something you earn, or something you are able to obtain."},{"kind":"para","text":"The great king David says, salvation is something that belongs to God."},{"kind":"para","text":"God gets to use salvation how God see's fit."},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot obtain it."},{"kind":"para","text":"The blessing is upon God's chosen people."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's upon those that He has called."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Who is called then?\" you might ask."},{"kind":"para","text":"All of us are!"},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are called have the chance to be born again."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, there are those who reject the calling of salvation, and therefore will not be a part of God's chosen people."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the Old Testament, the chosen people of God are the Israelites."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the New Testament, the chosen people of God is the church."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's a topic for a different time."},{"kind":"para","text":"The point of the matter is, salvation is not a sweet reward for a life well lived."},{"kind":"para","text":"Salvation is a gift given to those that accept God's calling."},{"kind":"para","text":"David understands this, and so he makes it very clear here that there is nothing that he can do to earn God's salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"He just has to rest in the fact that God will save, and has promised to save those who are accepting it."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8}]},
    "4": {"chapter":4,"intro":[],"previously":["I have no doubt that when David wrote these Psalms (at least in the majority) he was feeling hurt and troubled. He felt discouraged more times than encouraged, and that is encouraging to us because we know we are not alone when we are going through a trial. In our last chapter, David reminds us of this.","In this chapter, David continues to remind us about what we should do through our discouragement, and why we should be weary about trusting the voice of people, rather than the Word of God."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"David Cries Out","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"A Neginoth is some sort of stringed instrument."},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems that David was playing this Psalm to music."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've written quite a lot of music in my day."},{"kind":"para","text":"Played a lot of music."},{"kind":"para","text":"Still play music (praise the Lord)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whenever I would write music, I would put myself into a very deep depressed anguishing state."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Was it because I enjoyed that place?"},{"kind":"para","text":"No."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, I hated that place with every fiber of my being."},{"kind":"para","text":"I placed myself there because in order to make people feel your music, YOU need to feel your music."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you don't feel for your music, others will not feel for it either."},{"kind":"para","text":"David seems to understand this, and so he is in an emotionally deep state when writing this Psalm."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is crying to the Lord for help and guidance and desperately needs the Lord to answer."},{"kind":"para","text":"David uses the word \"distress\" here which is an extremely applicable verse for us today."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are all in some mode (or will be) in distress."},{"kind":"para","text":"Hearing and seeing the Lord work through our distress is what we really need."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will not find much encouragement from the people and world around us (sadly), and so we must rely on the great Psychologist to relieve our worries."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Take a moment and think about what David is saying here."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Selah is there so we stop and think."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Leasing\" means \"falsehood\" or \"a lie.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems the people around David were constantly seeking to bring him down."},{"kind":"para","text":"They were trying their best to rob David of his victories."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, we can look at this and say, \"David was pretty prideful and selfish if all he cares about were his own victories.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We would miss David's emotional state if we think of him like this."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Psalms seriously delve into the mind of David (and the mind of Christian musicians)."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are going to get the proper context, we must know the musician first."},{"kind":"para","text":"It would do us well to have a good study of David through 1&2 Samuel before coming to the book of Psalms, but if we do not do so, we should get a quick glimpse into who David is."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when he had removed him, he raised up unto them David to be their king; to whom also he gave testimony, and said, I have found David the son of Jesse, a man after mine own heart, which shall fulfil all my will.","ref":"Acts 13:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"Was David perfect?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Absolutely not (we will even see his imperfections in the book of Psalms), but you could not blame David for being a lazy follower of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everything David did was chased with what would bring God glory."},{"kind":"para","text":"There were hiccups, I won't deny that, but there was always a turning back to the Lord and a prayer of revival in David."},{"kind":"para","text":"David, here, is not seeking glory for himself because of his victories."},{"kind":"para","text":"David just wants God to work, and if people all around him are constantly battling David, or battling God even (or even battling David because of his faith in God) then these people should face God's judgement and wrath!"},{"kind":"para","text":"All they were doing was adding fuel to an evil fire that (left unchecked) could spiral out of control."},{"kind":"para","text":"David wanted his people to be happy in the Lord, and they were rejecting God left and right."},{"kind":"para","text":"David even says they were \"leasing\" or \"lying\" about what and who David really was."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't know if you've ever been in a position where someone has lied about your character, but it is not a very fun place to be."},{"kind":"para","text":"David was not the man that people were claiming him to be."},{"kind":"para","text":"He did not seek the glory, he sought the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"These people, were trying to take away the Lord's glory and David is very concerned about it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Especially because he was the face that people would blame for believing in the lies of others."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, after we've sat and thought about what David says here, David has a tempo shift."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has a mood shift in his lyrics."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is pretty common after a \"Selah\" takes place."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"title":"Stop and Be Still","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David has sat with his prayers in the previous two verses and now he hears the Lord's response."},{"kind":"para","text":"God reveals to David that He will take care of those that are set apart by Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will not let anyone that is His own go without guidance."},{"kind":"para","text":"David seems to know that God has listened to his cry, and David is confident that anyone else who cries to Him will be heard."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a great deal of people today crying to God and feeling that God is not listening."},{"kind":"para","text":"They feel as if God can't hear their voices."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some have grown weary in their crying, and are ready to give up."},{"kind":"para","text":"David will mention this later, but I think it's suffice to bring up now..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"They that sow in tears shall reap in joy.","ref":"Psalm 126:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"We should also understand that if we give up before the Lord answers, we might not see the Lord answer our cries."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And let us not be weary in well doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not.","ref":"Galatians 6:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes, living for the Lord, crying to the Lord, and depending on the Lord seems like a very lost hope."},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems that we are leaning on nothing, crying to nothing, and depending on nothing."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has a very interesting way to answer."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then there are times when God gives us immense peace and understanding."},{"kind":"para","text":"He gives us a hope beyond what we can comprehend."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might not be able to hold onto those times forever because God desires to put us in a state of need and distress."},{"kind":"para","text":"Here, David was in distress, yet God granted him hope."},{"kind":"para","text":"He had an uplifted spirit by the promises of God towards His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"Other times (as we will see in future psalms) God doesn't alleviate the stress."},{"kind":"para","text":"All-in-all, the way God answers our prayers, it up to the Lord."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"\"Be still.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"David loves to use these words in his Psalms."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be still, and know that I am God: I will be exalted among the heathen, I will be exalted in the earth.","ref":"Psalm 46:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him: fret not thyself because of him who prospereth in his way, because of the man who bringeth wicked devices to pass.","ref":"Psalm 37:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My soul, wait thou only upon God; for my expectation is from him.","ref":"Psalm 62:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Blessed are they that dwell in thy house: they will be still praising thee. Selah.","ref":"Psalm 84:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants us to think about this as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Take a moment.\" David says."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Just stop, think about what God wants. Commence with the Lord even in your bed. Be still and listen.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes that is our biggest issue today."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not still enough."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone is go go go, and not many are stop."},{"kind":"para","text":"People talk more than listen."},{"kind":"para","text":"They work more than rest."},{"kind":"para","text":"They stand more than sit."},{"kind":"para","text":"They do more than think."},{"kind":"para","text":"Lead more than follow."},{"kind":"para","text":"Men of God should be good at being still."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are the ones that need to be worked on the most about being still."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Bible speaks about the necessity of being still and waiting on the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why do we not take that to heart as often as we should?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Why do we ignore this very important command from the Lord?"},{"kind":"para","text":"We would have so much more blessings, so much more time and energy, if we can just learn to stop, be still, think, and wait on the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Stop. Think. Be Still. Musicians pause."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"title":"A Refresh Spirit","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here we go, now it's time for action!"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have stopped, we were still with God, and now we have motivation, we have compassion, we have joy, we have UNCTION to serve and to see God move!"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have a refreshed Spirit and are ready to go."},{"kind":"para","text":"So many of us have dwindled our Spirits down to nubs."},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot pour anything more out."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are stuck in our spirits."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are lacking in what we need."},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason we are lacking spiritually is because we have not been still long enough."},{"kind":"para","text":"We see David switch into gear after God has refreshed him in his stillness."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what we need."},{"kind":"para","text":"We need rejuvenation, and we can only get it if we are willing to stop and let God fill us back up to keep going!"},{"kind":"para","text":"We can be confident that when we are still with God, that God will not lead us astray."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"Being Still Provides","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The world is not good, but God is."},{"kind":"para","text":"We live in a fallen world, but we serve a risen Savior."},{"kind":"para","text":"We dwell on false promises, but we have a God who can never lie."},{"kind":"para","text":"We feel the abandonment of the people around us, but God has promised to never leave us nor forsake us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We won't find much good in this world, but we should pray like David that God would lift His light so we can traverse this dark and lonely world."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is our guiding light."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is our saving beacon."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must simply dwell in His light, and stay safe from the darkness of this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Be consistently in His light, dear Christian."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don't turn away, and don't give up hope."},{"kind":"para","text":"For if we are still, God will illuminate our path."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We've seen God provide throughout scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"He even provides through famines and inflation."},{"kind":"para","text":"God wants to provide for His children."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even more than physical providence (though) is God's providence of the heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has a way of uplifting your spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has a way of changing your countenance."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has a way of putting gladness in your heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"We need that more than we need the corn and wine that people can process."},{"kind":"para","text":"We need a spiritual power that passes anything this world can give us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We wouldn't have a worry in the world, if God took our worries away through a glad heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"So why are so many Christians living with sad hearts today?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe it's because they have not sat still with God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Still can sometimes feel uncomfortable."},{"kind":"para","text":"It can feel as if you must need to do something (maybe with your hands or with your feet)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Being still with God can be tricky sometimes, but it is so needful."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes we are in such a sad state that being still with God is the last thing you want to do, but it's the most needful thing."},{"kind":"para","text":"We all need to be alone, and be still with God."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we do this, we will have a heart full of gladness which gives us more hope and joy than anything else in this life."},{"kind":"para","text":"Many people drink to feel joy."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christians can have better joy through stillness with God."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I am a bit of an insomniac."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have a very difficult time sleeping."},{"kind":"para","text":"One of the burdens and pressures of ministry is my brain is always working, always praying, always thinking."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes in the middle of the night, I will get up to finish typing something I forgot about that particular day, or I will pray for a person that has suddenly come to mind."},{"kind":"para","text":"Most nights I try and just put it into my todo list for the next day, but my brain sometimes won't shut off unless I get it done right then and there."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm sure it isn't healthy."},{"kind":"para","text":"If I took more time to just be still with God, I might find more purpose to laying down in peace and sleeping."},{"kind":"para","text":"Being still with God provides us with safety."},{"kind":"para","text":"It makes us feel better, it brings gladness to our heart, and it gives us comfort and security."},{"kind":"para","text":"Stillness with God is a very important note (no pun intended) that David will continually play on, and it should be one that we think about often as well."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":8}]},
    "5": {"chapter":5,"intro":[],"previously":["David makes a lot of these psalms out to be something like a prayer. They will lead to future thoughts (which could be interpreted as prophecies) but they are current needs to him as well. I believe when he was writing out these psalms, he wasn't just doing it for his own personal sake. I believe he had future generations in mind. When I wrote music, I didn't just write music that was useful to me. I wanted to write music that others could relate to as well. David wants others to relate to him, and see where he finds correction, and refreshment in his own personal life so we can do the same.","In this chapter, it seems that David is pleading with the Lord as a desire to have His presence with him. He wants God to show Himself and get glory, even in the midst of great trials."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"David Pleads For God's Presence","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This will be the standard in which David often comes to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is a plea."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a true desire for God to listen to what he has to say because he is feeling very alone and vulnerable."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm afraid there are many \"Christians\" today who come to the Lord with false pretenses."},{"kind":"para","text":"They come to Him with a need, but not for the betterment of their faith."},{"kind":"para","text":"They want something, but it's not useful to God."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should not be coming to God with a desire to get everything we want, but rather with a desire to get what He wants to give us."},{"kind":"para","text":"David isn't coming to Him in hopes that David can come out as the know-it-all most-powerful child of the King."},{"kind":"para","text":"No, David is hurt."},{"kind":"para","text":"He needs God's presence and attention because there is nowhere else for him to turn."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David is looking for the response of the King."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants, desperately for God to hear him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because it will only be God that can supply for his needs."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no other person, or other being in the entire universe that can do what David knows only God can do."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Some trust in chariots, and some in horses: but we will remember the name of the LORD our God.","ref":"Psalm 20:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"David knows, and understands, that everyone else around him will let him down for what he is pleading with the Lord for."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think the best way to view this verse is in the constant thought that David has for his dire circumstances."},{"kind":"para","text":"He can't stop thinking about it."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is in so much distress that the first thing he does every day is plead with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants God to show Himself in these trials, and David can't move forward without Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you have not felt a need like this in your life, consider yourself blessed."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have no doubt that there will be a time when you do, but if you have you know exactly how David feels right now."},{"kind":"para","text":"You can relate to this need of God's presence and supplication."},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, David couldn't have the promises of the New Testament (because it hadn't been written yet)."},{"kind":"para","text":"He couldn't have the comfort of Jesus' words."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But the Comforter, which is the Holy Ghost, whom the Father will send in my name, he shall teach you all things, and bring all things to your remembrance, whatsoever I have said unto you.","ref":"John 14:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"But he certainly could have the comfort of the Old Testament."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said, My presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest.","ref":"Exodus 33:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, the entire first 5 books of the Old Testament were about God providing rest for His people, and them rejecting it over and over again."},{"kind":"para","text":"David would be able to read this and certainly trace the line back to God's desire to provide for His children in the face of great adversity."},{"kind":"para","text":"The same feelings of comfort can be traced to this age as well as the future one to come (highlighted through Revelation)."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"Evil Won't Prevail","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David understands that God doesn't desire evil to triumph in the lives of His children."},{"kind":"para","text":"David is also confused because it seems as if evil is triumphing all around him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe this is why he is crying out to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe he thought he was disconnected from God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe he felt as if God was trying to prove something to David, but David didn't feel very adequate for the test."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever it was, David was certain that God would not just leave him and allow evil to have the win."}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It will be so in the last days."},{"kind":"para","text":"It certainly was something that David needed in the presence, but I believe David is giving a prophetic message about the end times."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will have the final say so over evil."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will not allow evil to reign no matter how seemingly bleak the days look."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will triumph over evil, and evil will not have a say in the day of His return."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will punish the world for their evil, and the wicked for their iniquity; and I will cause the arrogancy of the proud to cease, and will lay low the haughtiness of the terrible.","ref":"Isaiah 13:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"This should give us a very comforting walk with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"There will be evil people all around us."},{"kind":"para","text":"Evil people trying to trip us up and leave us for dead."},{"kind":"para","text":"People who desire to see us perish and fail."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those people will not have to deal with us."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will not have to deal with the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will have to deal with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the end, they can do nothing against the Lord, and that is something that should help us love them even when they are hurting us."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"title":"Don't Stop Worship","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David pleads with God, and he knows that God will not let evil win, but the promise he is making to God here is a difficult one for him to make seeing as he feels God is not with him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He says, \"I need your presence, and I know that evil won't win, so I am here, Lord, pleading, waiting, wondering, and I will be here worshipping you, knowing that you will provide mercy, because I am not with the evil ones. I am searching for you.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"When we feel God is distant from us, it is wise of us to take a step back and think, \"Have I done something to distance God? Is there something in my life that needs to change?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"If there is nothing in your life that would keep God from being with you, then there is certainly something that God is teaching you in that time."},{"kind":"para","text":"For David, I believe he needed to build upon his worship for the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He might have felt like he was in a good spot spiritually, and his pride was getting the best of him."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has a good way of keep our pride at bay, and that's through allowing us a little distance from time to time to make us think."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I was a child, I was a mamas boy. I didn't want to be away from my mom for any extended period of time. I worried about her well being. I constantly checked up on her to see if she was alright. I couldn't think of any other place I wanted to be than by her side. I hated spending the night at friends house because it meant I would be away from her. She would go on trips with my dad and leave me with other family, and it would make me sick. Those times of separation (though hurt for the present), looking back now, were necessary. Of course, things changed as I got older and I no longer feel this same way, but that feeling of separation is the same I often feel when God's presence isn't with me."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are times in each one of our lives where we will experience separation anxiety from God."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must learn to use those times to get back with Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"To grow closer to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's okay to NEED God."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants you to need Him."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here's the desire of David."},{"kind":"para","text":"He had plenty of enemies, and there was no way for him to succeed in their presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"They were trying to trip him up all the time."},{"kind":"para","text":"He felt overburdened and inadequate."},{"kind":"para","text":"He just simply wanted God's presence, and to give glory to God and the people around him were trying to stop that from happening."},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems when there are people worshipping God, there are always others trying to stop it."},{"kind":"para","text":"While God is at work in the lives of people, Satan is at work in the lives of others."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan will use any means in his own power to make people stop their worship."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows it is something that God enjoys."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows it is something that we will all be doing for the rest of eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"So if he can stop it now, he will try his very best."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, God wants us to worship even in the middle of the trials."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants us to push through with worship anyway."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants us to give praise and honor to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many churches today who give a lot of thought, time, and energy into sermons and Sunday School lessons."},{"kind":"para","text":"They plan for this event and that event, but the most lacking ministry is their worship."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be spending more time in our worship preparation than we should anywhere else."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we can do that, God can use the rest for His glory."},{"kind":"para","text":"More than sermons, more than outreach, more than events and services, more than traditions and religions, may we increase our focus on worship."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we can do that, everything else can fall apart but we will stand strong."},{"kind":"para","text":"The electronics may stop working, but our worship will continue and God's Spirit won't stop working."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people around us may try and stop us from worshipping, but a Christian wholly yielded to God will not be able to stop themselves from giving God glory."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"title":"The Unfaithful's Punishment","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"How can an unbeliever stop your worship?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I've seen many people who have enjoyed their line of work for a long time."},{"kind":"para","text":"These people are Christians, and they got into that business by the will and direction of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Years later, they have a new boss (who is not a Christian) and this new boss tries to implement ungodly things into their ruling and company."},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, Christians can't stand up for those things, they can't even follow suit with them, and so they start to lose their sense of urgency and joy for their line of work."},{"kind":"para","text":"They can no longer worship the Lord like they should because an unbeliever has robbed them of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don't let unbelievers rob you of your worship."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don't allow the ungodly, unfaithful, and ungraceful company keep you from glorifying God in everything you do."},{"kind":"para","text":"What do they know about goodness?"}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is the prayer for every Christian that has been under the authority of an ungodly person."},{"kind":"para","text":"We desire that they would have a taste of their own medicine."},{"kind":"para","text":"They certainly will, but it may not be in this lifetime."},{"kind":"para","text":"They might get what they deserve in the day of judgement."},{"kind":"para","text":"How sad and ruthless we must be if we desire that they would suffer that day without warning. \"Say unto them, As I live, saith the Lord GOD, I have no pleasure in the death of the wicked; but that the wicked turn from his way and live: turn ye, turn ye from your evil ways; for why will ye die, O house of Israel?\" Ezekiel 33:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"It's okay for you to want God to give them what they deserve, but it is not okay for you to throw them aside so that they would."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"When I say unto the wicked, Thou shalt surely die; and thou givest him not warning, nor speakest to warn the wicked from his wicked way, to save his life; the same wicked man shall die in his iniquity; but his blood will I require at thine hand.","ref":"Ezekiel 3:18"}]}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"title":"Finding Joy","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We just want to see a victory."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't even have to be through us that the victory happens."},{"kind":"para","text":"As long as glorify goes back to God in the times of great distress, we will be content."},{"kind":"para","text":"David understands that the purpose of the battle, and the real reason that he is pleading for God's presence isn't because he wants to be the best name in the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"The real reason, rather, is because He wants God's name to be glorified!"},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to rejoice in the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to have joy in what he's been called to do."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is a difficult thing to find joy in joyless company, and there is nothing more needful and nothing more worth fighting for than to have joy in God's presence again."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many people who have left the faith, lost the faith, or rejected the faith altogether because they have no more rejoicing in God."},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth is, they don't have it because they weren't seeking it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They let the enemy win, and now they have a hard time loving God's name, let alone finding joy in it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don't let the enemy keep you from seeking out the joy of the Lord."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The encompassing presence of God is the only thing that is worth staying alive for."},{"kind":"para","text":"Eventually we will be in His presence forever, but to have His presence today is something that gives us great purpose and meaning in this life."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should desire that everyone would seek out this presence so that they can know this joy."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every day is new, may we spend it with a refilled joy from the Lord, and in the mornings seeking worship and praise to Him through the midst of a trial."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12}]},
    "6": {"chapter":6,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last Psalm, we see David pleading for the presence of God during a difficult trial in his life. It seems there were people looking for David to fail, and he wanted God to make intercession for him during this difficulty. He pointed out that evil will not prevail if the Lord has His way, and there is no reason to stop worshipping God because God will do what is right no matter what. He will punish the unfaithful and give joy to the righteous.","In this chapter, we see a man who has come so undone by his sin that he feels as if God is not even in his life anymore. He has lost God's spirit, and God's presence and he is looking to get both back. He feels like a man sinking in the ocean without a safety harness, and needs the Lord to provide something before he drowns."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":7,"title":"Begging For God's Mercy","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord doesn't throw a tantrum."},{"kind":"para","text":"This isn't like a human standard of anger."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we think of a father rebuking a child in anger, we often see it as \"Dad's angry, and so he's getting after me because of it.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes fathers can do some terrible things when they are angry."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our Heavenly Father doesn't work like that."},{"kind":"para","text":"If the Lord is angry with us, it is not because He is just taking His frustrations out on us."},{"kind":"para","text":"If He is angry it is solely because we have done something to hurt Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot physically hurt Him, but we certainly can spiritually hurt Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are a Christian today, you should not be in the business of spiritually inflicting pain upon the Lord to hurt Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't think I've ever met a Christian who WANTS to hurt the Lord, yet I've met plenty of Christians who HAVE hurt the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am one of them."},{"kind":"para","text":"David is, obviously, one of them as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"He had committed some sort of sin and he is begging the Lord to not give him what he deserves."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes we can fall in this category."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have sinned against the Lord, and the only thing we can do is fall to our knees, pleading that the Lord does not give us what we deserve."},{"kind":"para","text":"We deserve God's anger, and chastisement, but we certainly don't want it."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you have never experienced the Lords chastisement then you are either a perfect Christian, or there is something wrong with your walk (willing to bet it's the latter)."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has a way of showing us what He approves and disapproves, and it would be wise of us to listen to His voice in those moments."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here's the truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"We fall into sin, not because we desire it."},{"kind":"para","text":"There should be no Christian alive that DESIRES sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather, we fall into sin because David is right."},{"kind":"para","text":"God says, \"I am that I am.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"He says, \"I am the way the truth and the life...\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Before Abraham, \"was I am.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus is a great deal of amazing things that we can never compare to."},{"kind":"para","text":"So what am I?"},{"kind":"para","text":"David hits the nail on the head and says, \"I am weak.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"He is strong, He is mighty, He is righteous, He is judge, ruler, and just."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am weak."},{"kind":"para","text":"But he pleads with the Lord to not use His judgement and justice on him, but to rather have mercy, and \"heal\" him."},{"kind":"para","text":"David wants to be fixed of his weakness."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to embrace the Lord's presence and observe the Lord's Will."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, he is weak."},{"kind":"para","text":"His flesh overcomes him, and he ends up doing the things he knows he is not suppose to be doing."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the good that I would I do not: but the evil which I would not, that I do. Now if I do that I would not, it is no more I that do it, but sin that dwelleth in me. I find then a law, that, when I would do good, evil is present with me. For I delight in the law of God after the inward man: But I see another law in my members, warring against the law of my mind, and bringing me into captivity to the law of sin which is in my members. O wretched man that I am! who shall deliver me from the body of this death? I thank God through Jesus Christ our Lord. So then with the mind I myself serve the law of God; but with the flesh the law of sin.","ref":"Romans 7:19-25"},{"kind":"para","text":"If you feel like a perfect Christian, then you have no need for God's Word today."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are wasting our time reading this Psalm because it cannot apply to you."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, none of scripture can apply."},{"kind":"para","text":"You cannot put your faith into Christ because He only saves the weak."},{"kind":"para","text":"David needed some healing, and he needed some strength, and the only one that can give him either of those was the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is a strong example for us that we might seek the Lord when we are at our weakest moments."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here's another truth that many people don't seem to grasp."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes we are left in our weakness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes we are left in our sins."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Does God like us to be there?"},{"kind":"para","text":"No."},{"kind":"para","text":"He gives us over to those things we think we desire the most so we see how vain and empty it truly is."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our sins and weaknesses will not give us more power, but rather diminish our strength the longer we stay in them."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must find strength in the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must dive into His Word."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must plead for intercession."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must seek a cure from Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot come to the beginning of His work until we come to the end of ourselves."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is, obviously, not a command from David."},{"kind":"para","text":"David cannot command anything from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I find it interesting that there are people today who pray to specific angels or saints expecting them to listen to their needs and commands."},{"kind":"para","text":"They pray in a sense of authority, as if they have ownership over the angels and saints."},{"kind":"para","text":"They pray as if they can dictate and control the supernatural realm and bend it to their own personal wills and desires."},{"kind":"para","text":"Angels and saints don't listen to anyone but God."},{"kind":"para","text":"The scripture proves that over and over again."},{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn't bend to anyone's control."},{"kind":"para","text":"He does what He knows is right."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will leave you where you are until you have come to the end of yourself."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants you to empty yourself so you will cling closer to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can plead with the Lord, like David is here, but we must also understand that God will do what is right. Period."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is kind of a funny verse to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"David says, \"You don't want to give me what I deserve. If I get what I deserve Lord, who will praise you and give you thanks? You won't have me around to bring you glory.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth of the matter is, David seemed like the only one that was seeking to bringing glory to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"When Jesus comes and His ministry is revealed, it seems at that time HE was the only one bringing glory to God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Better than David though, was the fact that Jesus rose from the dead to give God praise."},{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn't need your praise."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has plenty of it in Heaven."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Praise him, ye heavens of heavens, and ye waters that be above the heavens.","ref":"Psalm 148:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"No, He WANTS our praise."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants us to desire to praise Him, and He is joyous when we have a heart full of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"If the Lord desired, He can have the graves sing praises to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He can have the rocks cry out for Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he answered and said unto them, I tell you that, if these should hold their peace, the stones would immediately cry out.","ref":"Luke 19:40"}]},{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It is not common that a man admits his crying."},{"kind":"para","text":"Being vulnerable is difficult for most men."},{"kind":"para","text":"David is extremely emotional before the Lord, and he knows and is assured that God already has seen it."},{"kind":"para","text":"He understands that God can take away his grief."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet God hasn't, and David doesn't understand why."},{"kind":"para","text":"He feels like he is swimming in his own tears."},{"kind":"para","text":"He feels like there is no life jacket to keep him afloat."},{"kind":"para","text":"He feels as if his whole body is being drained because of how terrible his situation is."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is interesting that this psalm is the antithesis of our previous Psalm."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our last psalm spoke much about God getting after His enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"This psalm faces the opposite dilemma and asks for God's mercies."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is showing both sides of the field here."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many who deserve God's judgement and anger because of their life choices."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have lived for worldly pleasure."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then there are those who are Christians and have been enticed into bad living who only realize how far away from God they have become once God gives them over to it."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be cautious about spending too much time in this world, and not enough time with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are more enamoured by the world around us, we will never be fit and prepared for the world above us."},{"kind":"para","text":"And we will ultimately be stuck like this psalmist, crying tears of pain and shame for we are in a position away from the Lord beginning for His presence and forgiveness."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":10,"title":"A Renewed Vision","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Psalmist is encouraging himself in God's promises."},{"kind":"para","text":"He, maybe, is remembering some of the things that God has made promises of and has kept His promises too."},{"kind":"para","text":"He may have remembered that God has not left him before, and God is FULL of mercy and compassion."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The LORD is gracious, and full of compassion; slow to anger, and of great mercy. The LORD is good to all: and his tender mercies are over all his works.","ref":"Psalm 145:8-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is the theme of all scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is the character of Jesus wrapped up into a song of praise."},{"kind":"para","text":"The days look bleak, and the people are terribly evil, yet we know that God can turn it all around, and when He does, He will provide mercy instead of wrath."},{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a day when God prods to turn it around, however, and no one will listen."},{"kind":"para","text":"That will be the day that God provides wrath instead of mercy..."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Psalmist is assured that God will answer him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is quite positive that God won't just leave his prayer unanswered."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is up to the Lord on how He will answer our prayers."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will not always give us what we want, but He will certainly do what is best."},{"kind":"para","text":"I imagine that the Psalmist pictures his enemies surrounding him, but because of his prayer he see's his enemies stop, become confused about their actions, and then are undone by themselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"They stand next to the Psalmist and say, \"What am I doing? I am so miserable. Why am I going after this man?\" and they just walk away dumbfounded and ashamed."},{"kind":"para","text":"How I wish all our enemies were such."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":10}]},
    "7": {"chapter":7,"intro":[],"previously":["The Psalmists have spent a good deal of time through the Psalms begging for mercy from the Lord. They want God's provision and guidance for specific issues. They feel as if the trial or the circumstances are quite bleak, and it is wise in those moments to drop to our needs and seek provision from the Lord.","In this Psalm, it is no different. We see David plead with the Lord to reveal the truth in his life against his enemies. If what his enemies say is true, then they should have his life. If it is not, then the Lord should have THEIR lives."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Cush The Benjamite","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I have seen people put their trust into small and insignificant things."},{"kind":"para","text":"Quite recently, our current president told the people that he would forgive student debt up to $20,000 per person. Our Supreme Court shot down the gesture when the bill passed by their table and told the people, \"the president did not have the authority to cancel up to $20,000 per borrower,\" and ended the effort that was made by our president. There are a lot of people who were likely depending on this relief and probably sitting pretty comfortably in their debt anticipating that Joe Biden would keep his promise... ...Now that he couldn't, they will feel a sense of dread and suffering because they put their trust into the wrong thing."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we put our trust in the Lord, we can depend on the Lord saving us from everyone that tries to persecute you."},{"kind":"para","text":"You will be delivered from your debt in sin."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David has seen his share of enemies, and has been in some serious battles against them all."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we read through the different accounts of David's battles and victories, we think God has certainly given this man so much power that he has no issues taking on such great feats of battle."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, here, in the Psalms, we see the real mind of David."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not sure who this \"Cush\" character is, but we are given some interesting facts about him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is a Benjamite, just like David."},{"kind":"para","text":"He had, in some way, made an enemy of David."},{"kind":"para","text":"And David doesn't want to be enemies with Cush."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is assumed by some scholars that Cush was a soldier of Saul."},{"kind":"para","text":"If this is the case, Cush and David may have been friends at one point, but now Cush is accusing David of trying to take the throne away from the king."},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course that is not what David is doing, but the people who were around Saul were getting the same spirit as Saul (which was an evil spirit to be sure)."},{"kind":"para","text":"David needed the Lords guidance in this matter because he felt like he was being wrongly accused of some things that Saul was accusing him of."},{"kind":"para","text":"David was a strong man, only after he had knelt to the ground before the Lord seeking him fervently for leadership."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":5,"title":"Have I Done Wrong?","entries":[{"start":3,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There's nothing worse than when a friend betrays you."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think, out of all that Christ experienced (and I am certainly not downplaying His suffering on the cross), the greatest pain He faced was the rejection of Judas."},{"kind":"para","text":"Judas didn't just betray Jesus, he altogether rejected Jesus, even after betraying him."},{"kind":"para","text":"David is facing a similar circumstance from a friend, except David isn't purpose."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus didn't have to think to Himself, \"Is there iniquity in my hands?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"He didn't have to say, \"Have I actually done something wrong?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"David knew there was nothing that he did which was wrong, yet he feels like he has to make sure?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because his greatest enemies at the moment were people that he admired and loved dearly."},{"kind":"para","text":"What a tragedy to be involved with a church whose leader does not live up to what he preaches."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've seen churches where there is great strong leaders in them, slowly crumble away because the leader is far busier trying to attack itself rather than taking the fight into the world and preaching the gospel."},{"kind":"para","text":"They preach MORE to their congregation about sin and salvation than they do to the lost."},{"kind":"para","text":"I certainly believe the gospel message should be preached in every sermon, but there should not be people suffering from spiritual food because of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"A Spiritual meal has sustenance."},{"kind":"para","text":"It has applicability."},{"kind":"para","text":"It has something that everyone can take home and use to grow closer to their Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"If It's a message about how useless we are, and how much we don't deserve Christ, we will not leave the church house full."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will leave it empty."},{"kind":"para","text":"Empty of spiritual food."},{"kind":"para","text":"And empty of the spirit of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"David was feeling quite empty at the moment."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have no doubt Saul had told him over and over again how useless he was to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"At the beginning of his relationship with Saul, it might have seemed that Saul loved him."},{"kind":"para","text":"David thought of Saul as the leader that God positioned on purpose!"},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet Saul was a terrible leader."},{"kind":"para","text":"David was seriously let down once the person he looked up to was trying to kill him, and even more let down when the friends he worked with took Saul's side on the matter."},{"kind":"para","text":"May we be cautious about taking sides."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be more like Jonathan than we should be a Cush."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we are like Jonathan, we seek out the matter and prove what is right and wrong."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Prove all things; hold fast that which is good. Abstain from all appearance of evil. And the very God of peace sanctify you wholly; and I pray God your whole spirit and soul and body be preserved blameless unto the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ... ...Faithful is he that calleth you, who also will do it. Brethren, pray for us.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 5:21-25"},{"kind":"para","text":"David was feeling as if he might have actually done wrong, and if he has, then the Lord should allow his enemy to take his life."},{"kind":"para","text":"We end this section on a \"Selah.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We must learn to pause at the \"Selah's\" so that we can transition to a new way of thinking on the topic."},{"kind":"para","text":"Stop, think, and then continue."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is the only way we will have clarity in our dire prayers."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":7,"title":"Return in Judgement","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a whole world of thought going on here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Firstly, this has transitioned quite a lot from how David was feeling just a moment ago."},{"kind":"para","text":"He thought he might have been in the wrong."},{"kind":"para","text":"After he waited on the Lord in his \"Selah\" break, he now has a new thought on the matter."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants God to take his enemies down with \"anger.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants God to cast judgement on them. \"For we must all appear before the judgment seat of Christ; that every one may receive the things done in his body, according to that he hath done, whether it be good or bad.\" 2 Corinthians 5:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the time is come that judgment must begin at the house of God: and if it first begin at us, what shall the end be of them that obey not the gospel of God?","ref":"1 Peter 4:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And as it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment:","ref":"Hebrews 9:27"},{"kind":"para","text":"The judgement of God is saved for the day of His wrath."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the wrath of God is revealed from heaven against all ungodliness and unrighteousness of men, who hold the truth in unrighteousness;","ref":"Romans 1:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"David was asking for an early judgement against his enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is known, hopefully at this point, that the Psalms give a picture of prophesying while at the same time speaking of current (or current for back then anyway) events."},{"kind":"para","text":"I do believe this is a prophecy of the end times."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be so that the world will have made an enemy with the Lord and His people, and God's anger and judgement will come and destroy all of the enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"And this is how we will be..."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"\"...return thou on high.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We will be surrounding the Lord when He returns."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that know Him and have trusted in Him will find no other safety from His wrath than to be by His side."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't think our brains can comprehend the scene that will take place."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might have a picture of the idea of Christ returning in judgement, but we will never fully understand it until we see it with our own eyes."},{"kind":"para","text":"David wants justice for the way he has been treated lately, and he knows he can't just do it himself."},{"kind":"para","text":"He needs GOD to take care of the issue."},{"kind":"para","text":"Or at the very least, to help David know what to do about it and where to go."},{"kind":"para","text":"Where do you go when the man of God is chasing you for your life?"},{"kind":"para","text":"How do you react when God's chosen hates you without a cause?"},{"kind":"para","text":"If you've never been in this place like David (maybe without the threats of murdering you but still the same complication) then consider yourself blessed."},{"kind":"para","text":"I pray you never experience this."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is a hurt that never goes away, and it was Gods way of making this man David..."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"title":"Judge the Heart","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It takes a lot of unction to ask the Lord to \"judge me.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't want God to judge us, because if He does, He will certainly find something wrong with us."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is, however, only through that mode of prayer that God can use us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must learn to ask the Lord, \"What is standing between me and you today? Forgive me of it, and help me to change.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"God will ALWAYS bring something to mind, and when He does, we cannot just ask for forgiveness and move on."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must allow His process of change to take place."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be uncomfortable, and sometimes painful, but it will always be worth it."},{"kind":"para","text":"A weight will be lifted."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you cannot find anything wrong with you, then you must be a perfect Christian."},{"kind":"para","text":"Congratulations."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, as long as there is a hell, there will be sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked will always have a place in this world until the return of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"David asks for establishment though."},{"kind":"para","text":"A granting of security and stability for the \"just.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The just are the \"justified.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Just\" means \"lawful,\" or \"right.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"There are people who just want to be established from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't like the wickedness of the Earth, and they certainly don't like their own wickedness."},{"kind":"para","text":"We need the Lord to establish us while there is wickedness around."},{"kind":"para","text":"God tries the hearts of man."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is, arguably, by the heart that God can tell who a man is."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of pastors and preachers alike who have great messages but bad hearts."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are full of passion, but lack compassion."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are full of words, but lack love."},{"kind":"para","text":"Full of fire, but lack grace."},{"kind":"para","text":"Full of themselves, and lacking the spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"They mean well, but it's not the spirit that God is trying, it's the heart. \"Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see God.\" Matthew 5:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"David will speak more about the heart later on, but it is important to realize and understand that God see's your heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't matter how well you clean up on the outside."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't matter what kind of spirit you think you have (Saul thought his spirit was fine)."},{"kind":"para","text":"What matters is what's in your heart."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":13,"title":"There's Time For Repentance","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We can take the words of everyone around us to heart, and think they know what they are talking about when they accuse us of all sorts of lies and hypocrisy."},{"kind":"para","text":"OR, we can take God's Words to heart, and believe what He says about us, being transformed into His image."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God.","ref":"Romans 12:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"The heart and the brain are connected."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have a pair of nerves on the sides of our neck called \"the Vagus Nerves.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"These nerves connect the brain to the heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our brain actually can tell the heart how fast or slow to beat depending on what we are actually doing."},{"kind":"para","text":"For instance, our heart shouldn't be beating fast when we are just sitting down and relaxed."},{"kind":"para","text":"It should be beating fast if we are exercising."},{"kind":"para","text":"If it's beating fast while you are sitting down you either have an issue that needs to be looked at, or you are nervous about something."},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, we are affected, one in the same, by our mind and our hearts."},{"kind":"para","text":"God looks at the heart, but it is our mind that can tell the heart what to do."},{"kind":"para","text":"So if we are to have clean hearts, we must have pure minds."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is, quite possibly, one of the most frustrating and hurtful verses in scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"David reminds his readers, here, that God is constantly angry with the wicked."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has been storing His wrath against people who are evil and terrible in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a great reminder to us that God will give them what they deserve, but it's also frustrating because God is constantly seeing it."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is hurt by the wickedness of this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"They try and play it off as if God won't do anything, and they have one over on the Christian."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Be not deceived; God is not mocked...\" Galatians 6:7a"}]},{"start":12,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The thing that we seem to forget is, the reason that God has not released His wrath is because these people still have a chance to turn."},{"kind":"para","text":"David didn't want to be against Saul or Cush."},{"kind":"para","text":"David wanted them to follow the Lord and turn from their wickedness."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wanted them to be saved from the Lord, and even more so, to be friends with David rather than enemies against him."},{"kind":"para","text":"When you read the situation between Saul and David, David has no idea why Saul is angry with him."},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems to come out of nowhere."},{"kind":"para","text":"As the readers, we kind of get a behind the scenes look and realize that Saul was just jealous of David."},{"kind":"para","text":"Saul liked the spotlight."},{"kind":"para","text":"Saul liked power."},{"kind":"para","text":"When people started paying attention to David, and David started getting glory for his victories, Saul hated David for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Saul wanted the publics attention and he wasn't getting it nearly as much as David was."},{"kind":"para","text":"The thing is, is David didn't ask for the attention."},{"kind":"para","text":"David didn't even ask to be king."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wasn't trying to take Saul's kingdom away from Saul."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wasn't trying to hurt Saul in any way, yet Saul didn't see it like this and tries to kill David."},{"kind":"para","text":"David understands that every battle (this is proven with Goliath the giant) belongs to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has His own weapons ready."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will not be literal swords or arrows, but these are great illustrations of how God will take care of those that reject Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is a time that is given to every man on Earth to turn to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"If they do not, they will eventually run out of time."}]}]},{"start":14,"end":16,"title":"Digging Your Own Grave","entries":[{"start":14,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"\"pate\" means \"crown of the head.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"When someone is trying to destroy, trap, or otherwise mistreat the righteous (or the Godly) all they do is set up traps for themselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"They might take a righteous person down, but they will be in the pit with them."},{"kind":"para","text":"What David is saying here is equivalent too, \"The wicked dig their own grave.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"That verse of Galatians was only partially read."},{"kind":"para","text":"The full verse states:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be not deceived; God is not mocked: for whatsoever a man soweth, that shall he also reap.","ref":"Galatians 6:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"This can be a friendly verse to the righteous."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are sowing seeds of good news."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are sowing seeds of hope and joy and eternal reward."},{"kind":"para","text":"But this can also be an unkind verse to the wicked."},{"kind":"para","text":"They sow seeds of hate, and hurt."},{"kind":"para","text":"Seeds of torture, torment."},{"kind":"para","text":"Seeds of despair and bitterness."},{"kind":"para","text":"What we sow, we will also reap."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we sow seeds of joy, we will reap that harvest."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we sow seeds of bitterness, we will reap that harvest."},{"kind":"para","text":"Be very cautious about what you sow, because you may not be digging a plot for planting seeds."},{"kind":"para","text":"You may be digging your own grave."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"title":"Sing to the Lord","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Even through all of the pain, and all of the heartache, David says, \"I will sing to the Lord.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"David has a reason to sing still."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should have a reason to sing still as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have had my share of legalistic preachers and pastors tell me what was good and pleasant to sing to the Lord and what was not."},{"kind":"para","text":"They do not determine my mode of worship."},{"kind":"para","text":"I know what brings praises to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is not the song, as much as it is the heart that God loves to hear."},{"kind":"para","text":"The lyrics, of course, should be worthy to bring God praise, but the heart should be pure to sing it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Worship can be corporate, but it is always personal."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17}]},
    "8": {"chapter":8,"intro":[],"previously":["The Psalmists have given ideas about how to pray to the Lord through difficult seasons. One of the things I like about Psalms is it gives us historical accounts, alongside of future promises, as well as applicable thoughts that we can use today. Our last chapter saw some dread and turmoil in the life of David and how He came to just trust that the Lord knew what He was doing. This won't be the last time that David finds himself in this position either.","In this chapter we see the Psalmist give absolute glory to God, pointing out his creation, and what God cares about the most out of all creation."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Glorify God Always","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here's a lesson we must learn when we are going through a difficult season."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is good, all the time."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is not a time when God isn't good."},{"kind":"para","text":"You have sin in your life?"},{"kind":"para","text":"God is good."},{"kind":"para","text":"You are going through a trial?"},{"kind":"para","text":"God is good."},{"kind":"para","text":"You are worried and anxious about the next steps in life?"},{"kind":"para","text":"God is good."},{"kind":"para","text":"You are on the highest mountains and reaping the greatest rewards?"},{"kind":"para","text":"God is good."},{"kind":"para","text":"There should never be a time where we can't sit and say, \"How excellent is thy name in all the earth!\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a lesson straight from Christ Himself."},{"kind":"para","text":"When He woke up for another day of ministry, He praises God."},{"kind":"para","text":"When He went to bed to get a few hours of sleep before having to heal more of the sick and seek more of the lost, He praises God."},{"kind":"para","text":"When He had to suffer and die on the cross for the sins of the entire world, He praises God."},{"kind":"para","text":"When He rises again from the dead, He praises God."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We are nothing more than children to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can be the most mature Christian adult this world has ever seen, but we will never be anything to the Lord but His dear children. The most popular song that my daughter would sing in our household often was \"Jesus loves me.\" At the age of 3 she knew how to do the whole song in sign language. The song specifically says, \"They (the children) are weak, but He (Christ) is strong.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It might seem like a foolish thing to many \"mature\" Christians to be children to the Lord, but it is the only way the Lord wants to use us."},{"kind":"para","text":"Today, my daughter is a mini teenager."},{"kind":"para","text":"She acts like a teenager and she's only 9 (as of this writing)."},{"kind":"para","text":"She no longer wants to spend time with her mom and dad, she over-dramatizes everything, and she is asking awkward questions about awkward things that I have no idea how she learns about."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are more like the stubborn teenager than we are like the faithfilled children."},{"kind":"para","text":"God does not want us to get over Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even small songs like \"Jesus Loves Me\" is a warming song to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think it would be wise to have a child-like faith in all things we do with God, otherwise we might not see what kind of blessings He can bestow on such weak, sinful vessels as us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And said, Verily I say unto you, Except ye be converted, and become as little children, ye shall not enter into the kingdom of heaven.","ref":"Matthew 18:3"}]}]},{"start":3,"end":5,"title":"Behold His Creation","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Have you ever looked at the moon."},{"kind":"para","text":"I put into my calendar to go see the full moon every time it's up."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moon is one of the most fascinating things to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are to be like little moons."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moon reflects the sun."},{"kind":"para","text":"It does not give off it's own life."},{"kind":"para","text":"We, too, are to reflect the Son, we are not to give off our own light."},{"kind":"para","text":"When Spurgeon was leaving after living with his grandfather for some time, he recounts..."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Grandfather tried to comfort me by saying, 'Ah, Child! You are going away from Stambourne; but the same moon will shine where you are going! It will always be the same moon.' Often I looked at the moon and remembered that Grandfather was looking at it, too, and we were not so very far away from one another.\" Charles Spurgeon"},{"kind":"para","text":"The moon is quite fascinating, and the stars are innumerable."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I was younger, we use to go camping quite a bit. I did not know the maker of the stars, but I knew there were too many to count... ...My mom and I would sit by the campfire, and she would entice me to count the stars. I would start, but I could never finish. Still today, I couldn't finish counting. Why? Because there are too many? No, because I would get too lost."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moon and stars are quite a work of art from the Lord, and it is something amazing to behold."},{"kind":"para","text":"To the world, it seems like a small thing that the galaxy is so vast and infinite, yet to the Christian, we are inspired."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because David mentions it in the next verse..."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has an amazing creation that we get to see all the time."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are partakers of His creation, and yet He still wants to know us."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to pay attention to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"The great mystery that Paul speaks about in Ephesians is surely this."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has made amazing, unfathomable things, and yet He still wants to be present with mankind."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't know of a thing that God loves greater than His creation of man."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has given US His own traits and attributes, not the animals."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has given US dominion of the Earth, not the plants."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has allowed US life and breath, not the dirt."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has come to US to die on the cross, not any other planet or life form."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why is it that God loves us so much above every other creation?"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the real mystery."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has made man a little lower than the angels."},{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine how much freeflow the angels are able to achieve."},{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine the things they have seen."},{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine what creations they have gotten to know far before mankind was even made."},{"kind":"para","text":"Angels have been a part of God's creation far before we were, and God has made man \"a little lower than the angels.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We do not contain the power of the angels."},{"kind":"para","text":"We do not hold the same abilities as they."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet it was for us that God has sent His Son to redeem."},{"kind":"para","text":"The angels cannot recieve that salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"They can only have knowledge of it, but they cannot take it for themselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are lower than the angels, and yet God loves us with an immeasurable amount of love."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ, too, was made \"lower than the angels.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It is Christ who is ultimately crowned with glory."},{"kind":"para","text":"He lived a life that no man can live, yet was 100% man in everything He did."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was able to accomplish more than the angels because He is 100% God."},{"kind":"para","text":"That Jesus would be willing to be lower than the angels in God's creation is a miracle to humanity."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is the greatest blessing that God has ever given the world."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"Who Has Dominion?","entries":[{"start":6,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In Genesis, God gave man dominion over His creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"We were tasked with stewarding the creation that God had made."},{"kind":"para","text":"He made the Earth for us."},{"kind":"para","text":"He made it so we can inherit it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan came to try and keep us from doing this, and trying to overthrow the throne of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"God, of course (in His great sovereignty) knew this would happen, and even allowed it, giving Satan a victory."},{"kind":"para","text":"This small victory of Satan has kept him going."},{"kind":"para","text":"He thinks he has one over on God, and that he currently unstoppable."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows the Bible well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan knows revelation."},{"kind":"para","text":"He also knows God is merciful, and kind, and loving."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is trying to beat the Lord by playing the long game, and enticing the smallest of us here on Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"He cannot have an angel army, but he can certainly have an earthly one."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't know what Satan did to entice a third of the angels to follow him to Earth, but I do know that they will never receive what he has promised."},{"kind":"para","text":"The same goes for those that reject Christ today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan is promising them freedom but giving them torment."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has given us freedom AND dominion over the Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, we can secure that dominion by accepting the one with ultimate dominion which is Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan cannot promise you earthly things, because it is God who still owns the Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has not given Satan dominion to rule the world, He gave that to man."},{"kind":"para","text":"And it is Christ who has redeemed man, so therefore it is now HIS to rule and reign over."},{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a day when He will do so, and that day will come quicker than anyone is anticipating."},{"kind":"para","text":"But until that day comes, we are given the ability to live on God's Earth, not Satan's!"},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan will be given power for a short time, but it will not suffice for God's children to follow his power, when we have The Lord's power granted to us."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"title":"An Amazing Gift To Ponder","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a time when every knee will bow at the name of Jesus."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth; And that every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.","ref":"Philippians 2:10-11"},{"kind":"para","text":"That time has not come yet, but that time will come eventually and His name will be excellent in all the earth!"},{"kind":"para","text":"No one will be able to deny that."},{"kind":"para","text":"We still have the honor and privilege to praise the name of the Lord even when the whole world is against it."},{"kind":"para","text":"May we use our breath to praise His name."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is wise of us to take time away from the wickedness of the world, and sit and look at God's creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Get away, by yourself, and search the stars."},{"kind":"para","text":"Stare at the moon."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at the trees, and flowers, and blooms."},{"kind":"para","text":"See what God has done, and praise His name for saving YOU."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is not the moon and stars, and trees, and flowers, and animals, and ocean, and ground, and sky that He is saving."},{"kind":"para","text":"Revelation says all of those things will be destroyed."},{"kind":"para","text":"No, it is MAN that He is saving."},{"kind":"para","text":"What an amazing gift to ponder."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9}]},
    "9": {"chapter":9,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last chapter, we see the Psalmist point out the amazing creations of the Lord and why they display His splendor and goodness, as well as His presence with us.","In this chapter we see God's provision for His people, as well as His concerns in the accounts of evil and perverse men. We see His desire to turn people toward Him, and take care of those that know Him already. The Psalmist gives us ample reason to praise God, even during the times of God's wrath being poured out."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Praise the Lord","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"The heart is deceitful above all things, and desperately wicked: who can know it?","ref":"Jeremiah 17:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"Is David wrong to praise the Lord with his whole heart?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Why should we trust our heart?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Jesus answered him, The first of all the commandments is, Hear, O Israel; The Lord our God is one Lord: And thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind, and with all thy strength: this is the first commandment. And the second is like, namely this, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself. There is none other commandment greater than these.","ref":"Mark 12:29-31"},{"kind":"para","text":"Brushing up on Catholic assumption, they have given a list of seven \"deadly\" sins, which are no more deadly than what the Ten Commandments reference."},{"kind":"para","text":"Their list consists of \"Pride, greed, wrath, envy, lust, gluttony, and sloth.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"I have thoughts on all seven of these specifically from scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"Pride:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But let every man prove his own work, and then shall he have rejoicing in himself alone, and not in another. For every man shall bear his own burden.","ref":"Galatians 6:4-5"},{"kind":"para","text":"Greed:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the love of money is the root of all evil: which while some coveted after, they have erred from the faith, and pierced themselves through with many sorrows.","ref":"1 Timothy 6:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Wrath:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be ye angry, and sin not: let not the sun go down upon your wrath:","ref":"Ephesians 4:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"Gluttony:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For even when we were with you, this we commanded you, that if any would not work, neither should he eat.","ref":"2 Thessalonians 3:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Jesus said unto them, I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall never hunger; and he that believeth on me shall never thirst.","ref":"John 6:35"},{"kind":"para","text":"Sloth:"},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't think I have to talk about the fact that Jesus walked everywhere He went, and we are told several times to \"walk with Christ\" not to \"run with Christ.\""},{"kind":"scripture","text":"As ye have therefore received Christ Jesus the Lord, so walk ye in him:","ref":"Colossians 2:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"The only two that have any bounds for actual concern is lust and envy."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be envious, however, of those that do what is good and right."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is room for that in our culture today."},{"kind":"para","text":"People are envious for evil things, but we (as Christians) should be envious of Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"Lust cannot be argued over."},{"kind":"para","text":"Lust is hurtful to the Lord, and to others."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's suffice to say, there are good ways, and bad ways to use your emotions and thoughts."},{"kind":"para","text":"Your flesh will want to use every type of emotion (including in your worship which we will read in a moment) to please itself."},{"kind":"para","text":"As a Christian, we should be listening to the Spirits leading on our emotions."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can use our hearts to praise the Lord!"},{"kind":"para","text":"We can use our words to do the same..."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Sing what to thy name?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Praise!"},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't have to have a set song, or a specific book to praise the Lord from."},{"kind":"para","text":"David didn't have the psalms to praise the Lord from, he was literally WRITING them."},{"kind":"para","text":"He just sang praises to him."},{"kind":"para","text":"We've had a discussion already about the importance of praise, and how it should not be dictated by church culture or religious ideology, but rather from the heart which is where David is coming from here."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"title":"Maintaining Your Cause","entries":[{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't matter what people may say or think about you as a Christian."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the end, as we've noticed throughout scripture, God has the final say."},{"kind":"para","text":"That should bring us great comfort when conflict comes into our life."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even better when you see the Lord \"maintain\" your \"right and your cause.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"When you are doing something for the Lord, and everyone around you is against you, or discouraging you, this doesn't mean you should just give up and go home."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather, it means that you should do what God wants you to, even if the whole world hated it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every time we do this, we see God get glory, and we know we are in the right because he \"maintains\" our \"right and cause\" for the mission He has given to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"I could tell you story after story about times when God has proven His vision to me, even though everyone else around me hated it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They saw what came of it, and they were sad because they weren't a part of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don't be the person rejecting everything that God is doing in someone elses life."},{"kind":"para","text":"Be the person curious enough to see what God is doing, and loving enough to help them bring glory to Christ!"}]}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"title":"No Rest For The Wicked","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When you are one against the Lord, you don't belittle the Christian or Christ, you belittle yourself."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think of Stephen, a man that was called out by the Apostles to help them reach others in the church who were being neglected."},{"kind":"para","text":"His ministry was short lived, but he was man that loved the Lord, and it was proven through his countenance and demeanor."},{"kind":"para","text":"There were hundreds of men in that time who were putting Stephen on trial (in the book of Acts)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Once Stephen proved the scriptures, the men that were listening hated it, plugged their ears with their fingers, and started screaming and biting Stephen, before throwing stones at him and killing him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"When they heard these things, they were cut to the heart, and they gnashed on him with their teeth. But he, being full of the Holy Ghost, looked up stedfastly into heaven, and saw the glory of God, and Jesus standing on the right hand of God, And said, Behold, I see the heavens opened, and the Son of man standing on the right hand of God. Then they cried out with a loud voice, and stopped their ears, and ran upon him with one accord, And cast him out of the city, and stoned him: and the witnesses laid down their clothes at a young man's feet, whose name was Saul. And they stoned Stephen, calling upon God, and saying, Lord Jesus, receive my spirit. And he kneeled down, and cried with a loud voice, Lord, lay not this sin to their charge. And when he had said this, he fell asleep.","ref":"Acts 7:54-60"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is quite the gruesome scene."},{"kind":"para","text":"Do you know the names of those that were trying to kill him?"},{"kind":"para","text":"There was only one other name mentioned here and this was \"Saul\" who later becomes known as the Apostle \"Paul.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The stoners names are not mentioned."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because God decreased their name."},{"kind":"para","text":"He \"put out their name for ever and ever.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Those people will not go down in history as the ones who triumphantly killed an innocent man."},{"kind":"para","text":"No, the innocent man (Stephen)'s name will go down in history as the one who was loving and caring to a hateful culture that eventually killed him."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has taken down whole cities multiple times through scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe this is why they are not as prominent or even existent today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Egypt still exists, but in turmoil."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rome still exists, but it's not the thriving mecha it once was."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even London has fallen."},{"kind":"para","text":"America seems to be on it's way out the door as well, and the Holy Spirit is landing in areas that are interesting."},{"kind":"para","text":"Supposedly, (according to a few studied I have found online) Christianity has been growing rapidly in Africa and Asia."},{"kind":"para","text":"America, if it continues to go unchecked in their faith, will be a destroyed city whose memory will rot with their destruction."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe that is how the Lord will come."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be in a time when there is no place for the Spirit to rest anymore on this Earth."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"title":"God Endures For Ever","entries":[{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This world may fall apart."},{"kind":"para","text":"America may not stand forever."},{"kind":"para","text":"There will be other nations that prosper and become bigger with the help of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"But one thing is for sure... God endures forever."},{"kind":"para","text":"What a huge encouragement and blessing to know that God endures and keeps tabs on what is happening here in the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is concerned about His people here."},{"kind":"para","text":"WE, are the center of God's universe."},{"kind":"para","text":"As far as I know, there is no other life in all of the galaxy or eternity that God has died for."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are the ones He loves enough to come and die a death He did not deserve just so we can have a life WE don't deserve."},{"kind":"para","text":"I want to notice something though, that might not stick out to most people (and it might only stick out to me because I just like to complicate things)."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"For\" and \"ever\" are separated in this verse."},{"kind":"para","text":"In our ordinary American English language, we usually put those words together."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Forever\" rolls easier."},{"kind":"para","text":"It looks cleaner and it's one less push of the space bar that we have to use."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet there's something about separating those words that make it more impactful."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we said, \"the Lord endures forever.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It sounds like God's endurance doesn't end, which is true."},{"kind":"para","text":"But if we said, \"The Lord endures for ever.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It sounds as if God has endurance specifically FOR eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"His endurances was made FOR the ever."},{"kind":"para","text":"Can you tell the difference here, or am I confusing the terminology?"},{"kind":"para","text":"God's endurance is forever, but it's also FOR ever."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"title":"A Refuge in His Name","entries":[{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Just because God is good, does not mean that man is too."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, it's because God is good, that man is provenly not."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's standards of good, and example of good, has no human example following it (save Jesus Christ)."},{"kind":"para","text":"There has been no man that has ever led a perfect example life of true goodness."},{"kind":"para","text":"No man has led a life where he hasn't stolen something."},{"kind":"para","text":"Or where he hasn't used God's name in vain."},{"kind":"para","text":"Or where he hasn't lied about something."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every single man throughout history (again, save for Christ) has lived up to a very poor standard of good."},{"kind":"para","text":"Because of this, those that try and live a life for God (that is, try and follow God's standard) will be met with ridicule and disruption."},{"kind":"para","text":"But we have a refuge."},{"kind":"para","text":"Where?"},{"kind":"para","text":"In the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"How do we find refuge in Him?"},{"kind":"para","text":"He's not a building after all, and it's not like we can enter eternity to get safety, we are strapped to Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our refuge is through prayer and study."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we are in distress, turn and go to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is your best place of refuge."},{"kind":"para","text":"Only those that know His name will be able to put their trust in Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"What is His name?"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the greatest question a person can ask."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He saith unto them, But whom say ye that I am?","ref":"Matthew 16:15"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth; And that every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.","ref":"Philippians 2:10-11"}]}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"title":"Sing Praises During Destruction","entries":[{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Even in God's wrath, God's people are protected."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look to Sodom and Gomorrah for reference."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look to Noah and his family for reference."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look to Jonah and the whale for reference."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look to Elijah and the famine for reference."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look to John and revelation for reference."},{"kind":"para","text":"While God takes care of the evil, we have a means to sing praises to him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why would we sing while God destroys people and cities?"},{"kind":"para","text":"It's because those people and cities were your enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many cities and people in scripture who were literally trying (and some even succeeding) to kill the Israelites."},{"kind":"para","text":"David and his people were constantly under attack, and the Lord had to provide protection."},{"kind":"para","text":"David was not taking the credit for what God had done, even if it was David that was being used for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"God obviously gave them victory in ways and means in which were impossible to the human eye."},{"kind":"para","text":"All they could do is sing to the Lord for the victory that He was giving them."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"title":"God Have Mercy","entries":[{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God's mercy should be very important to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"For God to pay attention to our trouble is a real blessing."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have seemingly made quite a few enemies because of my faith in the years recently, and it's not because I desire enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, I love even mine enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"I want them to know the Lord as deeply as I do as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Desiring God's mercy, and knowing God is paying attention to the injustices of those around me is something that brings me comfort."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"It is of the LORD's mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not.","ref":"Lamentations 3:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"I deserve to be consumed, in all honesty."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, God has not consumed me."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are fighting against me because of my faith I could argue deserve to be consumed more."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet they are not."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some of them are being consumed in spirit, and you can certainly see that. One particular instance was with a good friend of mine. I had been praying for his salvation for a long while at that point. I prayed something along the lines of \"God, save him, or prod him. Don't let him sit comfortably in his sin.\" It's simple enough, but I truly meant it. I didn't want my friend to reject the Lord. I had only shared the gospel with him one time, and he didn't really seem to care about any of it. One particular evening (out of the blue) he showed up to our church and started cursing at me and threatening to kill me and my family. At first I was very confused. There were a lot of security guards there ready to take my friend down, but I tried my best to de-escalate the situation before it got to that. Little kids were hearing what he was saying and running and crying asking their parents \"Why is that man saying those things to Jonathan?\" Once I just agreed with everything he said, he finally left. I was confused. \"Why would he act like that?\" To this day, the only conclusion I can draw is that it was through my prayers. God was doing a work on him. He was being consumed spiritually."},{"kind":"para","text":"You can be consumed spiritually and either fight against it, or accept God's changing in you."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that fight against it are rejecting salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that don't are accepting salvation."}]}]},{"start":15,"end":16,"title":"God Knows Best","entries":[{"start":15,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Fools make traps for the righteous, because God gives a path around the traps."},{"kind":"para","text":"What ends up happening, instead, is the fool gets caught in his own trap."},{"kind":"para","text":"It was intended for the innocent, but the evil is the one that will suffer for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"The lesson here is, don't set up traps for others."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you want to catch someone, give them something worth biting."},{"kind":"para","text":"The pleasures of this world are not worth the hook you sink into."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will take care of those that are His own."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that set up traps will have to take care of themselves, and if they fall into their own traps, it doesn't seem they are doing a very good job of that."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Higgaion\" means \"to muse,\" or \"to meditate.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The psalmist says, \"meditate on this fact.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Then he says, \"Pause, read back what you just read, and think about it before we change topics.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It is a fantastic verse to meditate on."},{"kind":"para","text":"Someone said that if there is a \"Selah\" that the Psalmist is transitioning into a statement about God's glory."},{"kind":"para","text":"Let's put that theory to the test here..."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"title":"The Reality of Hell","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Hmm..."},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems that that theory might be muddied a bit."},{"kind":"para","text":"I like it best to believe that the Selah tells us to think back, rather than anticipate forward."},{"kind":"para","text":"Too many of us are expecting a sigh of relief in the parts to come, when life is not like that."},{"kind":"para","text":"Life throws hard statements and plans at you."},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth, however, remains the truth, and those that are not righteous, those that are not Godly, those that are setting up traps, have made their home in hell."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that forget God will come to destruction."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those \"nations\" as we talked about earlier, will eventually decay and destroy themselves because of their lack of Godliness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Hell is a real place, and it's a place that is more described through Revelation."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no joke when it comes to the realities of hell."}]}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"title":"Rock Bottom","entries":[{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You might not know the needy persons name."},{"kind":"para","text":"You might meet them for a fleeting second, but if they take the riches of eternity, they will be known better in Heaven."},{"kind":"para","text":"A reality check for us is how well we treat those that are in need."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm not speaking about the needy in finances (those are plenty and few of them care about the real needs)."},{"kind":"para","text":"No, what I'm talking about is the needy in spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have come to their end."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have hit \"rock bottom.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"That's a good place to be."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you have truly hit \"rock bottom\" that means you cannot go any lower."},{"kind":"para","text":"Where is rock bottom?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The LORD is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust; my buckler, and the horn of my salvation, and my high tower.","ref":"Psalm 18:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For other foundation can no man lay than that is laid, which is Jesus Christ. Now if any man build upon this foundation gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, stubble; Every man's work shall be made manifest: for the day shall declare it, because it shall be revealed by fire; and the fire shall try every man's work of what sort it is.","ref":"1 Corinthians 3:11-13"}]}]},{"start":19,"end":20,"title":"Breaking Hearts","entries":[{"start":19,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That friend I spoke about earlier, do you know what my prayer is for him now?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The same thing."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't know how he is now, and I hope that there has been some sign of understanding in him somewhere, but I also ultimately hope that God is making him uncomfortable until he releases his pride and comes to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's obvious that this prayer is working, otherwise he wouldn't have flown off the handle like he did."},{"kind":"para","text":"God does a work that we know nothing about."},{"kind":"para","text":"It might be something He does physically, like destroying a city, but more often than not it is something He is doing spiritually, like breaking a heart."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh.","ref":"Ezekiel 36:26"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":20}]},
    "10": {"chapter":10,"intro":[],"previously":["Our last chapter was a bit of a whirlwind. David was writing about the highs and lows of our faith and walk with the Lord. He understands that God is paying attention, but there are times when it feels as if he's not. David knows that God has a purpose for all things, but He sometimes questions God's motives. Is there more to this life than just constant running from the enemy? Why does it seem the enemy is always succeeding more than God's children?","In this chapter, The Psalmist explores a little deeper into the life and cause of the wicked. He points out how the wicked get to be on top, and who suffers the consequences the most because of their evil reign."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":11,"title":"The Wicked Life","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Is it possible that God will stand far off from His children?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Is it in God's character to hide Himself from those that He has redeemed?"},{"kind":"para","text":"When Jesus was on the cross, He is seen saying this in Matthew:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And about the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani? that is to say, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?","ref":"Matthew 27:46"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is a quote from Psalm 22, so I won't spoil it quite yet."},{"kind":"para","text":"But we are getting the insinuation that the Psalmist, here, is feeling forsaken."},{"kind":"para","text":"God seems distant and hiding."},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps it's from the state of the writers spiritual standing."},{"kind":"para","text":"He may be far from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"My assumption is that this is still David writing and it's a bit of a continuation from the last Psalm where he said,"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the needy shall not alway be forgotten: the expectation of the poor shall not perish for ever. Arise, O LORD; let not man prevail: let the heathen be judged in thy sight. Put them in fear, O LORD: that the nations may know themselves to be but men. Selah.","ref":"Psalm 9:18-20"},{"kind":"para","text":"He's seeking God to serve justice to his oppressors, yet God seems to still be silent."},{"kind":"para","text":"So does God forsake His children?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Absolutely not."},{"kind":"para","text":"But He cannot look upon sin either."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sin, on this Earth, disgusts God."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is not to say there was an issue in David's life (though there were many), but this is to say that God wants to work a plan out for HIS good in the end, and it will require certain things to happen to innocent people (if we can call David this) so that it can transpire."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might not understand why it's happening when it does, but we can rest assured that God has a purpose for it in some way or another."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Psalmist will now give the image of the life of a wicked man."},{"kind":"para","text":"Wicked people abuse and persecute the poor."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are lacking are the ones they can hurt the most because they have the least."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, this is a still true statement and we see it a lot in our era today."},{"kind":"para","text":"The worst part is, it's only going to get worse when the end comes."},{"kind":"para","text":"The rich in this world will certainly be prospering, but they will be doing it on the corpses of the poor."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Psalmist wants the prideful to have a taste of their own medicine, and God will give them that."},{"kind":"para","text":"The most comforting thing to a Christian is to know that evil people will eventually have to have a conversation with the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And as it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment:","ref":"Hebrews 9:27"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You don't have to guess what's on the heart of the wicked."},{"kind":"para","text":"They usually make it known."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will talk about what they want, and they will do whatever it takes to get what they want."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've seen people sell extremely valuable possessions to get the next best thing (or at least what they think is the next best thing)."},{"kind":"para","text":"They may even be willing to give up arm and leg to get it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They cozy up to the people who can provide it so that they have a better standing for the possession, and then once they get it they bask in the presence of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe we all have this nature in us in one way or another."},{"kind":"para","text":"But this nature is abhorrent in God's eyes."},{"kind":"para","text":"God hates that we see material gain through our own strength and are willing to step on everyone to get it."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked won't seek God."},{"kind":"para","text":"They seek materialistic things to suffice their needs."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is their God."},{"kind":"para","text":"What can they get today that will make them feel better?"},{"kind":"para","text":"What is a good high to reach for while I am here on this Earth and I can buy it with my own hard earned money?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Those are their Gods."},{"kind":"para","text":"What kind of car do they drive?"},{"kind":"para","text":"What does their income look like?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Where are they living?"},{"kind":"para","text":"You can tell a lot about a person based on how they spend their money."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is the poor and needy that God takes special care of."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But I am poor and needy; yet the Lord thinketh upon me: thou art my help and my deliverer; make no tarrying, O my God.","ref":"Psalm 40:17"}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Those that have room for everything else on this Earth in their hearts, hardly ever have any room for the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They reject God because their gifts are for the here and now."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't seek for things that are eternal."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Set your affection on things above, not on things on the earth.","ref":"Colossians 3:2"}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Another obvious sign of a none believer is based on the words and stories he uses."},{"kind":"para","text":"Are his stories ones that are just air?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I mean do they speak just to be heard?"},{"kind":"para","text":"They might tell amazing stories, but in the end, did you learn anything from them?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Throughout the gospels (and this is not to say that Jesus didn't have a few times of just regular talk) the disciples represented Jesus as someone who always spent His moments with His friends telling stories that would help them LEARN something useful."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are called \"parables\" and they always spoke about eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"He didn't curse at anyone, he wasn't telling stories that were vain and meaningless, he wasn't lying about the stories and people either."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm not saying every word that comes out of your mouth should be used for teaching, but I believe that the sign of a mature Christian is one where they are constantly looking for opportunities to build others up (whether the other person is a Christian or not)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let no corrupt communication proceed out of your mouth, but that which is good to the use of edifying, that it may minister grace unto the hearers.","ref":"Ephesians 4:29"}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Wicked people go to wicked places."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are plenty of wicked places in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't call Las Vegas Strip \"Sin City\" for no reason."},{"kind":"para","text":"They tout their wickedness their."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are proud of it and accept the label, and anyone that goes there to gamble, and sit lurking, are usually there to avoid God and avoid righteousness."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are plenty of places in Vegas that are not \"Full of sin\" but that is boring to those that enjoy lurking."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have places even outside of Vegas that are the same."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you come to the beautiful, dry, high desert of California, you will still find strip clubs and bars."},{"kind":"para","text":"We found out pretty quickly who our governor was of this fine state the moment he closed down churches and kept the strip clubs and bars open during COVID."},{"kind":"para","text":"Ironically, those were also the first places he opened back up after COVID was \"over\" (as if this could ever be over, they are talking about requiring masks and vaccines again and it's been FOUR years)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Evil men like lurking places, and they like to murder the innocent (something else our governor is not shy of calling California \"The Abortion State\")."},{"kind":"para","text":"What does he know about the poor?"},{"kind":"para","text":"He hates those that are under him."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many poor people who have more money than others and they will look down on those who have less still."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a sad cruel world without the Lord."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked abuse the poor."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't mean just financially poor (though this is certainly true as well), but I'm talking about the spiritually poor."},{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked abuse those that are down in the dumps."},{"kind":"para","text":"They abuse those that aren't a benefit to them."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't want to help the poor, they want to keep the poor under their thumb."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is much of what state assistance does to the poor."},{"kind":"para","text":"It allows the government to help (as they should for the people) but their ultimate goal is to keep you in poverty, and keep you under their control and thumb."},{"kind":"para","text":"When Eva and I were first starting out, we were dirt poor. We didn't have a penny to our name. We didn't have any debts either so we were starting out pretty well. We went to see about Cashaid to help us financially get off our feet. They gave us quite a bit of money. After a little bit of this, Eva was able to get a job. We supposed that Cashaid would drop down a bit but it would still be something we can use as a mode of savings while we try and figure out our next steps. We didn't realize that they would get rid of it completely because she had a job. One job was not enough to support all three of us, so we were a bit stressed out. We called the place to see if there was a way we could keep even a small portion of the cashaid and they told us it was only for those that don't have a job at all... ...There can be no income coming into the household whatsoever if we wanted Cashaid. I'm not a English professor, but I'm pretty sure the suffix \"aid\" means \"help.\" This was suppose to be cash \"help\" not cash \"live off the government.\" I was a little confused. Why would they allow those that are not trying to get their lives straight to live free off the government? I believe it's because they want the poor and needy to depend on them."},{"kind":"para","text":"By the grace of God, we have not had to sign up again for Cashaid, and I hope we never do."},{"kind":"para","text":"But how sad and twisted it is for the higher ups, the so- called \"leaders\" to abuse their power to keep people dependent upon them."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be dependant upon the Lord and His provision, and these programs (if they were run by the right people and for the right reasons) should get us to see what kind of ethic the Lord wants His people to have."},{"kind":"para","text":"Worst yet, they lie about who they really are."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look what the Psalmist says about their demeanor."}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He pretends like he understands."},{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked man acts the part of a poor man so that he can trick a friendship with him and gain control over him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will even tell the poor, \"Obviously, God has forgotten you. God won't really care about your needs or take care of you.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Dear reader, can I just say, if a person tells you that God will not take care of you, you should be weary of that persons advice."},{"kind":"para","text":"Take everything they say with a grain of salt if they ever tell you that the Lord has forgotten."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":15,"title":"God Is Judge","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Psalmist is starting to believe the advice of the wicked."},{"kind":"para","text":"He's thinking, \"Did God forget us?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Evil people are soothsayers."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are enticing, flattering, and usually very warming to you."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will say all the right things, and play the part of a loving person very professionally, but they are only wearing a mask."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are \"hypocrites\" as Jesus liked to call them."},{"kind":"para","text":"A hypocrite (during the time of Jesus) was an actor in a play that wore a mask."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's what wicked people are to the poor."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are actors wearing a mask."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What's funny to me is there are a lot of Atheists (by definition, someone who doesn't believe in a god), who actually HATE God."},{"kind":"para","text":"How can they hate something that doesn't exist?"},{"kind":"para","text":"When prodded with this question they will say, \"Well we hate His representatives.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"They hate the poor of this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many, by and large (and I won't pretend there is not) who have given a bad name to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many in this world who pretend to represent the Lord and do a very poor job of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have no tact or grace in their message."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, they portray a God who does not love them and does not care for their wellbeing."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is just a judge."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is certainly a judge to them that don't know Him, but a Father to those that do."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have to remember this because we will get the wrong idea about our relationship with the Lord if we don't."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are too many pastors, leaders, and teachers who are teaching doctrines about the Lord as if He is the judge, and they are the jury."},{"kind":"para","text":"God makes the final judgement, but the pastor gets to put His congregation on the stand and testify against them."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is not how this works."},{"kind":"para","text":"Ministry leaders are not the jury."},{"kind":"para","text":"In California (and likely in most other states as well) if you are a registered voter, you will sometimes receive a jury-duty summons. You are required, by state law, to leave your place of work, attend a court date, and stand on the sidelines of a guy that you don't know, hear the case order, listen to the lawyers bicker between each other, and then come to a definitive decision with the rest of the jury to determine whether or not the person is innocent or guilty. And this is simply based on the limited information you received in the court hearing. Once the decision is made by the jury, that decision is taken to the judge and he rules whether or not the decision stands and what will ultimately be the responsibility of the person who is found guilty."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is a judge."},{"kind":"para","text":"He decides what happens to the guilty."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are all guilty before the judge (in this case, including the jury)."},{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn't have a jury though."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows everything about you."},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn't need evidence because He see's what you are doing."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has the right to convict you for lying, stealing, blaspheming, murder, and so much more."},{"kind":"para","text":"The pastor or leader of a church should not be there to condemn it's people."},{"kind":"para","text":"He should be there to point you to your lawyer, who is Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has the right to condemn you, but Jesus paid your fine."},{"kind":"para","text":"No jury is needed here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is your jury."},{"kind":"para","text":"He's the one that can dismiss your case."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we know Christ, God is not just a judge to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is our Father."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yes it is appointed unto man once to die and then we enter His judgement, but if we know Christ today we are entering the judgement hall to see our Father, not to just see the judge."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that don't know Christ today will see only a judge, and they will be placed on trial, and they will have no one to plead their case."},{"kind":"para","text":"May the Lord reach as many as possible before that comes."}]},{"start":14,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God know what is happening."},{"kind":"para","text":"He pays attention to the affairs of man."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is here with those that lean on Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has not left any of us or forsaken us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be strong and of a good courage, fear not, nor be afraid of them: for the LORD thy God, he it is that doth go with thee; he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.","ref":"Deuteronomy 31:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let your conversation be without covetousness; and be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.","ref":"Hebrews 13:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"God will take care of His own, and He will do what needs to be done with those that aren't."},{"kind":"para","text":"You can rest assured that God will punish the wicked."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will punish the world for their evil, and the wicked for their iniquity; and I will cause the arrogancy of the proud to cease, and will lay low the haughtiness of the terrible. I will make a man more precious than fine gold; even a man than the golden wedge of Ophir.","ref":"Isaiah 13:11-12"}]}]},{"start":16,"end":18,"title":"God Watches His Children","entries":[{"start":16,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will take care of His children."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows how to better than our own parents on Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows the purpose of trials."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows why He's allowed tests into His children's lives."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has a purpose for death, and crying, and mourning."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has a purpose for all things because He created all things."},{"kind":"para","text":"The things He created, He created with intention and meaning."},{"kind":"para","text":"He did not make an accident when He created tests."},{"kind":"para","text":"No, He does not test us with sin (that's a study for James), but He certainly tests us with fire."},{"kind":"para","text":"He tests us with spiritual issues that we would never know how to answer if we don't go to our Bibles to find them."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is King for ever and ever, and He will take care of those that feel they are lacking and in need of help."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":18}]},
    "11": {"chapter":11,"intro":[],"previously":["The book of Psalms, so far, has given us great reminders that God is in charge and He is constantly watching over His children even during the difficult and tiresome times of trial and testing. He is concerned about the affairs of mankind, and He does not desire that wickedness would prosper. In fact, He has done everything possible to make sure it doesn't. There will be a time in the end of days when wickedness will seem like it has won, and the battle is over, but the Lord will have the final sayso, and wickedness will not prosper (I promise you that).","In this chapter, we have a great reminder of who is on the throne. We can depend on the Lord during times of uncertainty, and we can't say that about anyone or anything else."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Nowhere Else To Go","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I have had many times of prayer in my life, even before I was a Christian."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a few times that come to mind, but one that I still won't forget until the day I day most likely."},{"kind":"para","text":"Before I was a Christian (this is during my teen years, roughly 16-18 years-old), I use to go camping a lot with my father. He enjoyed off-road vehicles (buggies, dirt bikes, quads and the sorts)... ...He bought (and it was fairly new at that time) a four-wheel buggy that kind of looked like a golf cart. He allowed me to drive it, and it was one of the most fun things to ride around in the dunes with. I took a few of the other boys in the camp along with me, and one was quite a few years younger than we were (around 12 years-old likely). I didn't check the seat belts on any of them because I assumed they knew what they were doing. We went up a few dunes and were starting to get a distance from the camp. I thought, \"I'll go up this one dune and head straight back towards camp.\" I went up the dune, and started heading back when I ran into what is called a \"Witches Eye.\" I had never seen one of these before today. It's basically just a big hole in the ground, but when you are driving it looks like flat ground as far as you can see. This particular drop was about 15 feet and there was nothing I can do going at about 50 miles per house straight towards it. My instinct was to hit my breaks and so I did, and we fell straight down, hitting nose first, flipping and smashing the top, and then landing on all four tires. The boy behind me didn't have his seat belt tight enough, and so he flew up, smacked his head on the crush roll bar, and then landed hard back into his seat. The amount of blood and pain he was in was enough to make the strongest people queasy. He couldn't breath. I was scared for his life, and the only thing I could do in a moment like this was pray. So that's what I did. I felt so horrible. He got about 13 stitches in his forehead, and we found out he broke a rib and it was pressing against his lung which is why he couldn't breathe."},{"kind":"para","text":"Today (now that I'm a Christian) I know better than to flee to the mountains for help."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only one I know to lean on and trust in for my souls matter is in the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have no one else I can trust to turn to when there are dire circumstances."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the only one that will always be there and will always have an answer to every problem I am going to face."},{"kind":"para","text":"David makes that clear in this verse here."},{"kind":"para","text":"His soul has nowhere to run."},{"kind":"para","text":"He HAS to trust in the Lord because the Lord is the only one with the answers and safety."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked may be firing at the righteous, but it is God who has the control over the arrow."},{"kind":"para","text":"This does not mean to purposely put yourself in harms way to see if God is willing to protect you, but rather when you find yourself in times of trouble, God will only allow what He wants to allow."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've seen it happen where guns jam point blank when aimed at someones head."},{"kind":"para","text":"God kept that person alive."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've seen it happen where cars break down after people are in a safe location rather than a few minutes before when they were on the freeway."},{"kind":"para","text":"God kept those people alive."},{"kind":"para","text":"God can control things that we call fluke, and it is obvious that it is a gift of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"You say, \"Well God could get rid of guns altogether, and He doesn't have to allow the car to break down.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"But really, you miss the teaching moments from the Lord when we think this way."},{"kind":"para","text":"Certainly God can keep our cars in tiptop shape, and He can keep our lives in it as well, but we must be willing to be used of Him to do so."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are not, then things fall apart, and that is no ones fault but our own."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will take care of what needs to be taken care of so that we are in full dependance on Him."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a great question."},{"kind":"para","text":"What is the foundation?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore whosoever heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them, I will liken him unto a wise man, which built his house upon a rock: And the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that house; and it fell not: for it was founded upon a rock. And every one that heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them not, shall be likened unto a foolish man, which built his house upon the sand: And the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that house; and it fell: and great was the fall of it.","ref":"Matthew 7:24-27"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For every house is builded by some man; but he that built all things is God.\" Hebrews 3:4 \"Except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain that build it: except the LORD keep the city, the watchman waketh but in vain.","ref":"Psalm 127:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"The foundation must be of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can build on faulty foundation (like building our lives on our sin, or on our own power) but those foundations will be destroyed."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then you will really have to ask, \"What can the righteous do?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"But if we build our lives on the foundation of Christ, we will never have to worry about it being destroyed."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now if any man build upon this foundation gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, stubble; Every man's work shall be made manifest: for the day shall declare it, because it shall be revealed by fire; and the fire shall try every man's work of what sort it is.","ref":"1 Corinthians 3:12-13"}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"Drink Your Cup","entries":[{"start":4,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously God is in power."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that reject Him, His power is against them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are for Him, His power is WITH them."},{"kind":"para","text":"We all have a choice in the morning to either reject the power of God, or accept the power of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"How our foundations prosper depends solely on our decision today."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They will drink from the cup they fill."},{"kind":"para","text":"They fill their cup up with snares, fire and brimstone, that is what they will drink from."},{"kind":"para","text":"They cannot drink from someone elses cup."},{"kind":"para","text":"Each person drinks from their own cup."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only one that drank from someone else cup was the Lord Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"He did not fill this cup Himself."},{"kind":"para","text":"We filled it for Him..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But I say unto you, I will not drink henceforth of this fruit of the vine, until that day when I drink it new with you in my Father's kingdom.","ref":"Matthew 26:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even that, though, He did with joy, knowing it meant that WE wouldn't have to drink from our own cups if we choose not to."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith; who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising the shame, and is set down at the right hand of the throne of God.","ref":"Hebrews 12:2"}]}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"title":"The Cup Of The Upright","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God wants to give us a cup full of joy and grace, and truth, and love, and every good gift!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, and cometh down from the Father of lights, with whom is no variableness, neither shadow of turning.","ref":"James 1:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"May we be seeking the Lord's good gift and filling so that we don't have to taste the bitter cup of death and sin."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For her sins have reached unto heaven, and God hath remembered her iniquities. Reward her even as she rewarded you, and double unto her double according to her works: in the cup which she hath filled fill to her double.","ref":"Revelation 18:5-6"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7}]},
    "12": {"chapter":12,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last chapter, we saw that God has a specific cup for every person to drink. We are obligated to drink from it when we put ourselves into positions that require it. Sometimes we are in a position of trial simply because we followed the Lord, other times we are put in a position of trial because we have not. Whatever the reason for it, we have to drink from the cup we pour ourselves. It is wise to pour the right things in rather than poison that will kill us because we neglected what we were suppose to be doing (likely out of fear).","In this chapter, we see the cup of sorrows being poured out, and it's a great picture of how it will look for the saved during the end times."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"A Cry For Help","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Faithful men calling for help from God is not a thing to be ridiculed or mocked."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of truly faithful men who are pressed hard enough that they feel overwhelmed."},{"kind":"para","text":"I find it odd that pastor's and preacher's all alike claim that their faith is so pure and holy that they never need to cry for help."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is unbiblical and absolutely un-Christlike."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus was constantly pleading with the Father about every need He ever had."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And in the morning, rising up a great while before day, he went out, and departed into a solitary place, and there prayed.","ref":"Mark 1:35"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then cometh Jesus with them unto a place called Gethsemane, and saith unto the disciples, Sit ye here, while I go and pray yonder.","ref":"Matthew 26:36"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he withdrew himself into the wilderness, and prayed.","ref":"Luke 5:16"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will pray the Father, and he shall give you another Comforter, that he may abide with you for ever;","ref":"John 14:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"It's okay to cry to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, it's recommended and needful to do so."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don't allow a second to pass by where you are not in prayer to God about your needs, begging Him for help."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are not searching to receive help from the Lord, God will be sure to put you in a position where you either have to, or you will become hardened even more."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"All David see's is a surrounding full of people who are not saved and who are not seeking after God."},{"kind":"para","text":"I do believe this will be a lot of what the last days will be like."},{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a Godly remnant still existing in those times, and they will see heinous and terrible things happening all around them, and they will pray and call out for help from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Worst yet, the Godly will likely see ungodly things happening behind the pulpits of the church."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will entice people with vain and useless things and draw away from the most important thing which is the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will preach about prosperity and self-fulfillment (much of what the church does today) and they will miss out on salvation and the work of the Lord."}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Some people think that their quips and clever remarks are SO GOOD that it even exceeds the Word of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many behind the pulpit today who talk about this issue or that issue, and they preach against this religion or that religion, or they yell about what this person is doing or that person is not doing."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be very weary of hearing this from God's podium."},{"kind":"para","text":"Life should flow from behind the pulpit."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's Word is the only thing that suffices."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we mix in our feelings and our political agendas with God's Word we get one of two messages."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will either be a very hateful message, or it will be a very diluted message."},{"kind":"para","text":"If it's hateful, no one will grow from it and everyone will feel attacked and betrayed by the preacher."},{"kind":"para","text":"If it's diluted, no one will grow from it and everyone will be tricked into thinking they doing just fine right where they are."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is a line that has to be walked if you are called to preach."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you preach, you must do it with prayer and Spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"You can tell when a preacher is missing one of those things."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"title":"Stop The Evil","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will allow the evil to have it's way for a time."},{"kind":"para","text":"It baffles me when people complain that God would \"allow\" evil to happen on this Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn't FORCE you to do evil things."},{"kind":"para","text":"If there are evil people, they are evil on their own behalfs and you cannot place charge to God because of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"But He certainly DOES allow evil to happen here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone will say it's \"for a reason\" but the real reason for it is often lost in translation."},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason for it is simple."},{"kind":"para","text":"When things are going well, evil people will say that they are doing a good job and their hard work got them there."},{"kind":"para","text":"When things are not going well, evil people blame the Lord for not intervening and then claim as if God never really cared to begin with."},{"kind":"para","text":"Evil things happen to evil people, and seeing as the whole world is evil, we all will experience evil things happening to us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;","ref":"Romans 3:23"},{"kind":"para","text":"God waits for evil to be put out there before He makes a move because He wants people to know that He has power to stop it and intercede if they would just come to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather than come to Him, however, people are usually upset with Him and reject Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He's also tried to bless people who are against Him and they STILL won't come to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"No matter what God does, there will be people who abuse their own strength, and so God allows this to happen for a time, but He doesn't allow it forever."},{"kind":"para","text":"Pain eventually ends, whether that's because the evil has been stopped through a change of heart, or the end of life..."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"God's Word Stands","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a very good verse."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's Word is \"refined.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It's been tried over and over again, and the trying of it has proved that it is worth more than gold."},{"kind":"para","text":"It can stand the tests of time."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is capable of being tested, and it is always able to prove itself right."},{"kind":"para","text":"People try and twist parts of it to match what they want it to mean, or they try and deny it because they don't like what it says, but just because you don't like it or because you try and twist it doesn't make it any less of the truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"Deny it, twist it all you want, in the end God's Word is final and it is PURE."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no flaw in it, and those that choose to deny it or twist it only cause damage to their own souls."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God's Word is everlasting."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But the word of the Lord endureth for ever. And this is the word which by the gospel is preached unto you.","ref":"1 Peter 1:25"},{"kind":"para","text":"I imagine that when we get to Heaven we will know it by heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will still be what we live by."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, things that we don't understand today will likely be illuminated in eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will see why we didn't understand it now, and we will see more than what was being illustrated through what we have here on Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"His Word will stand even after the world no longer is."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God's Word stands."},{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked (especially in the end) will be numerous, and they will look like the most powerful people of all time."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, wicked people usually have an army following them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are chosen of God usually have very little following them."},{"kind":"para","text":"There was a time when Jesus had thousands walking behind him, and it was dwindled down to 12."},{"kind":"para","text":"12 were found faithful in the end."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is a perfect look at the righteousness of this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will not find many who are truly God's, and so there will be wicked people who will rise up, and the wicked of this world (the fakes) will follow suit."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will follow wicked things because they are wicked people."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And we know that we are of God, and the whole world lieth in wickedness.","ref":"1 John 5:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is a rare thing to find truly sold out people of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a very easy thing to find people who are faking it, or people who are looking to follow wickedness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, that is who the world looks for."},{"kind":"para","text":"They look for the vilest men to exalt and lift up as their example of who to follow."},{"kind":"para","text":"Thankfully we have a better example and there is no wickedness in Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For thou art not a God that hath pleasure in wickedness: neither shall evil dwell with thee.","ref":"Psalm 5:4"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":8}]},
    "13": {"chapter":13,"intro":[],"previously":["It seems in these past few chapters that David was on a worship of plea to the Lord. He feels very heavy burdened, and so he continues to turn to the Lord. We see him start off, over and over again, with a plea for God's help, a prayer for God's action, and then an assurance of God's presence.","In this chapter, it is more of the same. David feels trapped and forgotten, he requests God's provision, and then rests in the choices that God will make. May we learn to do the same as we go through the trials with David in these chapters."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Where Are You?","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David was likely on the run from Saul at this particular point in the Psalms."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is likely writing this from the cave Adullam, and he is wondering where God is during this difficult trek in his life."},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn't know what to do."},{"kind":"para","text":"Does he just kill Saul and end it here, or does he live a life of a vagabond and continue to run."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think we have all run into this situation where we are asking why to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"We wonder where He is when everything seems to be falling apart, but the truth is, God uses those times the most in our lives."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might not enjoy it, but God chose us to go through it for a reason."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes we don't figure out that reason until much later in life, but we can be confident that God entrusted us with the trial and wanted us to go through it specifically."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Not only does David feel rejected by the Lord, but He also feels rejected by the people around him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He feels as if he is truly and utterly alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we read the account of his fleeing from Saul, there wasn't very much time where he was truly alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, there were a few hundred men who start following him when he gets into this particular cave."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet he feels alone somehow."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I've been in this style of despair before (maybe not with my life on the lines as was David, but feeling extremely alone and forgotten about), and yet I knew there were hundreds of people all around me who cared enough to try and counsel me."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet I felt alone, not because of the people."},{"kind":"para","text":"I felt alone because of the absence of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"When God doesn't seem like he's there, there is nothing that anyone can say or do around you to make you feel any better."},{"kind":"para","text":"It truly feels like you are alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christians become so keen of feeling God's Spirit in them, that they don't think much of maintaining that Spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"So when it's depleted (which it certainly can be), they don't know what's wrong."},{"kind":"para","text":"They feel like everything is off and nothing will be the same again."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is very much possible to fill your Spirit again, it will just take some time and care."},{"kind":"para","text":"A full Spirit is one that is worth seeking out and waiting on, because an empty spirit makes for misery and sadness."},{"kind":"para","text":"So what do we do to get the right spirit?"},{"kind":"para","text":"David learns this quickly..."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"title":"Help Me Rest","entries":[{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David turns to the Lord for a renewed spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"He asks the Lord to open his eyes and see what God see's."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants a new vision for the things he's experiencing."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to know what God knows."},{"kind":"para","text":"What a truly connective verse to us today who have gone through a situation that just doesn't make sense."},{"kind":"para","text":"God, in all His sovereignty, chooses to allow us to go through trials and drifting."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then, He brings us back in when we look to Him and ask for fresh eyes."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we ask, He always provides!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you:","ref":"Matthew 7:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"Our enemies would love to catch us sleeping when they are in pursuit."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes our enemy is someone that is close to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"David loved Saul, and he was afraid to sleep because he knew Saul was after him and trying to kill him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Saul's son, Jonathan, usually went to David to help encourage him in the Lord, but David didn't have that privilege in this particular area."},{"kind":"para","text":"So David decides to ask God for some comfort while he tries to get some rest, so that his enemy doesn't try and kill him and destroy him in his sleep."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"title":"Trust in the Lord","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That is how our Spirit can be renewed."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moment we stop worrying about the situation and just say, \"Well, I have trusted in the Lord. I prayed to Him, gave it to Him, and have let it go. Now it is up to the Lord to do what He wants with it. If it's good, than great! If it's bad, than great! It's completely up to God now.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"What an amazing comfort that comes over us when we leave the situation up to God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even if it goes wrong, it will be right because the Lord can only do what is good."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We can rejoice over the fact that God will do what is right."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can rest in the fact that God knows what's best."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can gain confidence in the fact that God will always know what to do."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can grow in faith in fact that God is always paying attention."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can have peace because we know God cares about the issues of man."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can sing because God has the victory."},{"kind":"para","text":"No matter what situation we might face (even if it's some of the most difficult situations our lives can bear), God will always have the glory, and He deserves to be praised because He knows, and does all things for His good pleasure and Will."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6}]},
    "14": {"chapter":14,"intro":[],"previously":["In the last chapter, the Psalmist was seeking closeness from the Lord during a very turbulous life stage. He needed the Lords comfort and guidance through the dangers of this world, and searched it out every where he could. Eventually he realizes that the Lord is there and that He is providing love and direction to those that seek Him.","In this chapter, we see desolation, desperation, and depletion from this world and the saints that live in it. There will be a day (and it could be counted even now) where God will not be able to find a soul that is willing to be saved. He will be searching, and the whole world will have turned against Him."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Nothing Left To Save","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Fools call the Christians fools, which is kind of funny to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"Being called a fool for believing in the Lord by another human being doesn't bother me nearly as much as being called a fool by the Lord in this verse here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, it's pretty foolish for a man to reject the obvious existence of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether you want to believe in the God of the Bible or not, you cannot deny the evidential truth of a creator."},{"kind":"para","text":"The wisdom of this world only provides you with a false sense of security."},{"kind":"para","text":"As a man who lived by the worlds wisdom for most of my life, I can relate to your desire to seek after vain pleasures and traditions of the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Today, we have a lot of false truths being presented in society."},{"kind":"para","text":"Many men and women alike are falling victim to a false reality that they can become or be anything that they desire and it will make them somehow feel good about who they are and about their lives."},{"kind":"para","text":"In reality, many have treaded those paths, have taken those pills, and have come out on the otherside further in debt, more lonely and more confused."},{"kind":"para","text":"The God of scripture gives us a clear viewpoint and understanding of this life."},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn't sugarcoat your ears with fancies of easy living."},{"kind":"para","text":"He tells you the truth, whether you like it or not, and He will give you the answers, whether you like it or not."},{"kind":"para","text":"My only advice for those that are struggling with speaking this truth to the world is to continue to keep on doing it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It might seem redundant and simple to you, but to everyone else it's new and confusing."},{"kind":"para","text":"Continue to give the plain evidentual truth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"\"Let no man deceive himself. If any man among you seemeth to be wise in this world, let him become a fool, that he may be wise. For the wisdom of this world is foolishness with God. For it is written, He taketh the wise in their own craftiness.\" 1","ref":"Corinthians 3:18-19"},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason many reject the gospel message today is not because they don't believe it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's because they don't want to let go of their lifestyle of sin, and it's far easier to stay the same than it is to seek the truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"But eternity will beg for them to accept the truth now."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That is what the Lord is constantly doing."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows who will be saved and who won't."},{"kind":"para","text":"He put each of us in this world knowing exactly what we were going to do with our faith and our salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows whether or not we are going to come to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"But He is constantly watching and looking and guiding for each person to their specific destination."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether that be Heaven with Him, or Hell in torment."},{"kind":"para","text":"God watches, and He intervenes in everyone's affairs."},{"kind":"para","text":"The problem is, those that don't want Him, reject every notion of intervening by the Lord."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Since the beginning of time, there have been none that seeks to do good."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the New Testament, there is still no change."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;","ref":"Romans 3:23"},{"kind":"para","text":"In the end times, this will be the viewpoint of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be far worse because there will not be a single soul left on Earth that is willing to turn to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are all going to be living in their luxuries, abusing the poor, killing the Christians, and rejecting the Creator."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will look down and seek for ONE man to turn to Him, and won't find it."},{"kind":"para","text":"The whole world will have gone aside, and there will be nothing left for Him to save."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"Nothing Good Left","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Think about it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's one thing for the world to be against God (and plenty of atheists acclaim that they are), but it's another thing entirely to be a people against the people of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't just hate God, they hate people."},{"kind":"para","text":"I could argue they even hate atheistic people."},{"kind":"para","text":"They lead people away from the truth, and torment them with false ideologies and vain theories without any sort of proof."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have more proof that the God of scripture exists than they do that He doesn't, and yet they would rather accept the lack of proof and the lack of evidence because (and I truly believe this to be the case) they hate people."},{"kind":"para","text":"They like the idea of people feeling miserable and having no desire for the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They enjoy seeing people struggle, and giving them anguish and pain in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"This world is certainly painful, and the people of this world are evil and hateful (which further proves scripture by the way)."},{"kind":"para","text":"But those that indoctrinate nonbelievers are people enjoy watching the world burn."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't want a better society, they want a chaotic society."},{"kind":"para","text":"They want to hurt and maim even the least of these..."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Think back, was there every a generation of the righteous? Recently, my daughter was in her online class and one of the students said (out loud), \"God loves you.\" and the teacher muted her. When she became muted, another student typed in the group chat that Jesus loves them all, and the teacher got after these students for talking about these things. She said, \"We are not going to talk about that stuff in this class.\" I understand her precaution about this topic because it could be her job on the line, but I also understand these childrens desire to share the truth that they know and are assured of. They know that Jesus loves them, and they want others to know it too."},{"kind":"para","text":"Is this the generation of righteousness?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I doubt it, but I think there are still a good many generations before the generation of unrighteousness (and the end of all things)."},{"kind":"para","text":"This new generation gives me hope."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are willing to speak their mind in this generation with more confidence than their own teachers and leaders."},{"kind":"para","text":"I pray that it gives them boldness to tell others about this love rather than shy away."},{"kind":"para","text":"I pray that his generation is a generation of righteousness, and they are able to spark revival for their peers."},{"kind":"para","text":"I pray that this generation would be more of fire for preaching and witnessing about the Lord than my generation is about telling them that they are accidents."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The rich in this world only seek one thing and it isn't in promoting the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even rich preachers today are not seeking to promote and encourage others in the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They want more money."},{"kind":"para","text":"They never have enough."},{"kind":"para","text":"I forget who said it but he was a rich man in an interview. The interviewer said, \"You seem to just keep getting more and more rich by the second, what motivates you to keep going?\" and the rich man said, \"I wake up every morning and say, 'Just one more dollar.'\""},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the life he led."},{"kind":"para","text":"Just one more dollar."},{"kind":"para","text":"His dollars amount to nothing now in his eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, his dollars got him higher, and the rest of the people around him lower."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rich men do not care about those that have no money."},{"kind":"para","text":"They can't care less about the poor."},{"kind":"para","text":"The poor are so little to them that they belittle and abuse their power over them."},{"kind":"para","text":"They want to \"shame\" the poor rather than help the poor."},{"kind":"para","text":"It irritates me (and probably those that are truly in need of help) when big companies give money to big companies thinking they are helping those in need."},{"kind":"para","text":"That money is rarely ever seen to those that truly need it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They cannot give to anything that is actually important for those that are struggling."},{"kind":"para","text":"There aren't even many churches who are using their money for the proper things."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what a church is for."},{"kind":"para","text":"A genuine church is to provide for the poor and the needy."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are to help meet their financial needs and get them out of their poverty."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you truly want to give to the poor, start donating to small local churches who preach the gospel of Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will (I guarantee) provide to those that need it because they are commanded by their God to do so."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"title":"Scripture Fulfilled","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David is writing this during a time when Israel was living in a decent amount of prosperity."},{"kind":"para","text":"It would seem a bit strange for him to write this if they are in a generation seeking after the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe they were still struggling with their faith, and they needed a leader that would point that back to where they were suppose to go."},{"kind":"para","text":"They needed a leader who could be an example."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the future, however, there will be a time (and this is extremely true today) where Israel will turn away from the Lord once more, and will be led into captivity (again)."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will be searching for the savior at that point, and when this happens, they will be calling back to the Lord in search of His protection and guidance."},{"kind":"para","text":"And He will come."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ will return out of Zion and protect His people and lead them into the promised land."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously the Lord has a plan and a purpose for Israel in the future, and that is why we should take special note of the things that are happening there today."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7}]},
    "15": {"chapter":15,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last chapter, we get a bleak look at this world and the future of the lost. The Psalmist points out that there will be nothing left worth saving, no good will be found on this Earth, and scripture will always be fulfilled no matter what the human race might try and do to stop it.","In this chapter, we see a message on hope and encouragement towards the world to turn to the Lord and know how to dwell with Him. It is not through our actions and works, but through our desire to live for the Lord that we have a place to live with Him for eternity. This is a great chapter to remember how important the truth and Christ are for this world, and in our own personal lives."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Dwelling With God","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord has a Heavenly tabernacle that the book of Revelation speaks about."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I heard a great voice out of heaven saying, Behold, the tabernacle of God is with men, and he will dwell with them, and they shall be his people, and God himself shall be with them, and be their God.","ref":"Revelation 21:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to dwell with man, but that can't come about until sin has been destroyed (that will happen in the end by the way)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And there shall be no more curse: but the throne of God and of the Lamb shall be in it; and his servants shall serve him:","ref":"Revelation 22:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"Ugh, to be rid of sin once and for all cannot come soon enough."},{"kind":"para","text":"But here, in this chapter of scripture, David is speaking about a \"holy hill\" which will continuously be referenced as \"Zion.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It was where David enjoyed staying, and it became a well known symbol of God's overlooking of Israel."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, Zion is not much to look at today, and I don't imagine it was much to look at back then."},{"kind":"para","text":"I do find it odd that this is the place that represents a heavenly tabernacle, but that was the place in which the Lord was doing His working at the time, and that was the place in which David specifically chose out to represent it."},{"kind":"para","text":"The question is ask, \"Who will dwell there?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"A better question might be posed this way, \"Who will be ABLE to dwell there?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"If we looked at the world around us, we wouldn't find anyone worthy to dwell with the Lord on His holy hill."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is why Christ came."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the question the world must face."},{"kind":"para","text":"If God is real (and it couldn't be more evident that He is), then how do we live with Him? How do we come before His presence?"}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot walk uprightly on our own."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because we like our flesh."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"This I say then, Walk in the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfil the lust of the flesh. For the flesh lusteth against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh: and these are contrary the one to the other: so that ye cannot do the things that ye would.","ref":"Galatians 5:16-17"},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot have any righteousness to work on our own."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because we like our flesh!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But we are all as an unclean thing, and all our righteousnesses are as filthy rags; and we all do fade as a leaf; and our iniquities, like the wind, have taken us away.","ref":"Isaiah 64:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For Christ is the end of the law for righteousness to every one that believeth.","ref":"Romans 10:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot speak the truth in (or out of) our hearts."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because we like our flesh!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For with the heart man believeth unto righteousness; and with the mouth confession is made unto salvation.","ref":"Romans 10:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"David points out here that there is a way for us to dwell with God, but he gives us a list here that is not achievable and he knows it."},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot work to be these things because we will always work the opposite way."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe he might have been thinking of the old king when he wrote this perhaps."},{"kind":"para","text":"I know it's inspired, but Saul was the very opposite of what David is writing about here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Saul sought after his flesh in every circumstance."},{"kind":"para","text":"He didn't walk uprightly, or work righteousness, or speak the truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"He continuously did the opposite of this, and it was mostly toward David."},{"kind":"para","text":"David knows that the Lord must be the only one that provides this for a man, and the only way for a man to have these attributes is to accept the Lord's providence."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the entire symbol of the generations of Israel."},{"kind":"para","text":"If they rejected the Lord's leading, they fell apart."},{"kind":"para","text":"If they accepted it, they would dwell with God."},{"kind":"para","text":"It really is that simple."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now these three things are things that every human being can control within themselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should not be backbiting against anyone."},{"kind":"para","text":"We shouldn't be talking back and making life more difficult than it needs to be."},{"kind":"para","text":"We shouldn't be doing evil against people that we know, or against those that are around us."},{"kind":"para","text":"When it uses the term \"neighbour\" it's not talking about the person that lives next door to you."},{"kind":"para","text":"No, it's talking about a living person who is near you literally and physically."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you go to the store to grocery shop, you will be around people, and those people are now considered your \"neighbours.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We should all have the ability to abstain from reproaching or stirring up strife with our neighbors, but most of us won't."},{"kind":"para","text":"We won't because (once again) we like our flesh."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some of us stir up strife because we like to start fights."},{"kind":"para","text":"We get a kick out of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some of us do it because we want to get even."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some of us do it because we have a goal of coming out on top in this world, and we will gladly do it on the backs of our neighbors."},{"kind":"para","text":"But a Christian, one who is owned by the Lord, should not be found in these things."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we have strife against our neighbors, it should not be because we initiated it."},{"kind":"para","text":"If David meant that those that can dwell with God are those that have perfect communion with their neighbors, David was already out of the picture."},{"kind":"para","text":"He fought with the Philistines around him for years."},{"kind":"para","text":"But he wasn't the one initiating the fight."},{"kind":"para","text":"It was always the Philistines coming for a battle."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If it be possible, as much as lieth in you, live peaceably with all men.","ref":"Romans 12:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, that won't happen when the people who you are trying to live at peace with don't want to live in peace with you."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"title":"Preserving the Truth","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"\"contemned\" means \"disdain\" or \"to despise.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't see this much today."},{"kind":"para","text":"We honor the vile."},{"kind":"para","text":"We honor those that have a loud voice, and usually those that are heard the most are those that don't have anything good to say."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are filled with sugar."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yes, it sounds sweet and good to those of this world, but in the end it just leaves them hungry and aching."},{"kind":"para","text":"Too much sugar will kill you, and that's all this world wants."},{"kind":"para","text":"But the Lord has not called us to be \"sugar.\""},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye are the salt of the earth: but if the salt have lost his savour, wherewith shall it be salted? it is thenceforth good for nothing, but to be cast out, and to be trodden under foot of men.","ref":"Matthew 5:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"There's much I could say about this verse (and there will certainly be time to speak about it in the book of Matthew) but this insinuates that we should add something special to the conversation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Salt is a preservative."},{"kind":"para","text":"It helps to SAVE food when it's salted."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are certainly suppose to add that to the conversation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet it's not usually the Christians that are lifted up with honor."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is usually the vile, and they don't preserve anything but themselves..."},{"kind":"para","text":"HOWEVER, the Lord will honor those that follow Him and are not swayed by the sugar of this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that dwell with God are not willing to be swayed by the culture, and will even be willing to be hurt for the truth (as this verse insinuates \"he that sweareth to his own hurt...\")"},{"kind":"para","text":"That's a great question to ask yourself."},{"kind":"para","text":"How valuable is the truth to us?"},{"kind":"para","text":"What are we willing to do for the truth?"},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems there are many willing to go to great lengths for a klondike bar more than they are willing to for the truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"There's another sermon topic for you for free!"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Can you be bribed away from the truth?"},{"kind":"para","text":"How much does the truth cost to you?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Is it so valuable that you cannot put a price on it, or can you be bought off so that the truth will be hidden?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth has value."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Buy the truth, and sell it not; also wisdom, and instruction, and understanding.","ref":"Proverbs 23:23"},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth costs something."},{"kind":"para","text":"Lies also cost, but it's usually the person that lies who gets the paycheck."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we speak the truth, we don't usually get paid for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"We usually get reprimanded for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I was growing up, telling the truth to my dad was a difficult task. He would beat us if we told the truth, and he would beat us harder if he found out we lied... ...The truth seemed like an easier beating to take. For example, one particular evening my dad came into the house and started in on us about a brick that had fallen off the wall outside. We had a brick wall that was about 2 feet tall to separate our front yard from the neighbors front yard and it went along our driveway all the way to the sidewalk in the neighborhood. Apparently some kid came over and knocked the end brick off, and my dad thought it was one of us. We exclaimed that it was not us. \"I know one of you is lying,\" he said, \"and you are both grounded until one of you confesses.\" Of course my brother didn't want to confess to something he didn't do, so he tasked me with the job. \"Just go tell him you did it so we can get out of grounding!\" he said. \"But I DIDN'T do it!\" I shot back. \"So what? Do you want to stay grounded forever?\" No. Of course I didn't. And I was willing to lie about it now so I can face the punishment and get it over with. So I went, and I lied to my dad telling him I knocked it over and I was sorry. \"It wasn't you.\" He said. \"Until you guys tell me the truth you are still both grounded.\" What can I do now? I was in trouble for lying, and I was in trouble for telling the truth. Lying seemed like a better reward and it gave me the same outcome in this situation and the lie was for something GOOD."},{"kind":"para","text":"Lying is never right unless it's to save a life."},{"kind":"para","text":"The cost of telling the truth will usually cost a life..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For ye are bought with a price: therefore glorify God in your body, and in your spirit, which are God's.","ref":"1 Corinthians 6:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"That price was very high, and it cost the life of the truth!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","ref":"John 14:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"What does the truth cost to you?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Can you be bought off to keep the truth a secret?"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":5}]},
    "16": {"chapter":16,"intro":[],"previously":["Psalms is a book written with a rollercoaster of emotions. You never know what you are going to get when you pick up the next Psalm. It could be something joyful, or it can be something woeful. The fact of the matter is, if you pick up a woeful Psalm, you will always see the Lord present some love and joy in there somewhere.","Todays Psalm is no different. It has (mostly) high notes throughout all of it, but it is very much centered around the Lord and His life. David (of course) was experiencing personal turmoil in his own life, but he is using his own circumstances to (probably unknowingly) prophecy of the Savior of the world."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"God Is Near","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Only God preserves what is good and right."},{"kind":"para","text":"His Word is preserved."},{"kind":"para","text":"His Son is preserved."},{"kind":"para","text":"His righteousness is preserved."},{"kind":"para","text":"His holiness is preserved."},{"kind":"para","text":"God knows how to preserve, and the things that are not preserved will not be preserved for a reason."},{"kind":"para","text":"Many of the Psalms (if not nearly all of them) talk about the Savior, and can be applied to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is likely how we can break this Psalm down as well, because it is a great picture of Jesus."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Something I should have suppose I have seen coming was my daughter calling me \"Dad\" rather than \"Daddy.\" I wouldn't guess that she would call me her \"Daddy\" for the rest of her life. It's one of those things that you kind of just grow out of. \"Daddy\" is easier for babies to say. Dad is the simplified version of saying it. I enjoyed that name. I enjoy the fact that I am her dad at all. I believe that the Lord enjoys it when we call Him Father, or Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"God should be the King of our lives, and we should be referencing Him as our Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"David seems to imply that his soul is filled with the desire to call out to the Lord by name and in closeness like this."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is Lord, but He is not unreachable."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"title":"Accepted In The Beloved","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We belong to Him, and He to us, and that is a very great privilege for all of us to have."},{"kind":"para","text":"We shouldn't be able to know God personally like He has allowed us to."},{"kind":"para","text":"If God is God, and I am me, then how can it be that we can have any sort of connection at all."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what God wants though."},{"kind":"para","text":"His delight is in the saints of this Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"He loves His own."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that know Him and follow Him love Him back."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that don't... Well, it's not a very happy life..."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The very names of those that reject the Lord are not worthy to be called upon."},{"kind":"para","text":"I want to love everyone that I come across, don't get me wrong, but there is never going to be a chance that I can trust someone who is not a saved person."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are even saved people whom you will have a hard time trusting, but I can trust you more if you are genuinely saved (proving your fruits) than if you are not (proving your ungodliness)."},{"kind":"para","text":"I will love you, and I will encourage you, but I will also never be able to receive that same thing FROM you and we will both know it."},{"kind":"para","text":"There will always be a disconnect between the saved and the unsaved."},{"kind":"para","text":"Think of it like a family."},{"kind":"para","text":"We all have family, and there will be some who are very loving and giving to one another."},{"kind":"para","text":"On the flip side, there will be some who are not forgiving and very unloving to one another."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I was younger, a cousin of mine came over to our house and I asked if he could spend the night. His father married my aunt, so we were not blood related at all. I asked him if he wanted to say, and he said, \"Well we aren't really cousins.\" \"Yes we are!\" I said. I went and asked my mom if he could stay, and my cousin shot out with, \"I completely understand if I'm not allowed to, I know we are not really related.\" I don't think my mom was ready for that response, and I think it hurt her a little bit so she said, \"It doesn't matter where you come from, or what you have done, you are our family.\" and my cousin nearly broke down in tears and said, \"Really?\" \"Of course!\" My mom said."},{"kind":"para","text":"When you are accepted by the Lord, you are fully accepted in His family."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you don't know the Lord, how can you be excepted?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Now if a stranger came into my house and I were to ask my mom that same question, she would of course say no, and likely kick the stranger out."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord knows His family, and He accepts them, and loves them as His own."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that don't know Him just have lives of weeping and misery because the family of this world has nothing nice to offer you."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"According as he hath chosen us in him before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy and without blame before him in love: Having predestinated us unto the adoption of children by Jesus Christ to himself, according to the good pleasure of his will, To the praise of the glory of his grace, wherein he hath made us accepted in the beloved.","ref":"Ephesians 1:4-6"}]}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"title":"A Full Cup","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a great verse!"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is my portion."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is my sustenance."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is my needs."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the portion of my inheritance."},{"kind":"para","text":"He gives me what is best (even if I don't think it's best, or I don't like it)."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is my cup."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't know about you, but if I had the choice between eating for the rest of my life or drinking for the rest of my life, I would prefer to drink."},{"kind":"para","text":"I love water, and soda, and teas, and all sorts of drinks."},{"kind":"para","text":"I may not enjoy my portions, but I will always finish my cup."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is strange to me to think about it this way, but it is often the referenced used in scripture."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"How sweet are thy words unto my taste! yea, sweeter than honey to my mouth!","ref":"Psalm 119:103"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But I tell you of a truth, there be some standing here, which shall not taste of death, till they see the kingdom of God.","ref":"Luke 9:27"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"O taste and see that the LORD is good: blessed is the man that trusteth in him.","ref":"Psalm 34:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Our taste buds are used in scripture to describe more than physical taste."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's Word is a sweet sustenance, and it is useful to preserving those that eat of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"I find it interesting that David uses the term \"cup\" here."},{"kind":"para","text":"It, too, can refer to many things of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Likewise also the cup after supper, saying, This cup is the new testament in my blood, which is shed for you.\" Luke 22:20 \"Thou shalt be filled with drunkenness and sorrow, with the cup of astonishment and desolation, with the cup of thy sister Samaria.\" Ezekiel 23:33"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Awake, awake, stand up, O Jerusalem, which hast drunk at the hand of the LORD the cup of his fury; thou hast drunken the dregs of the cup of trembling, and wrung them out.","ref":"Isaiah 51:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye cannot drink the cup of the Lord, and the cup of devils: ye cannot be partakers of the Lord's table, and of the table of devils.","ref":"1 Corinthians 10:21"},{"kind":"para","text":"I think the most relative verse is this one;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Saying, Father, if thou be willing, remove this cup from me: nevertheless not my will, but thine, be done.","ref":"Luke 22:42"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is a cup that is worthy to be drinking, and then there are cups that will make you sick."},{"kind":"para","text":"If the Lord is your cup, it is worth drinking the whole thing because He will provide more and more."},{"kind":"para","text":"A cup, I believe is a great illustration of us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are emptied out, or consumed quite often, yet the Lord has an overflowing amount of grace, mercy, peace, and love for those that are HIS cups. He pours His grace when we are feeling depleted. He pours His mercy when we are feeling defeated. He pours His peace when we are feeling confused. He pours His love when we are feeling rejected. Best part is, our cup runs OVER."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thou preparest a table before me in the presence of mine enemies: thou anointest my head with oil; my cup runneth over.","ref":"Psalm 23:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"But I'm getting ahead of myself."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord's leading is good for those that follow Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have a good heritage because we are in the family of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"David had a GREAT heritage because it's promised through him that the Messiah will be born."},{"kind":"para","text":"His lineage will lead to the salvation of the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"David knew very little about this Savior, and the Lord had dropped hints and glimmers of hope to every child of His throughout the Old Testament, but they weren't ready for it, and if they knew the extent of God's mercy and sacrifice, they wouldn't believe it anyway."},{"kind":"para","text":"I know this to be a fact because they had Isaiah's testimony and still don't believe it to this day."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":9,"title":"Taken Care Of","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When I wake up, I am usually very groggy and tired."},{"kind":"para","text":"I will roll over and open my phone (bad habits), and go to my bible app, and read the verse of the day (good habits)."},{"kind":"para","text":"But when I go to sleep, that is when my biggest worries come to mind."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I wake up, my brain is fresh with contemplations and things that I can't even think about."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I go to bed, my brain is running on full steam, and I can't help but think about the bills I have to worry about and the ministries I have to prepare for."},{"kind":"para","text":"The best counsel we can recieve is from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't know what God will do with my concerns, but I know He will counsel me, and I know it's wise to just listen to His instructions of comfort during the \"night seasons.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"When the times are the darkest, those are the times we should be searching for the light."}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These verses (along with 10 as we will read in a moment) is what Peter brings up at Pentecost in the book of Acts."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For David speaketh concerning him, I foresaw the Lord always before my face, for he is on my right hand, that I should not be moved: Therefore did my heart rejoice, and my tongue was glad; moreover also my flesh shall rest in hope:... ...Because thou wilt not leave my soul in hell, neither wilt thou suffer thine Holy One to see corruption. Thou hast made known to me the ways of life; thou shalt make me full of joy with thy countenance. Men and brethren, let me freely speak unto you of the patriarch David, that he is both dead and buried, and his sepulchre is with us unto this day. Therefore being a prophet, and knowing that God had sworn with an oath to him, that of the fruit of his loins, according to the flesh, he would raise up Christ to sit on his throne; He seeing this before spake of the resurrection of Christ, that his soul was not left in hell, neither his flesh did see corruption.","ref":"Acts 2:25-31"},{"kind":"para","text":"It speaks of the Lord's death and resurrection."},{"kind":"para","text":"It speaks about the Lord not forsaking the Savior, and bringing Him back to live with Him for all eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord Jesus Christ went to the grave with gladness, rejoicing, and hope."},{"kind":"para","text":"How do you die with being glad, rejoicing, and hopeful?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well because He had the Lord always before Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He couldn't be persuaded off of the course of the Lord because the Lord kept Him steadfast in the faith."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now Jesus (though He is 100% man) knew where He would be going when He died."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knew that He would be in eternity forever with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the hope and goal for every believer of God as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"His Word tells us over and over again that those that know Him and live in faith will not see Hell."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And these shall go away into everlasting punishment: but the righteous into life eternal.","ref":"Matthew 25:46"},{"kind":"para","text":"Let's go to our next verse to debate it a bit."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"title":"He Is Risen","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Paul says in Acts;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherefore he saith also in another psalm, Thou shalt not suffer thine Holy One to see corruption. For David, after he had served his own generation by the will of God, fell on sleep, and was laid unto his fathers, and saw corruption: But he, whom God raised again, saw no corruption.","ref":"Acts 13:35-37"},{"kind":"para","text":"The term \"Hell\" here means, \"The unseen place.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether that is physically Hell or not, I couldn't tell you."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is much debate about whether or not Jesus went to Hell when He died."},{"kind":"para","text":"Aside from the fact that it goes against everything else in scripture regarding the righteous man being saved, I don't think there would be any good reason for the Lord to have ever entered Hell."},{"kind":"para","text":"Over and over again Jesus talks about going to Heaven after He dies on the cross."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I came forth from the Father, and am come into the world: again, I leave the world, and go to the Father.","ref":"John 16:28"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In my Father's house are many mansions: if it were not so, I would have told you. I go to prepare a place for you. And if I go and prepare a place for you, I will come again, and receive you unto myself; that where I am, there ye may be also.","ref":"John 14:2-3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said unto Jesus, Lord, remember me when thou comest into thy kingdom. And Jesus said unto him, Verily I say unto thee, Today shalt thou be with me in paradise.","ref":"Luke 23:42-43"},{"kind":"para","text":"If Jesus was going to \"Paradise\" at that hour, and He meant to Hell, that man on the cross next to Him was in for a rude awakening."},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, The Lord is risen from the dead, and that is the part that should really be emphasized here."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have seen the Lord's ministry in verse 8, His death in verse 9, His resurrection in verse 10, and lastly His ascension in verse 11."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord sits at the Father's right hand."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who being the brightness of his glory, and the express image of his person, and upholding all things by the word of his power, when he had by himself purged our sins, sat down on the right hand of the Majesty on high;\" Hebrews 1:3 \"So then after the Lord had spoken unto them, he was received up into heaven, and sat on the right hand of God.","ref":"Mark 16:19"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Which he wrought in Christ, when he raised him from the dead, and set him at his own right hand in the heavenly places, Far above all principality, and power, and might, and dominion, and every name that is named, not only in this world, but also in that which is to come:","ref":"Ephesians 1:20-21"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore being by the right hand of God exalted, and having received of the Father the promise of the Holy Ghost, he hath shed forth this, which ye now see and hear.","ref":"Acts 2:33"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who is he that condemneth? It is Christ that died, yea rather, that is risen again, who is even at the right hand of God, who also maketh intercession for us.","ref":"Romans 8:34"},{"kind":"para","text":"I could go on, there is plenty of scripture suggesting Christ's seat."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is the fulness of our joy, and He is the pleasure of our life."},{"kind":"para","text":"I truly feel sympathy for those that have rejected the Lord, or those that have not committed to Him, because they have no idea the joys and pleasures they are missing out on."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11}]},
    "17": {"chapter":17,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last chapter, the Psalmist writes about how near the Lord is, that we are accepted by Him, that the Lord provides us with fulness and fatness, and we are guaranteed to be taken care of by Him.","In this chapter, we take a step back and ponder the Lord's presence. It seems David is in a bit of turmoil, and he is starting to second guess God's presence in the moment. Obvious God is not absent in the trials, but it might seem as if He's distant because of the hardships we face. This is a great Psalm to remember that God is very near to those that seek Him out and need Him the most. Don't worry about what the world can throw at you, just concern yourself with where the Lord is."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"A Cry For Help","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are times in our lives when we must come to this point in our faith."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must come to the Lord in tears and dire need."},{"kind":"para","text":"I find that those moments are more needful than not, because it's in those times when we come to rely on the Lord the most."},{"kind":"para","text":"Over and over again through scripture we find the children of God coming to these seasons and it's through those times that God does His greatest work."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is what is happening here with David, and he is being provided a chance and a time to pray and deeply desire God's ear to hear him."},{"kind":"para","text":"His lips are not \"feigned\" or rather they are not pleading false or nonessential words."},{"kind":"para","text":"You can fake your countenance in front of many people, but you cannot fake your true heart before the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've seen people fake their tears for others before. Even at a funeral, tears can be faked. They can play the part and seem the good, but they are nothing short of phonies looking to take something or receive something. It takes a real special person to abuse already hurt people, and those special people are around us all the time. We are not to come to the Lord in this way, because He will just cast us aside if we are faking our true need for Him."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If David has dont something wrong, the Lord has every right to make it even with David."},{"kind":"para","text":"David is saying here, \"Whatever you see fit to do with this situation Lord, you do what is right.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It take's a very STRONG person to accept the Lord's leading, especially if you are in danger of the Lord being against you for something you have perhaps done."},{"kind":"para","text":"In David's instance, he is not sure why he is faced with this issue, and desires that the Lord would make it clear if it's his own fault."},{"kind":"para","text":"My assumption is that this is around the time of Saul pursuing David."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":5,"title":"Staying the Course","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David has pled with the Lord over and over again that it would be revealed where he is at fault, and through it all he cannot seem to get a revelation of fault."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has tried him, God has proved him, he has been through the depths and back, and yet there has been no turning away from David in the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has stayed the course, and yet God is allowing him to feel trapped and cornered."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well God strengthens his people the most through times of trials."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's not the way I would want it, but it's the way we learn the fastest, and David was going to need to learn fast if he was going to be the next king..."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think that is important to realize."},{"kind":"para","text":"David wasn't thinking about the future that God had bestowed upon him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows the promise to him was to become the next king, but he didn't know what that would entail (or if (at this point) God would keep His promise seeing as his life hung in the balance)."},{"kind":"para","text":"May we remember that through times of difficulty."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is preparing us for a future situation that we don't know about."},{"kind":"para","text":"David would need to be in the right place physically and mentally, and at the moment he wasn't in either."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He hasn't followed after the things of the world, or the things of Satan."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has tried to keep the Lord front and center through this time of trial."},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps this is true."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wasn't perfect in all his ways, but he was a man desirous to follow the Lord, and he was hopeful to be used by the Lord rather than by Satan."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's easy for a Christian to know if what you are doing is induced by Satan or lead by the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"The rest of the world might be confused by it (it certainly seemed Saul had a hard time figuring out what was what) but a true child of God knows exactly what direction they are suppose to take."},{"kind":"para","text":"The confusing part to us is when the road is rocky."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are under the impression that following the path of God is suppose to be simple and straightforward, but when we are on that path, we are constantly being tripped up by our adversary (the Devil)."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is a good measure of whether or not you are on the right path, if there is a lot of pushback by evil people..."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We will slip if we don't have the power and leading of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"David knows it all too well, and there are a lot of people who have learned that the hard way (some still learning it as they trek through this life in their own power claiming to have the power of Christ and slipping at every turn)."},{"kind":"para","text":"At least people are getting back up."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are some who have fallen who have never taken the hand of the Lord to continue forward, and it's sad to see them slide down this hill of life and away from the celestial city."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is their choice though, and there is nothing I can do to stop them unless they take us down with them."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"The Center","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I have read a lot of different prayers throughout scripture that match up the persons personal needs, but I think this prayer can be linked to Christ as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ was often found in prayer (most of the time at the Mount of Olives (He seemed to really like that place)), and He understood well that God would hear Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think we have an idea of how God is listening, but we don't take prayer nearly as seriously as David does here (or as Jesus did in His ministry)."},{"kind":"para","text":"We may go to God with the big things only, but we feel He won't listen to our true needs or try and help us with our small (or what we see as small) problems."},{"kind":"para","text":"David's life was in the balance (at least it was to David), but God had already promised him the kingdom."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why couldn't he just be content with the promises of God?"},{"kind":"para","text":"His faith was truly being build as these times were coming, and I believe through these prayers God reminded him over and over again that He was there with him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've recognized it in my own prayers as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"I could in dire straights, and pray to the Lord, and God will always remind me in some way that He is there."},{"kind":"para","text":"When He reminds me, I know I am not worthy of His presence and the fact that He would pay attention to me at all."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, He wants to be there for His children and help them along."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God's lovingkindness was shown to David the moment he woke up in the morning."},{"kind":"para","text":"God shows His lovingkindness to us by the fact that we woke up in a bed (perhaps even under a roof)."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are always ways to trace God's lovingkindness even in the middle of a cave."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has been faithful to us, and God was consistently faithful to David even when David couldn't really see it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Actually, I think a good thing for every child of God to do when they have felt down or neglected is search and seek for God's lovingkindness in the day."},{"kind":"para","text":"You will find how God has provided all the time if you are looking for it."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Such a good verse."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are the apple of God's eye."},{"kind":"para","text":"All of creation is under God's care, but God's children get a special notice from Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He loves us, and centers us in His vision."},{"kind":"para","text":"He surrounds the rest of His creation to guide His utmost cared for creation (that is His children, those who have turned to Him)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that seek Him, and pray to Him and study Him are those that God would consider to be the \"Apple of His Eye.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"This phrase has been thrown around a lot in our day and age, and even the Atheists use it, but they don't know where it derives from."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, it was first mention quite a while before this in Deuteronomy!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He found him in a desert land, and in the waste howling wilderness; he led him about, he instructed him, he kept him as the apple of his eye.","ref":"Deuteronomy 32:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"God is the author of this interesting quote."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"The Apple of my eye\" simply means \"to keep a person who you are extremely proud of.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It's interesting that God uses the term \"Apple\" for this picture isn't it?"},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Apple\" means \"pupil\" in Hebrew."},{"kind":"para","text":"The \"center\" if you will."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the garden of Eden, the center of Adam and Eve's eye were placed on a fruit, but it was placed on the wrong kind."},{"kind":"para","text":"The center of God's eye is placed on His children, and He is very concerned about what happens to them and how they fair."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"title":"Inclosed By the World","entries":[{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked are those who seek the world as their center."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't care about the Lord or about what God wants."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, they would be happier if they could just put a stop to God and His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"Someday they will succeed at doing this."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will kill off God's people, and they will oppress and misuse His people, and treat them like slaves and less-thans, but God will have the final say to those wicked people."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will put them in their place, and those people will regret having neglected the Lord for so long."}]}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"title":"Satan and Man","entries":[{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The same picture is given by Peter about Satan."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"\"Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:\" 1","ref":"Peter 5:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"I think the reason that the wicked men (both then and now) are viewed as a roaring lion here is because they are used by Satan rather than God."},{"kind":"para","text":"They like the sin of Satan."},{"kind":"para","text":"They like their flesh and their own personal desires."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is why they are trying to making it as common and as accepting as possible today."},{"kind":"para","text":"They want to bend the rules and laws so that others will accept the fact that their sin is fun to them so that way they don't have to give it up."},{"kind":"para","text":"If everyone accepts their sin, they can have it freely and do it wherever they want."},{"kind":"para","text":"Abortion certainly is a hot button topic today, and it's one of those sins that is becoming more and more accepting in our country."},{"kind":"para","text":"But we can take a step further and talk about hard drugs."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our government in California is openly handing out free drugs to people on the streets telling them it's okay to do it, instead of making it harder for them to get some."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then we have the crime of allowing people to steal from stores of up to $2000, which doesn't help the crime go down by the way (I don't know how they ignore the fact that stores are closing and people are more frightened then ever to work in a public setting because of all the violence and theft, but this is why you don't trust in your government for safety)."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can talk about rape, and even murder as being more acceptable in our culture today, because they think that if they allow it and accept it, then it won't be so bad when it happens."},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth is, when we accept it, it becomes worse and even more heinous."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is a proven historical fail since the beginning of time."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sodom and Gomorrah has some examples of this..."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"title":"Losing Your Soul","entries":[{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In danger of sounding like a broken record, may I just remind you that the treasures of this world fade away and you can't take them with you in the end."},{"kind":"para","text":"The rewards that we search for and strive towards today are our rewards forever."},{"kind":"para","text":"Are they worth the fight?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Are they worth the losing of everything else because we are so focused on that one thing?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I can't think of anything in this world that is worth losing our souls over."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For what shall it profit a man, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul?","ref":"Mark 8:36"}]}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"title":"Where Satisfaction is Found","entries":[{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is faithful, and when we have Him we can rest assured in our present trouble that He will deliver us."},{"kind":"para","text":"The forecast looks bleak, but He is our ray of sunshine."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our days may seem long, but He is our rest in weariness."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people may seem terrible, but He is our stay."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don't let the circumstances or the people sway you away from seeing the lovingkindness and provision of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is there to help, guide, and protect, and it would be wise if we looked for Him in everything we do, or are worried about doing."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15}]},
    "18": {"chapter":18,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last chapter David wrote a plea for help to the Lord. He desired to try and keep in line with where God would want him, and asked that God would guide. He wanted to keep God centered in his life, and it seems that David had a hard time doing that over and over again. He is surrounded by the enticements and influences of this world, and struggled in the battle against Satan and man. He talks about what the world offers verses what God offers, and it's far more satisfying to follow after Christ than to take the treasures of this world.","This chapter is a little more lengthy than usual, but there is so much good content and strong symbolism in here that I think will be extremely beneficial to the reader. This Psalm is looked at as a prayer of David (it is) and is usually pretty closed off to nothing more than the personal feelings of David. I believe it's so much more than that, and I want to spend quite a bit of time breaking this down and refreshing our souls in reading this account."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"I Love You, Lord","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are plenty of times in scripture when God has said that He loves His creation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.","ref":"John 3:16"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.","ref":"Romans 5:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Herein is love, not that we loved God, but that he loved us, and sent his Son to be the propitiation for our sins.","ref":"1 John 4:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The LORD hath appeared of old unto me, saying, Yea, I have loved thee with an everlasting love: therefore with lovingkindness have I drawn thee.","ref":"Jeremiah 31:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And to know the love of Christ, which passeth knowledge, that ye might be filled with all the fulness of God.","ref":"Ephesians 3:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"How often to do we confess our love to Him?"},{"kind":"para","text":"David is saying something that might be somewhat foreign to us today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Do we ever say, \"Lord, I love you\"?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Do we express our love to the Lord?"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is something we should grow accustomed to."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might not say it often to our Earthly fathers, or perhaps (some of you) may not say it often to your own wives, but we should make it a habit to tell the Lord that we love Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you haven't said it in some time, make that a priority right now in this moment before we go any further."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David has put immense amount of trust and hope in the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is essentially saying that he cannot do anything without Him, and his personal strength alone is not enough to suffice."},{"kind":"para","text":"He needs the power and might of the Lord in order to prosper, and it will have to be God that gives Him the occassion to rejoice, otherwise he will have no reason to do so."},{"kind":"para","text":"I like that saying, \"He is the horn of my salvation.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"\"horn\" means \"strength.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"You could say it like, \"The Lord is the strength of my salvation.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Horn is also a musical instrument, and perhaps the Lord is the victory horn as well."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And hath raised up an horn of salvation for us in the house of his servant David;","ref":"Luke 1:69"},{"kind":"para","text":"\"buckler\" means \"shield.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"He is our protection."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was the protection of Israel, but David takes this protection onto a more PERSONAL level."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is DAVID'S shield."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is OUR shield today."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Above all, taking the shield of faith, wherewith ye shall be able to quench all the fiery darts of the wicked.","ref":"Ephesians 6:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"We can trust in Him by faith to deliver us and guide us."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When everything seems to be against us, we can trust in the Lord like David here."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can say, \"He is worthy to be praised; and He will save me from my enemies.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Our biggest enemy today is Satan."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord can deliver us from temptation and trials of various sorts."},{"kind":"para","text":"The book of James gives us a great example of how God delivers us from trials."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"Released From The Grave","entries":[{"start":4,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Just like much of the other Psalms, we can take this as a thought and connection to Christ directly."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Hell\" here means \"grave.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be something that David will use a few times."},{"kind":"para","text":"This isn't speaking about the pits of hell, but rather the nearness of death."},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, David has some personal experience with some close calls, but he was never led into the grave (I mean until his actual death that is)."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is likely a Psalm written around the time of 2 Samuel 22."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The sorrows of hell compassed me about; the snares of death prevented me;","ref":"2 Samuel 22:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ was also led to the grave, except far more physically and specifically."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ was also not left in the grave as David prophecy's here, and so it's a Psalm that can be obviously linked to the Lord by that fact alone."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":16,"title":"The Wrath of God","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is another proof that this chapter is about Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"When Christ died, there was a great Earthquake."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom; and the earth did quake, and the rocks rent;","ref":"Matthew 27:51"},{"kind":"para","text":"It says that God was \"wroth.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Wroth\" means \"furious\" or \"to become angry.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord's anger is kindled against the ungodly."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the LORD's anger was kindled the same time, and he sware, saying,","ref":"Numbers 32:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the wrath of God is revealed from heaven against all ungodliness and unrighteousness of men, who hold the truth in unrighteousness;","ref":"Romans 1:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that believeth on the Son hath everlasting life: and he that believeth not the Son shall not see life; but the wrath of God abideth on him.","ref":"John 3:36"},{"kind":"para","text":"So when Christ died, God's anger was kindled."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was angry with the wickedness of man."},{"kind":"para","text":"But His anger was also satisfied, because Christ was perfect and specifically died so that we can be connected to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's important to note that God does not turn away from punishing the wicked."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might see wickedness reign, but we can be assured that it won't last forever."},{"kind":"para","text":"Someday, every man reaps what he sows."}]},{"start":8,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He delivered David from his enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"He delivered Christ from His enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"He delivers us from our enemies of sin and flesh."},{"kind":"para","text":"All we must do is trust in Him and trust in His providence."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is faithful to \"draw us out\" of many waters."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the multitude of trials, and in the middle of His wrath, He exacts to everyone their due."},{"kind":"para","text":"He protects His children, while simultaneously giving judgement to those that are in need of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"As good parents, we want to do whatever it takes to protect our kids. We want to comfort and console them when they are being mistreated. Sometimes there is truth said about our children and we can tend to side with them even though they are in the wrong. We must not treat our children with level respect. We, however, must not treat them as evil children when there is evil happening to them. We will do whatever it takes to protect our children from evil, and we will do whatever we can to make sure they are not taken advantage of while at the same time attacking and fighting against the evil of our day."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord can do this and more."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows what is evil and what is not."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is able to protect His own, and serve vengence on those who aren't His."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is fully capable of knowing who is wrong and who is right, and we should trust His protection even when it seems that everything else is falling apart around us."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will not let evil just simply go, and He will not forsake His own children."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":24,"title":"The Sin of David","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David has a testimony of being consistently delivered from the world around him."},{"kind":"para","text":"David, by all intensive purposes I'm saying this, was continuously messing up."},{"kind":"para","text":"You would think a man after God's heart would be a little more selfless in his life."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is GOD that labels this man this."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when he had removed him, he raised up unto them David to be their king; to whom also he gave testimony, and said, I have found David the son of Jesse, a man after mine own heart, which shall fulfil all my will.","ref":"Acts 13:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"When God says it, He says it a little differently though..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But now thy kingdom shall not continue: the LORD hath sought him a man after his own heart, and the LORD hath commanded him to be captain over his people, because thou hast not kept that which the LORD commanded thee.","ref":"1 Samuel 13:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"That man turns out to be David, but I think God presented a little bit of a bigger picture than that."},{"kind":"para","text":"This David fellow would lead to a lot more than just a simple following of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It would lead to Jesus Christ, who was truly a man after God's heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason that David felt inadequate when against his enemies, was often because he was a sinful man knowing he didn't deserve the intervening of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"What made David special, however, was when he messed up, he continuously went back to the Lord to search for His forgiveness and presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"God was always there to fix him up."},{"kind":"para","text":"And while David collapsed in strength, God renewed him and gave him mercy rather than wrath."},{"kind":"para","text":"David recognized that, and that is why he is able to praise the Lord in one of the most difficult moments of his life."}]},{"start":18,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Were David's hands clean?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I could avouch to say probably not."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But the word of the LORD came to me, saying, Thou hast shed blood abundantly, and hast made great wars: thou shalt not build an house unto my name, because thou hast shed much blood upon the earth in my sight.","ref":"1 Chronicles 22:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, David's hands were clean of starting anything against anybody."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, a good portion of the beginning of his reign saw him trying to make peace with the surrounding territories, and they didn't want to accept it."},{"kind":"para","text":"But again, this is another proof as to how this chapter can be linked directly to Jesus."},{"kind":"para","text":"His hands ARE clean."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the only real innocent one in all of scripture and in the entire world since the beginning of time."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our rejection of Him makes our hands dirty, and our sin against Him makes us unclean."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded.","ref":"James 4:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, this is also personal thoughts of David, and David felt delivered through every instance."},{"kind":"para","text":"He felt the Lord lead and guide and never forsake him."},{"kind":"para","text":"God could have forsaken him, but God didn't."},{"kind":"para","text":"God always remains faithful, and how undeserving we are of it."}]},{"start":21,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, not exactly right."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't want to have to do this, but we have a pretty strong account of David's sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can start it with his marrying two women in 1 Samuel, follow it through with his marrying of multiple other women after the fact (2 Samuel), continue the journey of sleeping with a woman and killing her husband, and continue it down the line to the sin of his sons (that he arguably ignored) and counting of the people (after he was told not to do it)."},{"kind":"para","text":"One thing is for sure, God will recompense you according to your righteousness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some of us play the role of \"righteous.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are genuinely righteous, God will give us our due reward."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are not, then it's not a question of why God isn't rewarding you."},{"kind":"para","text":"God rewards His own, and He can tell when you are true to Him and when you are not."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is plenty of reason for God to pay David back in terrible convicting ways (and God certainly does in some ways), but David also remorsed over his sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is why I believe Saul was never saved."},{"kind":"para","text":"We never see Saul actually cry over his sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"We see him cry over his loss of power, but never turn from his evil ways, and never admit is faults."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have a lot of questions for a person that cannot see their own sin and still proclaims Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"Saul never admitted his sins, and he never proclaimed to know the Lord ever."},{"kind":"para","text":"David admitted to his sins on several occasions, and begged the Lord to be forgiven over and over again."}]}]},{"start":25,"end":29,"title":"The Light of the World","entries":[{"start":25,"end":27,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will exact what you have produced."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will give everyone what they deserve."},{"kind":"para","text":"Boy, if you are without Christ today, you will get what you deserve."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are in Christ today, we should be in constant consideration about what we are giving so that the Lord can give us back what we deserve."},{"kind":"para","text":"What do the righteous deserve?"},{"kind":"para","text":"God's presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"Anything above that is just extended favor."}]},{"start":28,"end":29,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I suppose all of us have had some sort of moment where we were enveloped in darkness, and God shined a light on us."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's interesting that we would be walking through this world in utter darkness not seeing everything around us, and we just call this normal."},{"kind":"para","text":"We walk and walk, until Christ flashes a light in our eyes and we are confused about what we just saw."},{"kind":"para","text":"We suddenly sit there in contemplation and acknowledgment of our sin and wandering and pray that God would help us get out of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Instead of God taking us out of the darkness, He shines a light around us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We suddenly have a little light of our own."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm sure there are candles in our home, or we have lit candles before. Perhaps we can liken it to fireworks (that seems to be all the rage in our century today). Either way, we know that there is no way to light a candle without a source of light first. If we try and light a candle with the sun, we are going to have a difficult time in the process. Even lighting it with the sun gives the sun the original source. If we take a match, or a lighter, and light the candle, we are passing on the bigger fire (the match or the lighter) onto the little fire (the candle). That is what God does for His children the moment we are saved. He passes on the big fire so we can have little fires. We are lit up for His use."},{"kind":"para","text":"There's a recognizable theme of light throughout all of scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Apostle John recognizes this and rights pretty heavily about it in the book of John."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then spake Jesus again unto them, saying, I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life.","ref":"John 8:12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another, and the blood of Jesus Christ his Son cleanseth us from all sin.","ref":"1 John 1:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"This then is the message which we have heard of him, and declare unto you, that God is light, and in him is no darkness at all.","ref":"1 John 1:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then Jesus said unto them, Yet a little while is the light with you. Walk while ye have the light, lest darkness come upon you: for he that walketh in darkness knoweth not whither he goeth.","ref":"John 12:35"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"As long as I am in the world, I am the light of the world.","ref":"John 9:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the light shineth in darkness; and the darkness comprehended it not.","ref":"John 1:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a time in the end when the light of the world will be gone from the world (that is recognized in Revelation)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moment that happens, people will be happy to walk in darkness, and those that desire to look for light will not be able to figure out how to get it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that have found the light will be slain or killed by those that desire the darkness."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world will snuff out the candles of God, but in the end God will get rid of all darkness on this entire Earth and the only thing that will be left is the light of the Lord."}]}]},{"start":30,"end":45,"title":"A Need For Revival","entries":[{"start":30,"end":30,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God's way is provenly perfect."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's not that you could just take David's word for it (though you could trust the account of David here)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather, God proves His Word to be perfect."},{"kind":"para","text":"His Word is also a reflection of Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.","ref":"John 1:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is perfect."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's Word is perfect."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is tried."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's tested."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not only so, but YOU can personally test God's Word today. Some people don't give God's Word the proper testing. They give up at the first sign of a hypocrisy or a question. Some will even give up because they simply don't understand one word or another. I could probably go toe-to-toe with the atheist in trying to prove God's Word wrong. I could say like them, \"A-ha! The Word of the Lord is incorrect here! He said this before and now He's doing this! God is a liar!\" In fact, I have been in those shoes (even as a Christian), and God proves me wrong every time. I find out somewhere else in scripture how the hypocrisy connects. I then realize it was not hypocrisy, it was fulfilment."},{"kind":"para","text":"◦ \"The best commentary to the Bible is the Bible.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"I appreciate the fact that anyone would take time to read a commentary like this and utilize it for their own understandings and needs, and I hope and pray that it is useful to help you navigate further into scripture, but your best commentary is certainly not the one you are holding. You could spend anywhere upwards to about $1,000 for a really great biblical scholarly commentary (I pray and hope this commentary never gets that high in price), and it still won't be as good as the Bible commenting on itself."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you can't find the answer to your question right away in scripture, you can guarantee the answer is further along if you are not faint to keep searching."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's Word is tried and true, and when we trust in God for our understanding, He will be our buckler when we find the answers."}]},{"start":31,"end":31,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Great questions to ask."},{"kind":"para","text":"David will answer these in a moment, but we should ask this question too."},{"kind":"para","text":"Who could we put over the Lord?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Who can we say, \"Oh, that is God, that is perfection, strength, power and might! Oh, that is what real love looks like. There is no hypocrisy in Him!\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot say that about anyone here on Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you can, you have yourself fooled my friend, and you will be sorely disappointed when they mess up."}]},{"start":32,"end":35,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When the \"right hand\" is mentioned, we can link that to Christ as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is Christ who sits at the right hand of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will make mention of this more in the future, but it's suffice to say that David uses this as a testiment to Christ once again."},{"kind":"para","text":"God gives strength, and never leads us astray."},{"kind":"para","text":"He guides our steps, and helps us to take on the battle."},{"kind":"para","text":"He provides us with salvation, and keeps us going by His right hand."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's gentleness makes us great!"},{"kind":"para","text":"What line right there."},{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn't have to be harsh with us to make us into soldiers for Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, Israel rarely became a strong army based on God's wrath."},{"kind":"para","text":"They were good at kindling God's wrath, but God's love also poured out and that is ultimately what makes the people of God stronger and more faithful."},{"kind":"para","text":"As children of God, we are not to concentrate on the wrath of God more than we concentrate on His gentleness."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is extremely gentle with us, and He makes us stronger because of it."}]},{"start":36,"end":41,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God provides the victory."},{"kind":"para","text":"The battles we face all belong to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be in full dependence on Him if we desire to see a true victory."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moment we lose sight of that is the moment we lose the fight."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even those that don't know the Lord will cry to Him at some point or another, but God will not listen to them."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have had their chance."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can read through scripture (and Lord knows we have) and say, \"God is unfair, He has allowed the death of so many people around Israel, how is that okay?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"God has allowed the death of these cities and people (you are right) but not before giving them over FOUR HUNDRED YEARS to turn to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"How much more time can the Lord give?"},{"kind":"para","text":"If they haven't turn in 400 years, they are likely to never turn."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, in 400 years things just get worse and worse."},{"kind":"para","text":"We see the fruit of that today."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have had revivals in our country like no other has ever seen before. We could trace throughout history how the Christian church has led massive amounts of campaigns to see a vase majority come to Christ. We haven't seen that in my lifetime. This hasn't happened in quite a while... ...We have sat on the heels of revival for nearly 5 decades (50 years if you are trying to figure out what that means), and have seen nothing happen except the world turn worse and worse. Will it take us 400 years to get it right? If not, how long will the Lord have to wait for us?"},{"kind":"para","text":"He CAN wait forever, but there's also some things He has to move forward with as well!"},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, we are not worth waiting for, and it's a shock to me that God would continue to wait and continue to care even though in the past 5 decades (since the last revival period) we have grown colder and colder to Him."}]},{"start":42,"end":44,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Every knee will bow to Him eventually."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether they want to or not."},{"kind":"para","text":"I imagine that there won't be many who are able to stand in that day, and they might try and force themselves to stand (out of their own arrogance and pride) in the presence of Christ, but Christ will make them bow even if He must break their legs to do so..."}]},{"start":45,"end":45,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There's nowhere to hide away from the Lord and from His authority."},{"kind":"para","text":"Try as you might, you will be found."}]}]},{"start":46,"end":50,"title":"We Are Delivered!","entries":[{"start":46,"end":46,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"An amazing statement directly linked to Christ once again."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord lives!"},{"kind":"para","text":"The tomb is empty and He has risen!"},{"kind":"para","text":"Exalt His name!"}]},{"start":47,"end":48,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The violent man could be Satan of course."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is also all those being controlled by Satan and the flesh when Christ was on the cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you read the account of the crucifixion, there were a lot of violent men there."},{"kind":"para","text":"The massive crowd chanted \"crucify him, crucify him!\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Every person in attendance sought violence."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was delivered into their hands to be abused and mistreated, but in the end He was delivered into the hands of the Lord to provide forgiveness and everlasting life!"}]},{"start":49,"end":50,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is good!"},{"kind":"para","text":"He will give deliverance to anyone that wants it today."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only reason a man may not be delivered right now will only be because he has rejected the free gift that God has provided him."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's on you and no one else."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":29},{"start":30,"end":45},{"start":46,"end":50}]},
    "19": {"chapter":19,"intro":[],"previously":["Our last chapter saw a rollercoaster of emotions from David. He started with how much he loves the Lord, drawing to his salvation from death itself, spiralling into God's wrath (particularly at the sins of the world and the people), viewing the sin of a simple man (namely David), recognizing God's light in this world, desiring and praying for a revival in the land, and then proclaiming a deliverance from the Lord.","Chapter 19 is my favorite Psalm. I desire to do this one justice (I desire that for all the notes I take), so I am going to spend a good portion of time in expounding on these verses. This Psalm is fruitful to those that take their time in it and really meditate on it. I think it's a great Psalm to put to memory if we are willing and able."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":6,"title":"The Boundless Creation","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When it comes to proving God, we don't have to look far for proof."},{"kind":"para","text":"The sky and the stars are proof of a divine creator."},{"kind":"para","text":"The sun, and the moon, and all the planets give reverence to a perfect creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"You have to be on some level of crazy to suspect that everything just exists so perfectly in our solar system by some sort of cosmic accident."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, there are plenty of people today who are under the impression that creation just kind of happened, and everything is perfect because of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"How can you look at the sky and think anything less than of a creator?"},{"kind":"para","text":"How can you see the birds and the the trees and think that it all appears by accident?"},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems crazy to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has proven Himself, and it's a bit silly to think that all of these perfect things (too many to even count) just happened to be hear by accident."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Even the day and night cycles prove a creator."},{"kind":"para","text":"Think about it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Day always comes at the expected time."},{"kind":"para","text":"Night always arrives when the sun goes down."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moon and the sun are in constant rotation, and we have all grown to expect the sun to come up every single day."},{"kind":"para","text":"It would be quite a strange thing to see the sun stay in the sky or never appear again."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the fourth angel sounded, and the third part of the sun was smitten, and the third part of the moon, and the third part of the stars; so as the third part of them was darkened, and the day shone not for a third part of it, and the night likewise.","ref":"Revelation 8:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine this for a second."},{"kind":"para","text":"A third of the day is gone, and a third of the night."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we put that into 12 hours (sunlight) and 12 hours (nighttime) we get 8 hour days."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our days will be so short in that time that you wouldn't even be able to work a full shift before it was time to sleep."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will throw everyone's calendars off."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet they will still find ways of complaining about and rejecting the Lord."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is an interesting note that David is making here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every language understands the dialect of the sun and moon."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no language on Earth who can deny the existence of the sun and moon, and we all keep track of time by them."},{"kind":"para","text":"This would stand to reason that every language should be thinking about the creator of those two things."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even in a tyrannical country where they are not allowed to think about the Lord, the proof of His existence all around them should be enough for them to understand something is out there."}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Sun is powerful."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have likened the moon as an example for us."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm sure I've already said it before, and I will probably say it again, but it certainly bears repeating."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Sun gives off the light (or the SON rather), and the moon reflects that light."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are like the moon, we will reflect the light."},{"kind":"para","text":"The sun itself proves a God in Heaven."},{"kind":"para","text":"How has nobody ever wondered why for thousands of years (or in some people's beliefs MILLIONS of years) we have not been caught on fire?"},{"kind":"para","text":"That doesn't seem strange to anyone else?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Judging by these verses, I assume David is writing this Psalm during the night time."},{"kind":"para","text":"He's sitting outside looking up at the stars and anticipating the sun."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is something that we should all take the time to do."},{"kind":"para","text":"I know there are a lot of people who live in city areas. I live in a smaller rural city in California called Lancaster. It's in the desert, and there are a lot of draw backs living out here. Though it's growing, there are still plenty of spots to drive or stop at to just sit and stare at the stars. I sometimes go to these places just to watch the sky and it's fascinating. There's no light pollution to get in the way and often you can see the moon as bright as day. Actually, sometimes the moon will be so bright that you can walk around at night in the desert and see perfectly fine."},{"kind":"para","text":"If there's a way to sit and stare at the creation of God at night, I highly recommend taking some time to do it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Watching the night sky got David thinking about the majesty of God, and I am sure it will get us thinking about it as well."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Where do you suppose the end of heaven is?"},{"kind":"para","text":"When is the circuit of the sky complete?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Now there are people today (God bless their souls) who believe that the Earth is flat."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even though we have plenty of scientific evidence that it's not, and even though they can test their own hypothesis with their own camera equipment at home, they still have reason to believe it's flat."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even if it is, where does the sky end?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Does it perhaps end on the other side of the Earth?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Does it end with our galaxy?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Does it end with the planets and stars?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The universe is infinite, and therefore when David writes this thought here, he is implying that the Lord is infinite."},{"kind":"para","text":"Just as sure as the sun and moon come and go, the Lord stays consistent."},{"kind":"para","text":"If there is a consistent thing in our universe today, I don't see how it would be a stretch to believe that our God is the sustainer of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"You might think to yourself, \"Well what else is consistent? Certainly not humans, or live in general.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"This is right."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are often not found consistent."},{"kind":"para","text":"This means we must find consistence in things that never die."},{"kind":"para","text":"All things die as we see, and that's the cruel and sad reality of sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"But there are some things that don't die that we can BANK on continuously being consistent."},{"kind":"para","text":"One is Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"You may or may not believe Him, but whether you do or not, He will continously be consistent."},{"kind":"para","text":"Another is the love of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether you are saved today or not, God's love is poured out on humanity (and this is proven over and over again throughout history)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The one (I believe) is the best consistency we have is God's Word."},{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a time in the end where everyone will hate the Lord, and hate His word, and yet it will remain consistent."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Verily I say unto you, This generation shall not pass, till all these things be fulfilled. Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away.","ref":"Matthew 24:34-35"},{"kind":"para","text":"Though the entire Earth will be against the Lord, His Word will remain consistent."},{"kind":"para","text":"Though the entire Earth tries to destroy His Word, it will continue to remain consistent."},{"kind":"para","text":"The crazy part of this (to me) is that people have tried to destroy God's Word for years on end now."},{"kind":"para","text":"Since the beginning of time, Satan has been hard at work to get rid of God's Word, and he has not become even remotely successful."},{"kind":"para","text":"He might produce bad translations, but God's Word still stands today, and it will stand even in eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we die, we STILL won't be done with God's Word."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe there is still reason to study scripture in Heaven."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe there will be a place for studying and learning from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe the Lord's ministry and example here on Earth didn't stop at His ascension."},{"kind":"para","text":"We may know nearly everything in eternity, but there is still room to seek the Lord even in Heaven."},{"kind":"para","text":"God and His Word will always stay consistent because there is no end to Him."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":13,"title":"The Purpose of God's Intercession","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God's Word (being consistent) is also perfect!"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is the only word that can transform lives, and it's the only word that can be tested and proved as absolutely, 100%, sure."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, I've mentioned in the past that I've been called a \"simple\" man."},{"kind":"para","text":"I didn't much like that term when it was first told to me, but I've learned to appreciate it now."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well there are too many people who try and complicate things."},{"kind":"para","text":"If I can make things simple for people and their understanding, that is what I want to do."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't want them to shy away from scripture or a problem because it seems to difficult for them to understand."},{"kind":"para","text":"I want them to embrace the problem and find solutions in a simple means."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we do this with God's Word (not over complicating it when we don't have to) then we find that God brings Wisdom."},{"kind":"para","text":"His WORD makes a simple man (like myself) into something wise!"},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm not an intellectual by any means, but I have seen God use my simple thoughts from His Word to change the hearts of so many around me."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is not in my words, but in HIS Word that these lives are changed and made wise."},{"kind":"para","text":"It still astounds me that God can use my simple to expound His wisdom."},{"kind":"para","text":"But this is because we can rest assured that God's Word is perfect and consistent."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We have a breaking down of God's Word and applicability."},{"kind":"para","text":"What is God's law for?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Converting the soul."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why does God have a testimony?"},{"kind":"para","text":"To prove His wisdom."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Statutes\" means \"mandate\" or \"precepts.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason that God desires what He desires, and why He does what He does."},{"kind":"para","text":"So what are His statutes for?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Rejoicing the heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Commandment\" here is (of course) a dictation to do something, but it is better translated as \"the code of wisdom.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"I quite like that."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is not just \"the law\" in the same sense as we've already studied."},{"kind":"para","text":"God gives commands outside of the law, that should be well understood."},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe better said is that God commands ALONGSIDE the law."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is not going to command something that goes against His law, but He commands things that we should follow not because law dictates, but because God's love dictates."},{"kind":"para","text":"For instance, loving your neighbor as yourself."},{"kind":"para","text":"The law dictates we should follow that, but it's also God's command."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can either follow this command because we HAVE to (obligated by the law) or (as Jesus wants it) we can follow it because it's commanded by Him and we GET to."},{"kind":"para","text":"He also commands us to preach, and teach, and baptize."},{"kind":"para","text":"He commands us to pray, and grow, and study."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a plethora of other commands I could go through, but you can recognize that these commands (preaching, teaching, baptizing, etc.) are not given based on the law specifically."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are directed with the law, but they are not commanded by it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather, they are commanded through God with the intent that we would do it from the heart, not from the law."},{"kind":"para","text":"And why does God command us?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because it enlightens our eyes!"}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Fear is something that a lot of nonbelievers get hung up on."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some new believers get worried about this thought as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"When scripture uses the term \"fear\" as in \"fear the Lord\" it is speaking primarily about having an \"awe\" of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Being enamored by God's Work and doing."},{"kind":"para","text":"David makes it clear, here, that fearing the Lord is \"clean\" or (rather) a \"good\" thing."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why is fearing God a good thing?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because He endures forever!"},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Enduring\" means \"to stand\" or \"to remain.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"God will always exist, and He will always be faithful."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is a good reason to fear the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then we have the occassion of \"judgment.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"This is another word that a lot of people get hung up on."},{"kind":"para","text":"Judgement (in our world today) is not something that people want."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't want it, because they know that if they get judged, there WILL be found a flaw in them."},{"kind":"para","text":"People don't like it when their flaws are pointed out."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, over and over again we see righteous men of scripture not just \"talk\" about judgement, but they actually \"DESIRE\" judgement."},{"kind":"para","text":"They even REQUEST it!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The king's strength also loveth judgment; thou dost establish equity, thou executest judgment and righteousness in Jacob.","ref":"Psalm 99:4"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And all Israel heard of the judgment which the king had judged; and they feared the king: for they saw that the wisdom of God was in him, to do judgment.\" 1 Kings 3:28 \"And Samuel judged Israel all the days of his life. And he went from year to year in circuit to Bethel, and Gilgal, and Mizpeh, and judged Israel in all those places. And his return was to Ramah; for there was his house; and there he judged Israel; and there he built an altar unto the LORD.","ref":"1 Samuel 7:15-17"},{"kind":"para","text":"The book of Judges is another great picture of their desire and necessity of judgment."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God shall bring every work into judgment, with every secret thing, whether it be good, or whether it be evil.","ref":"Ecclesiates 12:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"God's Word will also judge us!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that rejecteth me, and receiveth not my words, hath one that judgeth him: the word that I have spoken, the same shall judge him in the last day.","ref":"John 12:48"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Judge me, O LORD my God, according to thy righteousness; and let them not rejoice over me.","ref":"Psalm 35:24"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He shall judge thy people with righteousness, and thy poor with judgment.","ref":"Psalm 72:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"I think we get the picture."},{"kind":"para","text":"Judgment isn't just about laying guilt on you to make you feel bad."},{"kind":"para","text":"Judgment is necessary to receive change."},{"kind":"para","text":"When our judgment is faulty (which it usually is) we will not change into proper and righteous people."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is why we must have the right standard of judgment."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our judgment is flawed."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's judgment is PERFECT."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why do we need His judgment?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because all of it is true and righteous."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are not judged of the Lord, we will not have truth or righteousness."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world shy's away from judgment, but Christians (as David will prove in a moment) should desire God's judgment."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well let's look at our next verses."}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God's judgments are valuable."},{"kind":"para","text":"They hold weight."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we are judged by our fellow man, we won't find much value in their judgment."},{"kind":"para","text":"I love the Living Waters ministry (and I do have a prayer for them) but often when they witness to people they come off as quite judgmental. I say this out of love for their ministry (because witnessing to people in judgment is better than not witnessing at all)... ...I believe there are people who certainly need that kind of conversation and judgment (and these are judgments by the standard of the Lord), and there are people who need a little push from the stance of love and accountability. It's one thing to judge them and then turn away from them, and another thing to give them the proper judgment and continue to nurture them. The one thing I don't agree with in Ray's method (and this is just my judgment) is that he lets these people go without a chance to further the conversation. I believe these people need a disciple, not just a judge. Perhaps he invites them to his church after, I don't know (he doesn't record that part), but there needs to be more than just telling them their faults and walking away."},{"kind":"para","text":"When Ray judges, it seems as if it's just your fellow man judging you and telling you your faults."},{"kind":"para","text":"But when we seek the LORDS judgment we find value and treasure in it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Interestingly enough, David calls God's judgment \"sweeter than honey straight from the comb.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Man's judgment is cheap."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's judgment is more valuable than the finest gold."},{"kind":"para","text":"Man's judgment is bitter."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's judgment is sweet."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we keep the commands of the Lord (again this is not just His law, but His commands altogether) and we accept His judgment, we will be rewarded with a lasting change."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of people who claim that no one can actually change."},{"kind":"para","text":"They just fake their new life."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is not true."},{"kind":"para","text":"I didn't want a new life in Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"I wasn't seeking it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ still found me, and I thank the Lord that He did."},{"kind":"para","text":"I didn't have any addictions, or ailments that I was leaning on the Lord to crutch me."},{"kind":"para","text":"I didn't have any reason to come to Christ other than He found me and changed me."},{"kind":"para","text":"I understood and realized (outside of judgment) that I was in need of a Savior."},{"kind":"para","text":"My brother had placed judgment on me (in a Ray Comfort method) and it went over my head."},{"kind":"para","text":"I simply agreed with my brother but it didn't make sense to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps I was agree more because I just wanted the conversation to be over rather than actually accepting the truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't really know."},{"kind":"para","text":"But in the end, when a man came to me and told me about what the Lord had done for me (without me even needing to confess my sins mind you (he didn't bring up the law once when talking to me about it)), I finally understood that there was nothing keeping me from taking Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"At that moment, my life changed, and I didn't even know I wanted it to change."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am not the man I use to be."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am not the man I would have been either if I didn't have Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"I praise the Lord that He changed me without my knowledge of necessity, and I pray that He do the same for others as well who seek after His judgment."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we have His judgment, we have a great warning, and a great reward."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":14,"title":"Am I The Problem?","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David was constantly requesting that the Lord bring up anything that he is doing wrong."},{"kind":"para","text":"David didn't want to be too careful about this."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wanted God to show him his errors."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should want the same."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we seek the Lord for judgment it is so we can become a better man."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we seek judgment from the world, we will change with the world (which is spiralling rather quickly if you haven't noticed)."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we seek judgment from the Lord, we change into what He wants us to be."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God.","ref":"Romans 12:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"\"Behold, I shew you a mystery; We shall not all sleep, but we shall all be changed, In a moment, in the twinkling of an eye, at the last trump: for the trumpet shall sound, and the dead shall be raised incorruptible, and we shall be changed.\" 1","ref":"Corinthians 15:51-52"},{"kind":"para","text":"We can experiencing change here on Earth as we trek through this dwindling life."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe it's important to search for change today."},{"kind":"para","text":"We won't come into FULL change until eternity, but we should be nearing change every day that we get closer to eternity."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"As David looks into the sky he doesn't just look at the astounding creation of God (if it isn't obvious enough)."},{"kind":"para","text":"David looks at how little he is in the grand scheme of things, and so he prays to the Lord who pays attention to the little things."},{"kind":"para","text":"He points out the fact that God recognizes DAVID out of all the vast expanse of the universe."},{"kind":"para","text":"He recognizes you today who are sitting and reading this."},{"kind":"para","text":"He see's your hurt, and He see's your needs."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants you to enjoy His law, His testimony, His statutes, His commandments, His fear, and His judgments."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"So you can just change and be a better person in this world?"},{"kind":"para","text":"So you can leave this world in better shape than when you arrived?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord knows that this world will not get better in time, even if you made the strongest impact."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather, the reason He wants you to enjoy these things is so you can enjoy His presence!"},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants you to be connected to Him, and when we are living in our sins, and we are clammed up to our own virtues and judgments, and we are rejectful of His perfection, we are disconnected from the only source of true power, love, and grace that can ever exist."},{"kind":"para","text":"You will not find love, nor power, nor grace, nor perfection, nor direction, nor testimony, nor law, nor statutes, nor commands, nor judgments on this Earth that are worth any value to you."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world might have tricked you into believing their opinion is the most valuable, but I promise you (in the light of the view of the universe) their opinion is small and not fit to grab your attention."},{"kind":"para","text":"Seek the Lord's judgment, and you will BE seen and valued."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a great close to this chapter of Psalm."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should all have this prayer in mind."},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't want anything that comes out of our mouth to be resentful or anti-biblical."},{"kind":"para","text":"We want the things we do, and the things we think to be acceptable to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Notice the way David says it, \"...the words of my mouth...\" insinuates His actions."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is what people will see and hear."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants what he says and does to be acceptable to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"...the meditation of my heart...\" these are the inward thoughts and motives."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants his own desires to be acceptable to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because God is his strength, and his redeemer, and without the Lord David will lead his people astray."},{"kind":"para","text":"If only our leadership today would take this psalm to heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe this Psalm should be an inspiration to every leader in every place."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should seek God's perfect law and judgment and desire to be pleasing in every approach we take."},{"kind":"para","text":"Was David perfect as a leader?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Absolutely not."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact (as we've looked at through 2 Samuel specifically) David made a lot of very terrible mistakes."},{"kind":"para","text":"What sets him apart from our bad leaders today (however) is the fact that he went to the Lord and begged for forgiveness."},{"kind":"para","text":"He fessed up to his problems and owned his mistakes."},{"kind":"para","text":"He didn't continue to try and hide them, he would just admit his faults and request a refilling of God's grace."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's what a good leader should do."},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't want a leader that doesn't make mistakes (that is impossible until the Lord is dwelling with us in judgment in the end)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now we want a leader that will admit his mistakes, confess his mistakes, seek the Lord for judgment, and allow the Lord to correct course."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how the nations have prospered in the past, and that is the only way a nation will prosper today."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how cities prospered in the past, and that is the only way a city will prosper today."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how churches prospered in the past, and that is the only way churches will prosper today."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how homes prospered in the past, and that is the only way homes will prosper today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Leaders (no matter what level of leadership you are in) must seek the Lord's judgment in a matter, rather than just bashing through their leadership with their own ideas, and rejecting correction."},{"kind":"para","text":"A good many churches and homes (and nations even) today are in turmoil because they are not mindful of the Lords judgment."},{"kind":"para","text":"If only we had a heart like David is here to receive His judgment and own up to our flaws..."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":13},{"start":12,"end":14}]},
    "20": {"chapter":20,"intro":[],"previously":["Our last chapter saw the boundlessness of God's creation, the purpose for God's intercession, and addressing what the true problem of the universe really is. The Lord is good, and the last chapter gives us a very in depth description of His goodness.","This chapter see's a hope and prayer of salvation. This is a gospel Psalm. It's a Psalm of deliverance from the Lord, and a desire for God to save His people. I think it's a great one to use for the Old Testament stiffs (those that try and disconnect the Old Testament from the New, or those that only stick to Old Testament and think that the New Testament is corrupt)."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"A Prayer to Christ","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, when we read Psalms like this, we can instantly connect and identify that it's a prayer."},{"kind":"para","text":"David is lifting up his desires to the Lord, and one of the things that he prays for (quite a bit) is deliverance and safety."},{"kind":"para","text":"He says, \"...in the day of trouble...\" He wants the God of Jacob (or Israel) to defend it's people."},{"kind":"para","text":"Which day is not a troublesome day?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Our last chapter saw a lot of lifting in the name of the Lord, but even during the seasons of praise there is no doubt trouble all around."},{"kind":"para","text":"But the days of trouble are the days of our leniency upon the Lord, and that is really where the Lord likes us to be."},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps many troubles are allowed for that simple fact alone."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Zion was a chosen place to David."},{"kind":"para","text":"He truly believed that God's throne sat there."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think he was right to choose this place for worshipping the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"There was no place like it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't look like much today, but it was certainly a grandeur place in David's time."},{"kind":"para","text":"David really built it up."},{"kind":"para","text":"Think about it;"},{"kind":"para","text":"Before David came and built his house there, it was a desolate place with not much happening for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"He builds his house, builds the city, and the remains of it are still present with us today."},{"kind":"para","text":"What other nation (great or small) can still showcase this?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Romans?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Babylonians?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Egyptians?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps the Egyptians are about as far as it comes to the most ancient examples of continuation."},{"kind":"para","text":"The pyramids are not much to look at, but they are a very important reminder that Egypt had power at some point or another."},{"kind":"para","text":"This prayer is likely a prayer for the Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's about sending His salvation to the people."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the greatest prayer we can make today."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is why I believe we are talking about Christ here."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's not talking about remembering all OUR offerings."},{"kind":"para","text":"David says, \"Remember all thy offerings...\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ makes the true and lasting offerings that we cannot."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is where God's eyes should be fixed too."},{"kind":"para","text":"If He is fixed on our offerings alone, we will have utterly failed."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our offerings cannot even compare to the Lord's, and when we try and compare them, we learn quite quickly that we fall widely short of anything worthy."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is why Christ had to come and offer Himself."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is the only offering that is sufficient."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":9,"title":"Save, Lord","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, not according to OUR heart, but according to the Lord's heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"What does the Lord want for His creation more than anything else?"},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to provide salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants a relationship with us!"},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well I don't really know."},{"kind":"para","text":"He loves us, even though we are terrible towards Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the true essence of this prayer."},{"kind":"para","text":"Really what David says is, \"Lord, do what YOUR heart wants, because OUR hearts are wicked...\""},{"kind":"para","text":"5 We will rejoice in thy salvation, and in the name of our God we will set up our banners: the Lord fulfil all thy petitions."},{"kind":"para","text":"When God has His way, He gives the world salvation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.","ref":"John 3:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"The important thing to note in this verse is \"...so loved the world that...\""},{"kind":"para","text":"God loved the world, so much, that He gives His Son for us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have a reason to rejoice when we come to know and accept this love and gift."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is God's offering."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's His Son, which leads the believer to salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"If God has His way, His way is to salvation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"\"The Lord is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.\" 2","ref":"Peter 3:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"6 Now know I that the Lord saveth his anointed; he will hear him from his holy heaven with the saving strength of his right hand."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is the Lord's saving strength."},{"kind":"para","text":"It would do us well to consider it, and remember it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, we have a mediator (which is Christ) to request our \"petitions\" (like David says here)."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is before the Lord continually on our behalf."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For there is one God, and one mediator between God and men, the man Christ Jesus;","ref":"1 Timothy 2:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no earthly authority that can do this for you."},{"kind":"para","text":"No one here, on Earth, can speak to the Lord on your behalf."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a failed attempt if they try."},{"kind":"para","text":"It must be YOU, who personally goes to Him, and it must be CHRIST who personally mediates for you."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you don't know Christ, you cannot speak to the Father."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is necessary for a conversation with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are trying to access His throne in some other way, we will be wasting our times and efforts."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no other way."},{"kind":"para","text":"David continues..."},{"kind":"para","text":"7 Some trust in chariots, and some in horses: but we will remember the name of the Lord our God."},{"kind":"para","text":"What are you trusting today?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I think there are a lot of Christians who are trusting in the seen."},{"kind":"para","text":"They trust in what they can grasp and touch."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christians are not called to put their trust in chariots or horses."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are called to put their trust in the Lord alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't use animals (anymore) to cleanse our sins, because we have the Lamb that was slain for us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Saying with a loud voice, Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing.","ref":"Revelation 5:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't use might to cleanse our sins (or any personal works) because our works are not worthy of it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But we are all as an unclean thing, and all our righteousnesses are as filthy rags; and we all do fade as a leaf; and our iniquities, like the wind, have taken us away.","ref":"Isaiah 64:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't use confession to the church to cleanse our sins because there is no earthly authority that can cleanse us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.","ref":"1 John 1:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"We must go STRAIGHT to Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must have our trust in Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we confess our sins to Him, we are saying, \"Lord I am evil, and I have done wrong, but you are good, and you can forgive sin and turn me around.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what true confession is."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's not an, \"I hope the Lord forgives me.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It's an, \"I know the Lord forgives me, because He sent His Son to die for me on the cross!\""},{"kind":"para","text":"If there are Christians who sin without conviction, they are likely not Christians at all."},{"kind":"para","text":"Possibly self-professed Christians, but they certainly don't trust in the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are the ones that trust in \"Chariots and horses...\" or (rather) the physical authorities."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christians who know Christ don't trust in what they can physically see, they trust in what they spiritually KNOW."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is faithful to forgive."},{"kind":"para","text":"8 They are brought down and fallen: but we are risen, and stand upright."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that trust in the seen will be brought down but those things."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those things won't last for eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will eventually let you down."},{"kind":"para","text":"Your strength will let you down."},{"kind":"para","text":"Your thoughts will let you down."},{"kind":"para","text":"Your works will let you down."},{"kind":"para","text":"Your family will let you down."},{"kind":"para","text":"Your friends will let you down."},{"kind":"para","text":"Your circumstance will let you down."},{"kind":"para","text":"Your money will let you down."},{"kind":"para","text":"Your religion will let you down."},{"kind":"para","text":"Your materials will let you down."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is nothing in this world that will keep you going."},{"kind":"para","text":"David says, \"Those that trust in the Lord, they are the ones that are risen and are able to stand straight.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"If you want a collapse, trust in the seen."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you want stability, trust in the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"9 Save, Lord: let the king hear us when we call."},{"kind":"para","text":"What a verse!"},{"kind":"para","text":"Save, Lord!"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the anthem of the Christian."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should desire that everyone would be saved by the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't know a great many things, but here's what I know;"},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ came and lived a perfect life."},{"kind":"para","text":"He died on the cross by people who hated his ministry and teachings (little did they know this was intentional)."},{"kind":"para","text":"He rose again the third day (completing prophecies of Old Testament, and proving His teaching was legitimate)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Because of this, He has died and resurrected for the whole world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now the tricky part is who is actually going to be saved."},{"kind":"para","text":"Actually, I shouldn't call it \"tricky\" because it really isn't."},{"kind":"para","text":"Though Christ died for the whole world, not everyone will be saved."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well it's because they have to accept His death and resurrection to recieve that gift of salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"For instance, if there was a war that breaks out, and there was a large battle that takes place with all of the people around you, and people were dying left and right, you would be pretty frightened. You would probably look for the strongest and most skill man for the battle to stay behind because he is most victorious. He gets you through the whole mess and you have reason to rejoice! Your choice was placed on following the savior in that battle. He was saving people by putting his own life on the line to get you through it. That is what Christ did."},{"kind":"para","text":"He took the blow on your behalf, and it is up to us to make the conscience decision to follow Him and stay behind Him through the battle. He is our victor, and He is our salvation. Those that don't follow Him will die in battle because He is the only one that will make it through."},{"kind":"para","text":"You know why people stopped trusting in Saul half-way through his kingship?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because he became prideful and arrogant, and the people couldn't trust him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was strong, but his strength took him further away from the Lord, not closer."},{"kind":"para","text":"People trusted David all the way through, because David learned to keep his strength in check and to heavily rely on the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He made his mistakes, but in the end the people were proud of their king because he looked out for them and saved them."},{"kind":"para","text":"David saved the Israelites time and time again."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ saved the world, once, forever, and all we have to is trust in that to be accepted into the kingdom."},{"kind":"para","text":"After we come to know Him, our response should be the same as David."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Save, Lord!\""}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":9}]},
    "21": {"chapter":21,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last chapter our Psalmist gave us a prayer to Christ, and the desire for the Lord to save His children. He desperately wanted the Lord's mercy and hand upon the Earth to keep His children going and to give them a reason to rejoice.","In this chapter, we will see how God's salvation looks and works. God has saved, and God WILL save. We will have that assurance throughout all of scripture, and for the rest of eternity as we walk with the Lord in our own lives."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"The Lords Salvation","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"A common theme in the book of Psalms is of the Psalmist's being rescued by the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"You will see the word \"salvation\" thrown around a lot because the Lord has been faithful (since the beginning of time) to save."},{"kind":"para","text":"That literally IS the Bible's story."},{"kind":"para","text":"From Genesis to Revelation, the theme is the salvation of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Salvation\" means \"deliverance\" or \"something saved.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The king rejoices because of the Lord's salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is given strength from it."},{"kind":"para","text":"WE are given strength from the Lord's salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are so many people today who try and rob the children of God of their strength, but the Lord continuously provides strength to His own."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world may try and throw things your way to get you sidetracked from the value the Lord has in you, but God is so much bigger and mightier than anything anyone else can bring your way."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot in this world who try and rob the Lord of His salvation as well (either by denying Christ, or rejecting scripture), and this Psalm is a great tool too prove them wrong."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord has given the king his hearts desire, but the desire of the heart is often sinful and foolish."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, what is being referenced here, has more to do with something that aligns with the Lord's will, and I would assume it has to do with a victorious battle."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever it might have been at this particular time frame, I can't say."},{"kind":"para","text":"But we can link this into any part of scripture (whether the victories of Israel, or the victories of the Apostles) and it would be sufficient to say that the Lord has given us what is GOOD."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might not always think that what the Lord has given is \"good\" but you can bet any money that it is perfect for our needs."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":13,"title":"God Triumphs","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now, let's get down to who the king is."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are going to look at these verses and think \"Well, obviously, the writer of this psalm is speaking about David. This is the era of David obviously, so who else could he be writing about?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"While I think it's sufficient to look at this Psalm in that way, I also find that it matches BETTER with Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is blessed with goodness."},{"kind":"para","text":"There was nothing evil or sinful in Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can know that for a fact and for certainty."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For even hereunto were ye called: because Christ also suffered for us, leaving us an example, that ye should follow his steps: Who did no sin, neither was guile found in his mouth: Who, when he was reviled, reviled not again; when he suffered, he threatened not; but committed himself to him that judgeth righteously: Who his own self bare our sins in his own body on the tree, that we, being dead to sins, should live unto righteousness: by whose stripes ye were healed.","ref":"1 Peter 2:21-24"},{"kind":"para","text":"Now we read this and say, \"Well yeah, that's Peter. He's a New Testament guy. Of course he acclaims this. Give me Old Testament proof.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm glad you asked."},{"kind":"para","text":"Peter is actually quoting from Isaiah here."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But he was wounded for our transgressions, he was bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace was upon him; and with his stripes we are healed.","ref":"Isaiah 53:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"There was no sin in him, and yet he was beaten and killed for it just like the prophet promises."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore we read that this king is crowned with \"pure\" gold."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our Lord was crowned with thorns."},{"kind":"para","text":"But His death was by design you see."},{"kind":"para","text":"He died on the cross to recieve a crown of gold, and to give all of those who are followers of Him crowns as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is the High Priest."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the High King."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the only one worth of a \"crown of gold.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"All other kings pale in comparison."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ died, I don't think anyone would dispute this."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even Atheists believe that part."},{"kind":"para","text":"But Christ ALSO rose again from the dead."},{"kind":"para","text":"He came back to life."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's what most people can't seem to agree on."},{"kind":"para","text":"The evidence is clear, and there will be time to talk about this especially in the gospels, but Christ is the one who has life from the Father, and lives for ever and ever."},{"kind":"para","text":"God gives ALL of His children life forever!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Verily, verily, I say unto you, If a man keep my saying, he shall never see death.","ref":"John 8:51"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.","ref":"Romans 6:23"},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Eternal\" means it does not end."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's \"everlasting.\""},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.","ref":"John 3:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"God is eternal, so when we know the Lord, and we are saved by Him (as even the psalmist says) we have a home with Him in His eternal home."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord (Jesus Christ) is the reason for our home there."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Psalmist makes that clear in the next verse."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is received into glory, and His salvation is evident in the lives of those that trust in Him today."},{"kind":"para","text":"People say, \"People don't change.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"They are right."},{"kind":"para","text":"They can't change."},{"kind":"para","text":"They can't change because they are solidified in their sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"When you live a life of sin, there is nothing you can do to get out of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"You are stuck there."},{"kind":"para","text":"But Christ gives you freedom from that sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"While YOU can't do anything to free yourself, Christ can set you free by His sacrifice."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moment we place our trust in the promised Messiah, is the moment we are let go of sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what salvation is."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what every time the word \"salvation\" is mentioned in scripture is talking about."},{"kind":"para","text":"David knew it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Abraham knew it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Moses knew it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Solomon knew it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even Jonah knew it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Salvation belongs to Christ, and it is on HIM that Honor and Majesty has been laid upon."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now unto the King eternal, immortal, invisible, the only wise God, be honour and glory for ever and ever. Amen.","ref":"1 Timothy 1:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"To the only wise God our Saviour, be glory and majesty, dominion and power, both now and ever. Amen.","ref":"Jude 1:25"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For we have not followed cunningly devised fables, when we made known unto you the power and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but were eyewitnesses of his majesty.","ref":"2 Peter 1:16"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ brings a smile to the Lords face."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yes, Christ is God's Son, but He is also GOD in the flesh."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our Heavenly Father didn't just send His Son to die for our sins, He sent Himself, and HE (personally) felt the pain of the cross on our behalf."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord loves His children, and made a way to give us salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only person that has \"pleased\" the Lord in everything He has done is Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world has fully gone against the Lord in nearly everything they do (including the religionists today), but the Lord can complete and and accomplish His law on His own."},{"kind":"para","text":"See the law was to show us how little we are compared to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"The law was supposed to lead us to His salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"So many have missed that today, and still miss it knowing what Jesus has done for them."},{"kind":"para","text":"They think it has to be Jesus+Law, when really the equation is \"Jesus+Faith.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Religion says \"Do.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus says, \"Done.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is glad for the work that is finished."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Guess who sits on the throne today?"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is not David."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is not any of the great and mighty kings of the past."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is worthy to sit there, and it's only the God's mercy that He is sitting there today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine if God decided not to bring Christ back from the dead."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what the Atheists hope for today."},{"kind":"para","text":"They hope that Christ was not brought back to life (because then they would be wrong)."},{"kind":"para","text":"But they fail to realize that if He was not brought back to life, that is a doomed destiny for the entire world."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might as well quit while we are ahead."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is nothing more than can be done except to recieve God's wrath."},{"kind":"para","text":"Thankfully, we are assured that the Lord has risen again, and we have salvation and eternity because of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"He currently sits on the throne, and He currently intercedes for every believer today."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Where is Christ seated?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well, it's on the right hand of God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who is gone into heaven, and is on the right hand of God; angels and authorities and powers being made subject unto him.","ref":"1 Peter 3:22"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Him hath God exalted with his right hand to be a Prince and a Saviour, for to give repentance to Israel, and forgiveness of sins.","ref":"Acts 5:31"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore being by the right hand of God exalted, and having received of the Father the promise of the Holy Ghost, he hath shed forth this, which ye now see and hear.\" Acts 2:33 \"Hereafter shall the Son of man sit on the right hand of the power of God.","ref":"Luke 22:69"},{"kind":"para","text":"Now there will be plenty of time to speak about the importance of God's right hand in later books, but it is evident that it has been (and is currently) reserved for our Lord Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ knows who is for the Lord, and who hates the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows how to save and how to reject."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be Christ who we come in contact with in judgement."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be Him who says, \"Well done\" or \"Depart from me.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It is not lost on the Lord who is saved and who is not."},{"kind":"para","text":"He can see it all and He can determine the outcome before we even know it will come to pass."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord will have His time in judgement (no doubt) when everything comes to an end."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord knows how to take care of those that are His."},{"kind":"para","text":"He also knows how to deal with those that aren't."},{"kind":"para","text":"It won't be a pretty picture in that day."},{"kind":"para","text":"People can see this and think, \"The Lord doesn't seem too loving to me. He is literally talking about throwing them into an 'oven' and 'swallowing them up in his wrath.' How is that a loving God?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"They are right."},{"kind":"para","text":"That doesn't sound like a loving God."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can talk about God's wrath a bit deeper in Revelation, but here's what I will say;"},{"kind":"para","text":"God's wrath is reserved for the evil sinful people here who don't love the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's love is reserved for the forgiven, faithful people here who DO love the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's that easy."},{"kind":"para","text":"The wrath that is poured down on the evil will be for those who have really gone too far."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, this discussion is best saved for Revelation, but David will give a little more clarity on why they deserve it in the next verse as well."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They want to do whatever it takes to hurt the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Evil people hate God."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's the only way to put it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They can't do anything to Him, so who do you think these evil people will take it out on."},{"kind":"para","text":"I wish they could just sit in their evil thoughts alone, but they can't help themselves but to do something."},{"kind":"para","text":"So they attack God's children."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are the ones they can see."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are the ones they can hurt."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord will have no choice but to give them what they deserve."},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps you have seen in movies (or have experienced it in your own life), where a bully is destructive towards all the weaker people around him. People hate him, and he seems to always get away with his evil. By the end of the movie he finally gets what he deserves. I am a huge \"Back to the Future\" fan (guilty pleasure), and it's always great to see the scene where George McFly punches the lights out of Biff. The bully finally gets what he deserves."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the end, evil will get what it deserves, and that is from God's wrath being poured out on them."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will seem as if they had gotten away with their terrible deeds, but God doesn't just let it go."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord will face you personally if you are against Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have no doubt there are plenty of nonbelievers who have seen the Lord's work in their lives, and they have chosen to reject it and call it fluke."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord can't make it any more obvious except killing you and pulling you up before His judgement."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, He wants to give you a chance, and He wants His people to live in love and unity here on Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"So He sends His servants to go into all the world, and His servants are largely rejected."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's the sad reality of following Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are often quite lonely in the work."},{"kind":"para","text":"The church is great, and the believers are to be good encouragers, but they are also to be good helpers."},{"kind":"para","text":"Most of the time they are not helpers, however, and they end with encouragement as their final act of worship."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves.","ref":"James 1:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"People, here, are left without excuse but to follow Christ and to make Christ known to others."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We will sing and praise God even while His wrath is being poured out."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, because we know what they deserve."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will have done terrible things."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our world has seen that come to reality today."},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't call them terrible but they truly are."},{"kind":"para","text":"Killing babies inside or outside of the womb is a terrible thing (California's motto is \"a sanctuary for abortion)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Robbing people, and neglecting people is a terrible thing (In multiple states, robbing is legalized)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Murdering adults is a terrible thing (In Canada, you can ask your government with suicide assistance)."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can look at much of our current culture and call it terrible."},{"kind":"para","text":"Most people have accepted this line of thinking and called it \"the new normal.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The sad news is, it will only get worse."},{"kind":"para","text":"Revelation tells us that they will become more greedy, more evil, and more bloodthirsty..."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's why God's children will rejoice when God finally ends the evil here on Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"No one in their right mind should be happy when evil wins."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should ALL desire that evil would be banished and it would be impossible for anyone to ever do anything evil again."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":13}]},
    "22": {"chapter":22,"intro":[],"previously":["As we have gone through Psalms, I have found it amazing how many connections we can make to the Lord Jesus Christ and His ministry/sacrifice for the world. There are so many things that I know have been personal to David, but are actually prophecies of the Lord and come to fruition in the gospel accounts.","Today's chapter is no different. We get a real in-depth look at the thoughts and feelings that Jesus faced on the cross, and the purpose that He reminds us of why He had to face these difficult and terrible things to save all of humanity. This is a wonderful Psalm about the mind of Christ, and it is a somber (yet encouraging) reminder to the reader of what Jesus went through specifically for you."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Why Have You Forsaken Me?","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This should be a familiar verse to all of us reading here."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"NAnd about the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani? that is to say, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?","ref":"Matthew 27:46"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have recognized quite a few tie-ins through Psalms leading to the Savior, and this chapter is definitely one of them."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is a very sad (yet prominent) chapter of our scriptures."},{"kind":"para","text":"We get a taste of Christ's suffering through the gospel."},{"kind":"para","text":"We understand His beatings and His death as meaning punishment for our sins."},{"kind":"para","text":"But there's a deeper thought here."},{"kind":"para","text":"We get to see into the mind of Christ during this time."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yes, He quotes this psalm here, but there's more to it then just asking \"God why hast thou forsaken me?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It's deeper than that."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is speaking to the Lord in a moment of great torment and anguish and there's a real struggle happening in His physical pain."},{"kind":"para","text":"No doubt, David (as he's penning this) felt alone and rejected of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"There was a few mistakes that David made in his lifetime that would insinuate that God would not be able to use or protect him."},{"kind":"para","text":"But Jesus Christ... He never did anything to be rejected of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"So in this moment of Him crying from the cross, He felt rejected for the very first time."},{"kind":"para","text":"God had turned away from Him as He bore the entire worlds sins on the cross, and so Jesus cries out from the cross asking \"Why have you forsaken me?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"That conversation continues with this thought, \"Why are you so far from helping me, and from the words of my roaring?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Roaring\" means \"distressed cry.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It is certainly obvious that Christ's crying from the cross was stressful."},{"kind":"para","text":"It certainly was stressful for Christ, but it was also stressful for every one of His disciples, and His mother who was sitting close by."},{"kind":"para","text":"So He cries out to God asking where His presence is."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you have never been in a situation where you have lost the presence of God, you are a very blessed man."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is the worst feeling in the world to feel God's presence turn away from you in your life."},{"kind":"para","text":"Often it's by sin... other times it's by faith."},{"kind":"para","text":"God builds our faith up in seemingly harsh ways sometimes, but we don't know how wonderful the presence of the Lord is until we are missing it for a while."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus cries out to the Lord quite often in the gospels."},{"kind":"para","text":"We constantly see Him alone in His prayers and thoughts speaking to God and crying out to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"The pain of the cross lasted for hours, and He was seen crying out to God while He was up there."},{"kind":"para","text":"He spent more time on the cross speaking to the Lord, than He did speaking to the people around Him watching."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is a very important example for us to remember."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we are in a season of great trial, we should seek the Lord before seeking others."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, we have this backwards."},{"kind":"para","text":"We want to seek help from others, and get as many people on our side to face the trial, rather than just going straight to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Bible has a theme of why this is wrong over and over again, and we should learn (if not anywhere else) from the cross that the Lord is whom we depend on alone for our burdens."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ cried to the Lord all the time."},{"kind":"para","text":"He never stopped speaking to God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"\"See that none render evil for evil unto any man; but ever follow that which is good, both among yourselves, and to all men.\" 1","ref":"Thessalonians 5:15"}]}]},{"start":3,"end":5,"title":"The Praises of Israel","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The purpose of the cross should be evident to the Christian."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should understand that the reason that God sent His Son to die on the cross is very plainly obvious and simple."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are a sinful world."},{"kind":"para","text":"We go against the Lord in every waking moment."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moment we are born we start our walk in unrighteousness."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm about to have another child soon (Lord Willing), and I have grown quite immensely in my patience since my first child. The Lord has taught me some lessons as I've raised up my daughter, and I'm hoping that I can use some of those lessons for this second child. My first though, however, when knowing the future strain (just of having children in general) is, \"How can I lead this child to live in righteousness?\" See, they are born, and they start their life of sin right away. The curse takes a hold on them, and you can see it start to fester in their beings as soon as they are born."},{"kind":"para","text":"Apparently when I was a baby (I don't remember this, but I'm told from 3 different people that it's true), I was sitting in the living room one day, and my father was outside doing something. My brother was set to watch over me while my dad worked on what he needed to work on... ...As soon as my dad left the house, I started crying like crazy. My dad rushed back in and started in on my brother. \"What did you do?\" He yelled at him, and my brother said, \"Nothing! I was watching him like you asked, and didn't do anything! He just started crying.\" My dad went back outside, and I started screaming and crying again. He came back inside a little more angry and asked my brother again, \"What did you do? You have to be doing something, he's only crying as soon as I leave!\" \"Nothing! I swear!\" My brother said. So the third time, my dad pretended to leave. He opened the door and shut it but stayed inside and peeked around the corner. I began to start crying and my brother tried to calm me down. \"No, no, no, please don't start again!\" He said, and I just let loose. My dad found out that I was just crying (likely) to get my brother in trouble. Perhaps, maybe, I was afraid of my dad leaving? I don't know (I don't think I had ever had the problem before)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sin is present the moment we are born, and so the initial purpose of God sending His Son is to give a payment for that sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"He sent His Son to die on the cross (taking our punishment FOR US) because He is holy and He inhabits the praises of Israel (that is the Lord's redeemed)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But he was wounded for our transgressions, he was bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace was upon him; and with his stripes we are healed. All we like sheep have gone astray; we have turned every one to his own way; and the LORD hath laid on him the iniquity of us all.","ref":"Isaiah 53:5-6"},{"kind":"para","text":"God gave His Son for the whole world (yes) but only those that accept Him have a reason to praise Him."}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites had a lot of men in the lineage to cry out to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"There were more (however) that did not."},{"kind":"para","text":"There were plenty more who forsook the Lord in their lifetime and did not lead a good legacy for their children to follow."},{"kind":"para","text":"Us (reading this today) probably don't come from a very long line of believers either."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have a lot in our family tree who have forsaken the Lord in their traveling through this world, and have not passed down the most essential information to the feeding of the soul in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Millennials catch a lot of flak for some of the way in which this world has turned out to be. The truth is (and I'm just being honest here), it's the generation before us that has failed us. It's the generation before them that has failed them. The lineage of Christ should have been passed down along the lines somewhere, and at some point, our fathers stopped crying to the Lord, and started forsaking Him. I can't think of a single time in my life (growing up) where someone told me or explained to me about who Jesus was and what He did for me. I went to Jehovah's Witness churches, and Catholic Churches, and churches of all sorts and types, and not a single person stopped and spoke to me about Jesus... ...It wasn't until I was a teenager (almost an adult) that I heard my first message about Christ. I rejected it until I became an adult, but it's sad that it took that long for me to hear that message. My mother had told me there was a God. There were certain prayers she would have me pray, but there was no talk about Jesus Christ in our household. They did not have that information passed down to them. I am told that my grandparents knew about Christ. I am told that we come from a line of Christians somewhere in our family history, yet there was no mention of Him until my generation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ knows that God is there to deliver those that cry out to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows that God will not leave Him there forsaken."},{"kind":"para","text":"David understands this too."},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason this is there is because God has a proven track record of taking care of His children."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you did not know, Christ doesn't stay on that cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn't stay in the grave."},{"kind":"para","text":"He comes back to life."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord doesn't forsaken Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the moment, perhaps He did (or at the very least that is how Christ had felt), but in the end, we see God is doing a work in the world that can only be accomplished in this way."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we cannot look to the cross and see how terrible and sinful we are in this world, we are not taking the cross of Christ seriously."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"Less Than Men","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"How little Christ thinks of Himself."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is not saying this because He is \"trying\" to be humble."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is saying this because He truly feels like the least in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"David felt this way about himself (no doubt) and he was king of one of the most prosperous nations at the time."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus was not in a place of \"authority\" in the same sense, but he was certainly above everyone that was watching His crucifixion, and instead of saying, \"I am God, and I am King! I have all authority to destroy these people...\" He says, \"I am a worm, and no man...\""},{"kind":"para","text":"He considers Himself to be nothing more than an object lesson for the onlookers."},{"kind":"para","text":"He's vile to the people around Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"No body cared about who He actually was."},{"kind":"para","text":"He told them several times that He is God in the flesh, and instead of worshipping Him (which they were literally doing a week ago), they chant \"Crucify him, crucify him!\" over and over again."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But they cried, saying, Crucify him, crucify him.","ref":"Luke 23:21"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"When the chief priests therefore and officers saw him, they cried out, saying, Crucify him, crucify him. Pilate saith unto them, Take ye him, and crucify him: for I find no fault in him.","ref":"John 19:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"He was rejected of His own people, and mistreated for His Godly acts."},{"kind":"para","text":"Nothing has changed today either."},{"kind":"para","text":"Much of this world still chants \"Crucify Him.\""}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Look at what the onlookers say in the gospel:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He trusted in God; let him deliver him now, if he will have him: for he said, I am the Son of God.","ref":"Matthew 27:43"},{"kind":"para","text":"They literally answered a prophecy without even knowing it FROM THE SAME PSALM THAT JESUS HAS QUOTED!"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is quite possible that this entire Psalm is played out through the gospel message on the cross verbatim!"},{"kind":"para","text":"The sad thing is, (as you may recall) they knew His acclamation as the Son of God, and they are still seen mocking Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"They may not have believed He was the Son of God, but it was a dangerous gamble they were making."},{"kind":"para","text":"If He is not the Son of God, they would be crucifying a plain man for no reason."},{"kind":"para","text":"They would have just murdered an innocent bystander."},{"kind":"para","text":"If He IS the Son of God (however) they just murdered the Son of the Creator of the universe."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is a very serious problem if it's true."},{"kind":"para","text":"If God can create, He can certainly destroy."},{"kind":"para","text":"The amount of torment and torture they would face if Christ is God's Son."},{"kind":"para","text":"Except, Christ says one thing that keeps them from the wrath of God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then said Jesus, Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do. And they parted his raiment, and cast lots.","ref":"Luke 23:34"},{"kind":"para","text":"If Christ didn't say this from the cross, there would be a lot more anguish for the people here today."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord held His anger back from destroying these people right then and there on the behalf of the pleading of His perfectly sinless Son."},{"kind":"para","text":"He does the same for us today, and for all of eternity, only because of Christ's pleading in this moment."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, I believe Christ is in presence of God continuously pleading with Him every day and every moment."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto God by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.","ref":"Hebrews 7:25"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he that searcheth the hearts knoweth what is the mind of the Spirit, because he maketh intercession for the saints according to the will of God.","ref":"Romans 8:27"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who is he that condemneth? It is Christ that died, yea rather, that is risen again, who is even at the right hand of God, who also maketh intercession for us.","ref":"Romans 8:34"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore will I divide him a portion with the great, and he shall divide the spoil with the strong; because he hath poured out his soul unto death: and he was numbered with the transgressors; and he bare the sin of many, and made intercession for the transgressors.","ref":"Isaiah 53:12"}]}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"title":"Follow God","entries":[{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ (from the beginning) knew the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"God could have just sent Christ down from above."},{"kind":"para","text":"He could have made Him come down like a mighty angel, or a powerful revenger."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is not what God does, however, because Christ will come down that way eventually, and it won't be for the salvation of the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather, He had His Son literally BORN into this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"It could be (therefore) argued that the sin nature is complete through the father."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is not sinful, so this child could not be either."},{"kind":"para","text":"When Christ was born He was not born with a sinful nature like the rest of the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"He didn't need to be taught how to be righteous."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's Spirit was with Him from the beginning."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the angel answered and said unto her, The Holy Ghost shall come upon thee, and the power of the Highest shall overshadow thee: therefore also that holy thing which shall be born of thee shall be called the Son of God.","ref":"Luke 1:35"},{"kind":"para","text":"You might say, \"Well why didn't God do this to everyone then? Couldn't He just provide the Spirit to everyone and it be done?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"God wanted the world to be replenished by His creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wanted us to experience His goodness on our own."},{"kind":"para","text":"We rejected that (and still reject that often), and so we experience the evil as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"But from the beginning, the plan was to have ONE Savior, not a bunch of saved zombies with no mind of their own."},{"kind":"para","text":"God wants us to depend on Him, and seek after Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason that Christ is the only one born this way was to show an example of how God wants US to live our lives."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is 100% God (of course), but He was also 100% man, and the 100% man part is where we are supposed to get our example."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might not have the gift of healing, and of tongues or prophecying, but we certainly have the gift of the Holy Ghost today, and we are then able to follow Christ's example of how to pray, how to preach, who to look out for, and what compassion looks like."},{"kind":"para","text":"God gives all of us a choice to follow Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He did not give that choice to Jesus."},{"kind":"para","text":"Though (personally) I believe that Jesus could have turned away from the lord if He wanted to, but there was nothing in His being that would make Him want to do that."},{"kind":"para","text":"He loved His Father, and so He spent His whole life speaking with Him, and following Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"From the moment He was conceived, He started to follow God."}]}]},{"start":11,"end":13,"title":"Animals Devour","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is not far from those who call on Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was not far from Jesus either even while Christ was on the cross feeling forsaken by God and everyone around Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"The LORD is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit.\" Psalm 34:18 (Spoiler Alert)"},{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn't altogether cast Jesus to the side."},{"kind":"para","text":"He comes back for His Son."},{"kind":"para","text":"It personally could be argued that the reason God turns away in this moment is because of the sin of the people, not the sin of Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ BORE our sins (yes, that means He wore them), but there was no sin found in Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And ye know that he was manifested to take away our sins; and in him is no sin.","ref":"1 John 3:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"So God is turning away from the sins of the people at this moment, and it is why Christ felt forsaken."},{"kind":"para","text":"God could not watch this scene unfold."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are some under the impression that God IS watching this unfold here, and when it says \"forsaken\" it just means that Jesus feels forgotten."},{"kind":"para","text":"Let's take that for a moment as truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"If God was watching this unfold, as a just and righteous Father of the universe and of Christ, He would not stand by and be unamused by it."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has a strong compassion for His children who love Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He protects His children and gives them safety."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is not what Christ was getting at this moment, and it it pretty well assured that God was not willing to watch His children reject His only Son."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.","ref":"John 3:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"God was still there, He was just waiting for this cruel and terrible scene to be over."}]},{"start":12,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These people that were crucifying Christ were like wild animals."},{"kind":"para","text":"They were just tearing Him apart, and without mercy or remorse."},{"kind":"para","text":"They were terrible people, doing terrible things, literally ignoring their conscience."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can take a look at the people around the cross (other than them mocking Jesus, and chanting \"crucify him\") and see that their sin has numbed them to compassion."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And sitting down they watched him there;","ref":"Matthew 27:36"},{"kind":"para","text":"They literally sat and watched as Jesus was pleading out and in suffering."},{"kind":"para","text":"They had no care at all at what had just taken place."},{"kind":"para","text":"They couldn't find any fault in them, and they wanted to watch this innocent man suffer."},{"kind":"para","text":"The fact that they wanted to watch any man suffer is kind of wild to me, but especially and specifically Jesus?"},{"kind":"para","text":"That's just outrageous."}]}]},{"start":14,"end":18,"title":"The Crucifixion Detailed","entries":[{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"So the crucifixion comes during the Roman empire."},{"kind":"para","text":"During the time of this writing, there was no such thing as death by crucifixion."},{"kind":"para","text":"But this verse (here) gives the literal outline of what a crucifixion looks like."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's the type of anguish a man would face on the cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"His bones would be out of joint (trying to lift himself up for air using those nails through his hands as leverage), his life being drained from him (poured out like water), his heart melting away as he tries to save every painful breath until it's his last..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But one of the soldiers with a spear pierced his side, and forthwith came there out blood and water.","ref":"John 19:34"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is certainly scientific explanation of why there was water that came out (as he was trying to breathe, his lungs filled with water, that is still a thing that can happen to people who are in dire pain while breathing)."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe it was also His heart that was ruptured."},{"kind":"para","text":"His heart was filled with blood and water."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think that's best demonstrated in the gospels of course (John specifically)"}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"After so much blood loss, and so much energy used to try and breathe, your strength just starts to fade away."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus also talks about being thirsty on the cross, and the guard gives Him vinegar to drink."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"After this, Jesus knowing that all things were now accomplished, that the scripture might be fulfilled, saith, I thirst.","ref":"John 19:28"},{"kind":"para","text":"I have no doubt that Jesus felt His death as it was coming."},{"kind":"para","text":"He felt every bit of the pain on that cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"He felt the pain of the sins of the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"He felt His death literally enveloping Him."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is such a crazy in-depth description of the crucifixion."},{"kind":"para","text":"They literally DO pierce Christ's hands and feet."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, we must remember that crucifixion did not exist during the time of this writing by David."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is a foreign concept to David and the people during this time."},{"kind":"para","text":"I would think that anyone reading this Psalm would say, \"What is he talking about? Nobody pierced his hands and feet. This is a weird thing to say.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"But David is speaking prophetically here."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is speaking through the inspiration of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is the one speaking here."},{"kind":"para","text":"He see's the wickedness of humanity all around Him, and the pain that He has caused Him through this method of crucifixion."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are like \"dogs\" he says."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are pacing around Christ and barking."}]},{"start":17,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, another very clear and obvious prophecy coming true."},{"kind":"para","text":"We read it a moment ago."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they crucified him, and parted his garments, casting lots: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, They parted my garments among them, and upon my vesture did they cast lots.","ref":"Matthew 27:35"},{"kind":"para","text":"It was the people around Him AGAIN fulfilling this prophecy from this ONE SINGLE Psalm."},{"kind":"para","text":"What a powerful Psalm David writes here."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is the Psalm for every Good Friday service."}]}]},{"start":19,"end":22,"title":"God Saves","entries":[{"start":19,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is saved, and He IS the Savior."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is delivered, but not until after the pain."},{"kind":"para","text":"He redeems the saints, but not until after the purchase."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is freed, but not until after captivity."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is heard, but not until after He is forsaken."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is alive, but not until after He is dead."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord delivers Him!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when Jesus had cried with a loud voice, he said, Father, into thy hands I commend my spirit: and having said thus, he gave up the ghost.","ref":"Luke 23:46"},{"kind":"para","text":"God controls the Spirits, and He knows exactly what to do and how to place Christ's Spirit where it needs to be."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Through the Holy Ghost, Christ declares God's name to the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ's ministry on Earth was to declare God's name to His brethren (that is His disciples)."},{"kind":"para","text":"They got a front row seat to Jesus' preaching every single day for about 3 years."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, they will take that message and with the power and boldness that the Spirit of God provides (and that it provided for Jesus), they will declare the name of God to the rest of the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will preach His praises about the crucifixion of Christ!"},{"kind":"para","text":"An important note I want to make here."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will not forcefully use people in whichever fashion He see's fit."},{"kind":"para","text":"I know I've heard some people say that God treats a portion of people in scripture like a \"puppet\" but that is not true."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will use people who are willing to be used."},{"kind":"para","text":"If they are not willing, He will not force them."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is included with Balaam, and Jonah, and some of the wicked people in the Old Testament."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even Judas Iscariot."},{"kind":"para","text":"You don't have to be saved to be used of God, you just have to be willing."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, if you are not saved when you are used of God, you will not have a good time being used."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will sting, and it will hardly seem worth it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is the same with the Apostles in the book of Acts."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only way they could preach God's name like they did is if they were willing to be used of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"If they rejected God's calling for them, then God would send someone else."},{"kind":"para","text":"They, however, WANTED God to use them."}]}]},{"start":23,"end":24,"title":"He Has Not Despised","entries":[{"start":23,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ cried to the Lord, the Lord heard His cry."},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps the Lord looked away..."},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe He could not look on the suffering of His Son."},{"kind":"para","text":"His compassion shows His anguish for His only Son who is taking the penalty for sin here."},{"kind":"para","text":"That does NOT mean that God cannot hear."},{"kind":"para","text":"He may not have looked, but He certainly was willing to hear."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is always willing to hear our prayers."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is always ready to meet with us after we cry out to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is disgusted by sin, but He is pleased with our repentance."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The foolish shall not stand in thy sight: thou hatest all workers of iniquity.","ref":"Psalm 5:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The fear of the LORD is to hate evil: pride, and arrogancy, and the evil way, and the froward mouth, do I hate.","ref":"Proverbs 8:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But your iniquities have separated between you and your God, and your sins have hid his face from you, that he will not hear.","ref":"Isaiah 59:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"He couldn't look at the sin and Isaiah says \"He doesn't hear you because of your sin\" but it was not Jesus' sin that God was looking away from."},{"kind":"para","text":"He turned away from the killers AROUND Jesus."},{"kind":"para","text":"His ears (however) were always listening and attentive to His Son's cries."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is why there is reason to rejoice."},{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn't leave Jesus in His pain and in His death."},{"kind":"para","text":"He brings Christ back to life!"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is a great reason for people to rejoice all over the world!"},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, if everyone knew that and believed it, we would have a very hard time NOT rejoicing Him."}]}]},{"start":25,"end":28,"title":"He Paid His Vow","entries":[{"start":25,"end":28,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The moment that Christ died it seemed that all was lost."},{"kind":"para","text":"But that is how Christ paid His vows."},{"kind":"para","text":"It was how He kept His promise to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It was the single most important purpose for Christ to be born to begin with."},{"kind":"para","text":"He came into this world, specifically to live a perfect life, and die on the cross completing the law."},{"kind":"para","text":"Without it, we would not have \"All the ends of the world\" remembering and turning to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ paid His vow, and there was a moment before He did where He asked the Lord if there was another way to pay it..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he went a little further, and fell on his face, and prayed, saying, O my Father, if it be possible, let this cup pass from me: nevertheless not as I will, but as thou wilt.","ref":"Matthew 26:39"},{"kind":"para","text":"There was no other way, and so Christ pays his vows with the predetermined way of the Father."},{"kind":"para","text":"Praise the Lord He did."}]}]},{"start":29,"end":31,"title":"We All Bow","entries":[{"start":29,"end":29,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This last part here is all about Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone will worship Him at one point or another."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that say they will never bow to the Lord are greatly mistaken."},{"kind":"para","text":"Multiple times in scripture it says that everyone will bow."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For it is written, As I live, saith the Lord, every knee shall bow to me, and every tongue shall confess to God.","ref":"Romans 14:11"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth;","ref":"Philippians 2:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe the moment each one of us goes into eternity, we will all be too weak to stand before God and fall straight to our knees."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that know Him will fall in reverence to His holiness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that don't know Him shall fall by the fact that they were wrong, and they have signed their death warrant..."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should all know that we have no control over our soul."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have as much control over our soul as do over our knees before the face of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"So, because of this, we must rely on the Lord with it."},{"kind":"para","text":"How?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well it's by trusting His gift given to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have spent this entire chapter talking about that gift, and He has given it to this entire world to hold and trust in."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we do that, we are then free to let go of our souls in trust to the Savior."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what the Savior saves by the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"He does not save your physical stature."},{"kind":"para","text":"He does not save your trials."},{"kind":"para","text":"He saves your soul."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is why we must read this with Christ in mind, because that is the most precious and valuable thing that the Lord is aiming for."}]},{"start":30,"end":30,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"All it takes is one."},{"kind":"para","text":"If none of the rest of the world comes to know Christ except for ONE man, that is well worth it in the end."},{"kind":"para","text":"If there isn't even one, then Jesus will have every reason to come back His second time, and it won't be to die on the cross for you."}]},{"start":31,"end":31,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This information has been passed down from generation to generation."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Apostles kept the message of the gospel going, and those that gladly received their word took that message and gave it to others until we get to this moment in our time of history today."},{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a time, however, when people will stop taking the message, and (as I've already said) Jesus will have reason to return."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that know Him rejoice over His return."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that don't know Him are doomed for all of eternity."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":28},{"start":29,"end":31}]},
    "23": {"chapter":23,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last Psalm, we see the crucifixion of the Savior. There's an amazing connection between what David is penning (in chapter 22), and what happens to Christ on the cross. Obviously there is a link between the two (David is prophecying of the future Messiah), but there is a lot more detail we can pull from the Psalm about that horrific moment. It asks, \"Why are you forsaking me\" to the Lord, speaks about the praises of Israel, how Christ was treated as less than a man, what it looks like to follow God, how the people around the cross were acting, the details of the crucifixion (before crucifixion was even a thing mind you), and the purpose of the crucifixion.","In our chapter today (after studying some really heavy topics in the last chapter), we see what makes God good. We can look at something like the crucifixion and think, \"God is not protecting His men. He is not concerned about our business here.\" But that is not what the Lord is doing. He is concerned, and He is there to help us in our times of need. He does not turn away from us, or reject us when we are His. That's what this Psalm is a reminder of."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"The Lord Shepherds","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When I was a new Christian and I read this for the first time, I understood it as, \"The Lord is my shepherd; I don't want Him.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"I thought, \"Why would the Psalmist say He doesn't want the Shepherd? That seems like a very strange way to start off this psalm.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course as we continue to read, we find that the Psalmist WANTS the Shepherd, but he is not IN want."},{"kind":"para","text":"In otherwords, the Shepherd provides for him."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what a Shepherd is supposed to do."},{"kind":"para","text":"He provides for His sheep because He loves His sheep, and He wants His sheep to succeed."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, I will say that all of scripture is about the Lord (we should get that through our heads right now), but it's also all about how we can correct ourselves, and live righteously before Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"This Psalm displays that in a perfect way."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Psalmist says \"The Lord\" giving preeminence to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then he says, \"is MY Shepherd. I shall not want.\" giving necessity to himself."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is a Shepherd for His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the Shepherd of His children, and we are the beneficiaries of His sacrifice and leading."},{"kind":"para","text":"He leads, and we are to follow."},{"kind":"para","text":"Without Him, we have not master and no guidance."},{"kind":"para","text":"Without us, He has no love, and no compassion."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"We love him, because he first loved us.","ref":"1 John 4:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"Not only so, but He is YOUR personal Shepherd."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is something to behold."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think there are a lot of people (Christians in particular) who feel outcasted, or neglected by their pastors and teachers."},{"kind":"para","text":"They feel left behind, and uncared for."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is not what the Lord wants."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to Shepherd you."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to bring you in and take care of you."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants you to lack nothing."},{"kind":"para","text":"It would be wise of us, then, to come to Him for the fulfillment of our needs."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Psalmist gives plenty for us to rejoice over the Shepherd over in the coming verses."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Growing up, my parents used to take my brother and I on trips going camping or going boating. That was all well and fine, and I had no problems with any of that. I didn't mind going motorcycle riding, or going fishing. I actually enjoyed that stuff (when I wasn't being yelled at for making a small mistake)... ...The part I loved more than all of that, though, was being able to walk around where we were staying. I liked to just sit by the water and watch it. I liked to hike up and down the dunes rather than drive up them. I thought it was a lot more fun to stay on the ground and explore than to be on a bike or on a boat and watch the whole world quickly pass you by. It was even better if I had someone to go with me and see all the stuff."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is not just about sustaining you and getting you by."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is about spending time with you."},{"kind":"para","text":"He gives you green pastures to lay down in, yes, but He also LEADS you beside the still waters."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is with us when we travel."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to explore WITH you."},{"kind":"para","text":"The part that baffles me is, He never gets tired of spending time with His children."},{"kind":"para","text":"He's already walked these roads with others before."},{"kind":"para","text":"He's walked much of these roads Himself (except without sin), and yet He still finds it a joy to go with us on our journey's."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what makes the Lord so beautiful to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"He could just leave us to our own devices."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has already come to Earth and finished His course."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has already paid the price for all humanity, and can now just sit in Heaven on the throne, and just watch as people make complete fools of themselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, that's not what He desires."},{"kind":"para","text":"He desires to give us His Spirit so that He is always with us no matter where we go."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, Thomas, because thou hast seen me, thou hast believed: blessed are they that have not seen, and yet have believed.","ref":"John 20:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"If I were to walk around the lake with someone who didn't want to be there, it would be a pretty boring and dismal journey. They would likely either be complaining the whole time, or they would be silent and depressing. Even if they were silent and WANTED to be there it would make it so much better. We can take in the sites together and just enjoy the creation that we see all around us. The Lord doesn't have to speak with us when we are journeying, and yet He still does. He isn't just a silent bystander, He is present with us, and He is able to use His Word to talk to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"He leads, and we should follow."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows where to go, and it would be wise of us to take His paths rather than tread our own."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of people who think they know the path better."},{"kind":"para","text":"They try to lead the shepherd rather than be a follower, and the Shepherd will not have it that way."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sheep don't know what they are doing."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will lead other sheep astray."},{"kind":"para","text":"There must be a master Shepherd who is able to keep the sheep in order and guide them the correct way."},{"kind":"para","text":"Otherwise, we might be led to dry and dead pastures rather than green ones."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of Christians going through some deep valleys (which we will talk about in a moment) and think to themselves, \"Boy, the Lord is not refreshing me like this Psalm says. I do not feel my soul restored. I feel more and more burdened with each passing moment.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth is, if we are walking with the Lord into \"paths of righteousness\" there's a good chance others will see that and hate it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They like the broad paths, and you are walking in at the straight gate."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat: Because strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it.","ref":"Matthew 7:13-14"},{"kind":"para","text":"They think to themselves, \"Well good for him, he has a Shepherd to guide him, but some of us have to actually work for what we got.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"They are wrong."},{"kind":"para","text":"They can have the Shepherd too if they are willing to follow."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't think they belong, but they certainly do."},{"kind":"para","text":"All they must do is follow Him, and He will lead those same people on the same paths."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world, however, hates this, and so they reject Him with every fiber of their being, and it can wear on an individual."},{"kind":"para","text":"I know it certainly wears on me."},{"kind":"para","text":"It starts to feel like a burden to follow the Lord because the world pressing against you every step of the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"They make you feel like less than human."},{"kind":"para","text":"They make you feel like you are making a mistake."},{"kind":"para","text":"As if you are walking into the grave."},{"kind":"para","text":"The sad part is, the opposite is true."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that tell you not to follow the Lord, are (themselves) walking into the grave by their own leisure."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are trying to take people with them into their failures and doom."},{"kind":"para","text":"An unrighteous man should not be able to wear us down to the point where we stop following the Shepherd."},{"kind":"para","text":"If one can, you might have been a sheep following sheep rather than knowing the Shepherd personally."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When we are close to the Lord, we have a comfort from Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rods and staffs are not comforting tools, I think that should be well understood."},{"kind":"para","text":"The rod and staff were used to keep the sheep in order."},{"kind":"para","text":"The staff was used to press the sheep in a certain direction and keep them together."},{"kind":"para","text":"The rod was used to protect the sheep if needed."},{"kind":"para","text":"It would be used to fight off any predators that were traveling their way and wanted to attack the sheep."},{"kind":"para","text":"As long as the Shepherd was there with His staff, the sheep were protected."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes the staff would be used to \"catch\" sheep that tried to veer away from the pack."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sheep do that quite a lot."},{"kind":"para","text":"We start to think about what it would be like to stop here for a bit and tread our own paths."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can just catch up to the Shepherd later."},{"kind":"para","text":"99% of the time that sheep do this they end up becoming lost."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Shepherd will leave all His sheep to go find that ONE sheep who has gotten himself into trouble."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"What man of you, having an hundred sheep, if he lose one of them, doth not leave the ninety and nine in the wilderness, and go after that which is lost, until he find it?... ...And when he hath found it, he layeth it on his shoulders, rejoicing. And when he cometh home, he calleth together his friends and neighbours, saying unto them, Rejoice with me; for I have found my sheep which was lost. I say unto you, that likewise joy shall be in heaven over one sinner that repenteth, more than over ninety and nine just persons, which need no repentance.","ref":"Luke 15:4-7"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord rejoices over His sheep staying with Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is happy to know His sheep, and care for His sheep personally enough to go out of His way to find them if they ever wander off."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is not willing that any would be outside of His leading and presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"He does what it takes to guide us, and protect us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can walk through the worst parts of our lives (that would be \"the valley of the shadow of death\") and yet we can feel comfort knowing that He is there for us."},{"kind":"para","text":"This applies to so many things in our lives."},{"kind":"para","text":"Most people struggle the most in their finances."},{"kind":"para","text":"They struggle with certain sins as well, but finances (today) are a big worry."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe the Lord is even shepherding through that as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is there to protect you and give you direction."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is there to help you when you are in desperate need no matter the circumstance."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord wants to be with you in the times that are treacherous as well as the times that are well."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to be with you all the time, and we should always find reason to follow Him and stay under His protection wherever we go."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"title":"Questioning God","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When everything looks bleak, the Lord sets the table."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord takes care of His own."},{"kind":"para","text":"The whole world can be against you, and make it difficult for you to survive and continue forward, but when you have the Lord, you always have a table set."},{"kind":"para","text":"He anoints us with oil (which is a good picture of the Holy Ghost), and he provides us with more than we deserve (the cup running over means it above plenty for yourself)."},{"kind":"para","text":"God runs over your cup with everything good."},{"kind":"para","text":"He gives you more grace than you can handle..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But he giveth more grace. Wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble.","ref":"James 4:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"More love than you can handle..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Beloved, let us love one another: for love is of God; and every one that loveth is born of God, and knoweth God.","ref":"1 John 4:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"More mercy than you can handle..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be ye therefore merciful, as your Father also is merciful.","ref":"Luke 6:36"},{"kind":"para","text":"More joy than you can handle..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Hitherto have ye asked nothing in my name: ask, and ye shall receive, that your joy may be full.","ref":"John 16:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"More provision than you can handle..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger: but they that seek the LORD shall not want any good thing.","ref":"Psalm 34:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"More Spirit than you can handle..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And be not drunk with wine, wherein is excess; but be filled with the Spirit;","ref":"Ephesians 5:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"More of Himself than you can handle..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"\"Therefore if any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new.\" 2","ref":"Corinthians 5:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"More life than you can handle..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The thief cometh not, but for to steal, and to kill, and to destroy: I am come that they might have life, and that they might have it more abundantly.","ref":"John 10:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"He provides above and beyond, to the point where it literal \"runs over.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It runs over and those that are around you get to experience His goodness with you (whether saved or not)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The table is set \"before the presence\" of his \"enemies\" mind you."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that hate the Lord cannot deny the work of the Lord (even though they try and pretend like they don't see it)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The table is set, and it is obvious that (even in the time of famine) God is providing for His own."},{"kind":"para","text":"The enemies are even able to sit at the table if they so desire (and are not willing to cause a stirup)."},{"kind":"para","text":"If they want provision, they must sit with us."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Going back to the burden of following Christ, we can read this and say, \"David is wrong. Goodness and mercy don't seem to follow me anywhere I go in this world.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"No."},{"kind":"para","text":"You are right."},{"kind":"para","text":"This world lacks goodness and mercy."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is why we must not seek it here."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we are looking above during our times of Earthly trials, we will always find goodness and mercy to hold onto."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are looking at our surroundings instead, we will have plenty of reasons to complain and worry."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Devil wants to keep your from looking above."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants you to fixate on the temporal and the trials."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants you to squirm during the times of difficulty."},{"kind":"para","text":"He would rather have you questioning your circumstances rather than relying on God for them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan wants you to question if God is really on your side, rather than taking your questions directly too God."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think a lot of people are afraid to question God. We are taught that questioning God is a sin, and we should simply just trust Him with our situations, and respect His decision on the matter. We certainly should trust Him, but that doesn't mean we cannot question Him. He WANTS you to come with your questions and burdens. He WANTS to answer your needs. The problem is, we feel as if questioning the Lord is the same thing as not having faith in the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you:","ref":"Matthew 7:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus promotes us to ask questions, seek Him, and knock at His door."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's okay to have questions for the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's okay to seek after Him in times of trial."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's okay to come to His home and request help."},{"kind":"para","text":"He actually LIKES that."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is a GOOD Father, and He seeks to help His children through every season of need and suffering."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don't shy away from the Lord, when it is through the trials that He is anticipating your questions the most."},{"kind":"para","text":"He can handle even the hardest questions you throw His way."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6}]},
    "24": {"chapter":24,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last Psalm, we read about the Shepherding life of the Lord. He is our guide and our stay. He brings us into the proper place and protects us when we are in danger. He gives us everything we need (above and beyond what we even deserve). Even in the middle of terrible people, God takes care of His own, and that is something that should draw us into His peace and assurance.","In this chapter, we give God all the glory. His creation magnifies His glory, His presence magnifies His glory, His hosts and children should magnify His glory. All glory belongs to Him, and this Psalm will give us a chance (and reason) to sing glory to His name."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"God's Creation","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think there is room to address (here) the difference between loving the world, and being friends with the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are told by James:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye adulterers and adulteresses, know ye not that the friendship of the world is enmity with God? whosoever therefore will be a friend of the world is the enemy of God.","ref":"James 4:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"And yet Jesus says:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.","ref":"John 3:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not allowed to be friends with the world, but we are to accept the fact that God loves the world?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Now we read in this Psalm that the earth is the Lord's!"},{"kind":"para","text":"If God is good, and He loves the Earth, and it belongs to Him, then why can we not be friends with the world?"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are to love His creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the key to understanding this."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must differentiate between loving creation, and loving worldly living."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not to love the world's lifestyle, but we are to love the world enough to reach them."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what God wants for His children."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants us to love those with a Godly love, not with a fleshly love."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is a stark difference between the two."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we love the world like the world see's love, we are only looking to try and adapt to their lifestyle."},{"kind":"para","text":"We want to consume in that type of love."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we love the world in a Godly form, we don't want to adapt to it, we want to change it and make it whole."},{"kind":"para","text":"We want to further creation, not diminish it."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what the love of the world does, it diminishes God's good creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"God loves His creation, and wants it to flourish, and everything that is in the world (the world itself as well) belongs to God."},{"kind":"para","text":"He should get to do whatever pleases Him with it, seeing as it belongs to Him anyway."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You might remember in God's creation that water was the opening source in the beginning."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the earth was without form, and void; and darkness was upon the face of the deep. And the Spirit of God moved upon the face of the waters.","ref":"Genesis 1:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"Then on the third day he divides the waters."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again (I've mentioned before), when scripture speaks about water, it is a symbol of God's Word."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a symbol of God's preservation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even in the beginning chapters of this book, God is preserving His Word."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might notice that there are a lot of things in this world that disappear and go away."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everything rots and decay's."},{"kind":"para","text":"Except for water."},{"kind":"para","text":"Somehow it never ends."},{"kind":"para","text":"We drink it up, and yet the oceans are still full."},{"kind":"para","text":"The clouds gather it and pour it upon the land, and yet the oceans still flow."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even climate change activists must see the abundance of water as a miracle right?"},{"kind":"para","text":"In the same sense, the Word of God has no ending either."},{"kind":"para","text":"It continues to flow, and continues to provide for His land and His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you have never taken a moment to visit a shoreline and just look at the vast ocean, I highly recommend doing that sometime soon."},{"kind":"para","text":"Take a trip to a local beach and just look at the vastness of the ocean."},{"kind":"para","text":"What a great and grand view to behold."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at it and realize, \"God owns this. This is all His doing, and it's His to work with.\""}]}]},{"start":3,"end":7,"title":"Being With God","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That's a great question."},{"kind":"para","text":"Who can stand in the place of God?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Who would want to?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I think there are a lot of people who desire to stand in God's place."},{"kind":"para","text":"I mean they literally desire to take His place on the throne."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are like Satan believing they can do a better job than God can."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan has done a lot of strange and silly things, but to assume such a position is probably his silliest."},{"kind":"para","text":"But the question is a legitimate one."},{"kind":"para","text":"David is asking, \"Who are the ones that can be in the presence of God?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"I think we all desire (at some level) to be in God's presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even the Atheists want to see the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will get to in due season, but it will be for all the wrong reasons."},{"kind":"para","text":"They won't like standing in God's presence because it means a home of torment and torture for their open rejection of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"I pray that they would change their minds before that time, because the Psalmist reveals the types of people who can stand before the Lord in the next verse."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Let's evaluate ourselves for a moment."},{"kind":"para","text":"Do we have clean hands?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps our hands are clean of deceit and lies."},{"kind":"para","text":"I doubt it, but I will give you all the benefit of the doubt (I certainly know my hands are not clean)."},{"kind":"para","text":"How about a pure heart?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The line starts to blur here."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are none with pure hearts reading this today."},{"kind":"para","text":"My desire is that my heart would be pure, but my flesh won't allow it..."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we cannot identify our hearts as pure, then we certainly won't be able to identify with the rest of this verse."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are a religionist today, you have lifted up your own soul into vanity."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm sorry, but that's the truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't blame you though, your church has taught you how to do that."},{"kind":"para","text":"They teach you how to control your own spirit, rather than taking the Spirit of the Lord and allow that to be your control."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have all sworn deceitfully, there is no getting away from that."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have done things that are not above par when it comes to benefitting ourselves in some fashion."},{"kind":"para","text":"So therefore, by the standard set forth in this Psalm, none of us will stand before the Lord in holiness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not even the Apostles will be there."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is, however, one who will be."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus Christ embodies this."},{"kind":"para","text":"He can stand before the Lord because He has clean hands, a pure heart, has never lifted his soul to vanity, and has never sworn deceitfully."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the embodiment of perfection."},{"kind":"para","text":"Thankfully, His sacrifice gives us access to this same perfection."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","ref":"John 14:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is not by my will and lifestyle that will get me there."},{"kind":"para","text":"He, alone, gets us access to God's Holy Place."},{"kind":"para","text":"Praise the Lord for Jesus who is the author and finisher of our faith."},{"kind":"para","text":"Without Him, we would be destined for Hell and failure."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ gives us access to God's throne and presence and I am so thankful for that."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let us therefore come boldly unto the throne of grace, that we may obtain mercy, and find grace to help in time of need.","ref":"Hebrews 4:16"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That is the only way to recieve blessing and righteousness."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's only through God's salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is only found in the person of Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be it known unto you all, and to all the people of Israel, that by the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, whom ye crucified, whom God raised from the dead, even by him doth this man stand here before you whole. This is the stone which was set at nought of you builders, which is become the head of the corner. Neither is there salvation in any other: for there is none other name under heaven given among men, whereby we must be saved.","ref":"Acts 4:10-12"},{"kind":"para","text":"When we have Christ, we are provided with blessings and righteousness to walk in."},{"kind":"para","text":"We still have a daily choice to walk in them, I think that should be well understood."},{"kind":"para","text":"Salvation doesn't simply mean that you are perfect forever."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather, salvation means you no longer have to follow your sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"You have the opportunity to turn from it and follow after righteousness and blessing."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you do not have salvation, you do not have the choice to turn from sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"You will live and dwell in sin, and there is nothing you can do to reject and turn from it."},{"kind":"para","text":"You are stuck in your sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn't want sin around His holy place."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants righteousness and blessing."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are still bound to your sin, you will not have access to His thrown."},{"kind":"para","text":"Does that mean we no longer have sin when we are saved?"},{"kind":"para","text":"No, that's not what I'm saying."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us. If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness. If we say that we have not sinned, we make him a liar, and his word is not in us.","ref":"1 John 1:8-10"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are sinners, through and through."},{"kind":"para","text":"As long as we are living on this Earth, we will always have sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"But again, we have access to the Father (the forgiver) through Jesus alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"So we are able to turn from our sin, and ask for forgiveness directly from the one we sinned against."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have always found it kind of odd that there would be such things as \"confessional booths.\" The idea is that you are able to air out your sins, and talk to a man about your problems. The thing that astounds me about this tradition is that people think they are talking to a \"holy\" man about their sins. They think they are talking to someone who can solve their sin problem. They can't do that though. It's obvious they don't solve the problem because you have to go back and confess those same sins again the next time you do it. Mind you, the one you are talking to is a sinner as well. If a \"holy\" means says he is not a sinner, he is a liar (just like John says). John is looked at as a holy man. Guess what? He was a sinner! The person you talk to in the confessional booth is just as much (if not more) of a sinner as you are! That is why we must have salvation. We can come straight to the Lord (who cannot sin) and confess our faults to the one who can TRULY change us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Whosoever is born of God doth not commit sin; for his seed remaineth in him: and he cannot sin, because he is born of God.","ref":"1 John 3:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"I think a good study to go through for the repercussions of sin (the lifestyle and freedom from it) would be through 1 John."},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, we are confident and assured that Christ's sacrifice to us, gives us the promise of salvation, which leads to God's blessing and righteousness placed upon our lives."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Look at the way this is written here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Going back to the confessional booth, I find it odd that there is a mesh between the priest and the congregant. Obviously this is for privacy purposes, but I believe the priest knows exactly who they are talking to. Obviously the person talking knows that it's the priest on the other side (or at least they should hope it is depending on what they are confessing). They don't see face to face. They don't speak to each other as if they are in the same room. There is a separation between them."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Psalmist says, \"This is the generation that seeks the face of the Lord.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We desire to be that generation today."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no vail, or wall, or mesh between our confession to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"We seek His FACE."},{"kind":"para","text":"We want to talk to Him personally as if He is right in front of us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We want open access to the Father."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord has provided that for His children, and I am so thankful I can go to my Father and speak to Him whenever I want."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't have to be at the church house."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't have to be in the confessional booth."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't have to go to a specific location."},{"kind":"para","text":"I can talk to Him right from my bed."},{"kind":"para","text":"I can talk to Him from my kitchen while making dinner."},{"kind":"para","text":"From my desk while writing notes."},{"kind":"para","text":"I can talk to Him if I go on a walk outside."},{"kind":"para","text":"I can talk to Him right after tragedy strikes, or while I am in a hospital bed."},{"kind":"para","text":"I can talk to Him, and be present with Him any time I like thanks to the sacrifice of Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"What a grand privilege that is bestowed on mere mortals!"}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The King of glory comes to your presence!"},{"kind":"para","text":"What a joy that we get to be a part of His presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"What an amazing reality we can behold!"},{"kind":"para","text":"We should never take God's presence for granted."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet it's something we will do."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's something that the Israelites have done, and it's something that the disciples will do, and it's something we still do today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Never lose the awe of having the King of glory in your presence!"}]}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"title":"The King of Glory","entries":[{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a funny question."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't think there is anyone that cannot answer that."},{"kind":"para","text":"If I were to go out on the streets today and ask this question to completely random strangers, they would all say God."},{"kind":"para","text":"They could not deny that He is the King of glory."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe the purpose of this question is to get the people to shout back the answer."},{"kind":"para","text":"God wants to hear His people say it."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is not just a King mind you."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the King \"of glory.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"In other words, He has higher praise than any other king in existence."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is King of kings."},{"kind":"para","text":"His glory gives us reason to lift our hands in praise and worship."},{"kind":"para","text":"This the way to worship the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"We shout praises to His glory, and open the gates for His presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Heavens sing of His glory."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"title":"The Lord of Hosts","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What an end to this chapter of Psalms."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a short and sweet Psalm, but it's a powerful one."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord deserves recognition for His glory."},{"kind":"para","text":"We often rob Him of that in various ways."},{"kind":"para","text":"We perhaps will rob God of glory by trying to put the glory and attention on ourselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe we will rob Him by trusting in a man behind a mesh screen."},{"kind":"para","text":"Or we will rob Him by trusting in our traditions and religions."},{"kind":"para","text":"We rob God of glory by rejecting His salvation through His Son alone as a gift to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We steal God's glory in various ways all the time, and that is not something we SHOULD be doing."},{"kind":"para","text":"It makes us weaker, and brittle when we take glory that belongs to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"All glory belongs to Him, so therefore we should not be taking any glory to ourselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we recieve glory for anything, it should only be from the Lord providing it to us (not man, and not ourselves)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Glory belongs to God, and we should preach and praise His name above everything else."},{"kind":"para","text":"This Psalm ends with a \"Selah.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"I think it's sufficient, when we come to the close of this Psalm to stop and just ponder what you read."},{"kind":"para","text":"Take a moment to sit and soak in the King of glory."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don't just skim through this in a passing study, but sit and contemplate His glory and presence for you."},{"kind":"para","text":"Meditate on what you just read."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10}]},
    "25": {"chapter":25,"intro":[],"previously":["The last Psalm showed God's creation, the importance of being in the presence of God, recognizing Him as the ultimate King of glory, and knowing the Lord of Hosts on a personal level. It was strongly emphasizing Jesus Christ and His majesty.","In this Psalm, we get the person of Christ in a more personal application. He is the only person that can give us clarity, direction, provision, comfort, and knowledge. We should seek Him out with everything we can, and this Psalm will be a proof of why that is so important."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"The Way","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, we can look at this from the eyes of David, but I think it's more appropriate to apply to the future providence of both Israel and ourselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus also lifted His soul to the Lord, it was not to some vain thing."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everything Christ did was focused on bringing mankind to Him, and if there are any today who do not trust in Christ it is only by their own negligence, not by the lack of want from God."},{"kind":"para","text":"There really is no excuse for us to not lift our souls to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has given us every reason to bring our entire being to Him."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes we might feel backed into a corner with nowhere to run."},{"kind":"para","text":"David felt this way in a lot of instances through his life."},{"kind":"para","text":"Israel will get to this point as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes that is where the Lord wants us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might spend so much time not paying attention to the Lord, and we somehow end up where we are not supposed to be which only requires us to look no further than up towards Heaven begging for mercy."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus was never backed in a corner, I want us to get that straight."},{"kind":"para","text":"But He did feel these pains."},{"kind":"para","text":"His enemy at the time was Satan."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously Satan doesn't triumph over Jesus, but he was able to inflict some pain on the Lord that is not fun to bear."},{"kind":"para","text":"It would seem (to the rest of the world) that the enemy one the moment Jesus was put up on that cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"Especially to the disciples."},{"kind":"para","text":"They looked at Jesus and thought \"That's it. We have failed. We are no longer salvageable.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously the Lord went to that cross on purpose, and they find out the purpose when they see Him again three days later."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Throughout all of scripture we see transgressors doing some pretty heinous things against the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every single one of them, however, feels shame at some point."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes it takes them up until their death before they feel it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Other times it just takes a moment of conviction and regret for them to feel it (like Judas)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, we can guarantee that no transgressor will ever feel successful in their sins at some point in their life."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even the hardest of criminals today are brought to shame one way or another."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might see some gang leader or drug dealer and they feel like they are on top of the world, but they will eventually fall off."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will eventually feel shame."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord will put them in their place one day."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether that's on their death bed fervently asking for mercy, or in Hell where it's too late."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have a place that the Lord will surely fix them on, but it's up to them to turn to Him before it's too late."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Everything that Christ did was in step with the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he that sent me is with me: the Father hath not left me alone; for I do always those things that please him.","ref":"John 8:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus was constantly praying and evaluating His next moves."},{"kind":"para","text":"He never did anything that was against the Father's Will, no matter how bleak or uncertain it might have looked."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, we must recognize that Jesus is 100% God and 100% man."},{"kind":"para","text":"He trekked this life like man, but had the mindset of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"He died like a man, and defeated death like God."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was tempted like a man, but overcame temptation like God."},{"kind":"para","text":"He walked this imperfect world like man, but lived a perfect life like God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every step was a path from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He depended on the Lord, and that was for an example of how we are to move."},{"kind":"para","text":"There were times when the Father told Christ, \"Son, you are going into dangerous territory. They are likely going to try and stone you, but I will be with you, and you will not be harmed.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ went, and that is surely what takes place, and yet God protects Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He made it clear that He would show Him the way, and teach Him the path."},{"kind":"para","text":"He can do that same thing for us today if we are in constantly obedience to His Will."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","ref":"John 14:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the way, and before they were called Christians they were called \"people of The Way.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be people of \"the Way\" and learn God's paths so we are always in step with where God would have us to go and what God would have us to do."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These past two verse illustrate John 14:6 so well and I don't want us to miss it."},{"kind":"para","text":"David pens, \"Show me the way\" and Jesus says, \"I am the way.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"David then says, \"Show me the truth\" and Jesus says, \"I am the truth.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"David then says, \"You are my salvation\" and Jesus says \"I am the life.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The answer to God's way, truth, and life is found in Jesus Christ alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you want to come to the Father you must learn of Christ and follow Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will give you access to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Wait\" means \"to hope\" or \"expect.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"When David says he is \"waiting\" on the Lord, what he is saying is \"On thee (God) do I hope all the day.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"He is expectant of God to be there and lead."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's a good expectancy for the world to have."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether they want to agree that God actually exists or not, I will hold on to the hope of the Lord and wait on Him all day."},{"kind":"para","text":"As the days get darker, my hope gets stronger."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ's Words of who He is (the way, the truth, and the life) should give us assurance and comfort in this ever changing and vastly sinful world."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"Sins Forever","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"From the beginning of scripture, to the penning of this verse, God has shown tender mercies and lovingkindness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some people read scripture and see the destruction, and sin, and chaos and think, \"The Lord is not in these events, if He is, He is cruel and harsh.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord saw these events, and He warned against them, but these people still flowed their own charts and paved their own ways."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, through it all (though the Lord had to put some people down, and take care of some terrible messes), He was merciful, and loving."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is a God of mercy."},{"kind":"para","text":"David will write that again in a moment."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows how to measure out His mercy and give it to people according to His own foreknowledge."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some people we see, we might think they don't deserve the mercy of God, and yet God still extends mercy to them for some reason."},{"kind":"para","text":"We wonder, \"God? Why are you not putting them in their place? Why are you allowing them to get away with this?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"But it's because He has \"tender\" mercies."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Tender mercies\" means \"compassion.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"He see's the world through the eyes of compassion."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we see Christ (again, who is 100% God) He walks and talks with absolute compassion."},{"kind":"para","text":"If He was angry and vengeful, people would not want to be around Him, and yet He had multitudes following Him nearly the entire three years that He presented His ministry."},{"kind":"para","text":"Since the beginning of time the Lord has been merciful and loving."},{"kind":"para","text":"He still is today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Nothing has changed from Adam to David."},{"kind":"para","text":"Nothing has changed from David to Jesus."},{"kind":"para","text":"Nothing has changed from Jesus to you."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is still merciful, and loving."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has not forgotten His soverign forgiveness and continual leading, and He never will forget."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"\"The sins of my youth\" are those sins from his past, and \"my transgressions\" are those sins from his present, and \"remember thou me (in mercy)\" are those sins in his future."},{"kind":"para","text":"David was a sinful man."},{"kind":"para","text":"We all are."},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot write this off as Jesus' lifestyle here."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, Christ did bear the sins of mankind on that cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"He felt the transgressions of Adam, of David, and of you and me when He hung up on that cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason that God will \"forget\" the transgressions of our past present and future is only because Jesus bore them in His death."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's goodness (which is the only thing that is actually good in this world) forgives us of our sins when we accept it."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must come to Him and say, \"God, don't remember my sins from my past, present and future. Give me Jesus, and help me to follow His way, truth, and life so I can live debt free before you. Give me new life.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"And crazy enough (if we truly mean it), God grants it to us!"},{"kind":"para","text":"He gives us forgiveness at that single moment."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's all it takes."},{"kind":"para","text":"David clarifies further:"}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, the \"Way\" is Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are all sinners."},{"kind":"para","text":"You, me, your neighbor, your wife, your daughter, your son, your granddaughter, your coworker, your boss, your sister, your brother, your mother, your father, whoever it is that you are coming in contact with, you can bet they are a sinner."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are two things I know to be absolutely true when I walk into any room with any persons."},{"kind":"para","text":"1. They are all liars."},{"kind":"para","text":"2. They are all struggling with sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"You can bet that no matter where you are (even in the church, that's just the nature of mankind so you will have to deal with and address it with grace and truth from the Word of God)."},{"kind":"para","text":"God CAN (and will if we allow) teach sinners in the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone might be a liar, but Christians should not be found purposely dealing lies."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone may be a sinner, but Christians should not be purposely living in it."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must be people of the Way, and people of the Way reject both every moment of every day."},{"kind":"para","text":"WE (those of the Way) have the option to follow sin and lies, or reject them and repent."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that don't know the way, are just sinners and liars without remorse."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is an absolute fact."},{"kind":"para","text":"David illustrates this further in the next couple verses:"}]}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"title":"Meekness and Truth","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The meek (arguably) are the only ones who can give proper judgement."},{"kind":"para","text":"They won't abuse their power like the prideful."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are prideful have power, and they misuse it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Their guidance comes from selfish ambitions and evil rulers."},{"kind":"para","text":"The guidance of the meek comes from the Lord specifically."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Will\" is an affirmative action."},{"kind":"para","text":"In other words, David says, \"God WILL (no questions about it) teach the meek His Way.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, Christ IS the Way."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the direction that humanity will prosper in."},{"kind":"para","text":"If humanity is not prospering, and things are falling apart, we are assured that it is not following Christ."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus is mercy, and truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can look through the oracles of time and trace God's mercy and truth through everything."},{"kind":"para","text":"His path will always lead to Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are trying to follow God without Christ, you will never get there."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus IS the truth, and it is through Jesus that we have mercy from the Father."}]}]},{"start":11,"end":13,"title":"Navigating Spirits","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David has spent a good portion of this reminding the Lord of His mercy and lovingkindness, and now he is requesting a pardon."},{"kind":"para","text":"He says, \"By the way Lord, because of your mercy, please forgive me for my sins. I know what I have done and I need you to forgive me because my iniquity 'is great.'\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Through the Way (that is Jesus) we have forgiveness for sins."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"\"My little children, these things write I unto you, that ye sin not. And if any man sin, we have an advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ the righteous: And he is the propitiation for our sins: and not for ours only, but also for the sins of the whole world.\" 1","ref":"John 2:1-2"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus pardons sins."},{"kind":"para","text":"He forgives the sin of the person who comes to Him, and He forgives the sins of those that already know Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is a sin forgiver."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's what His mercy looks like."},{"kind":"para","text":"God forgiving us of our sins even though we know we don't deserve His forgiveness."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The way of the Lord is taught to His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's not something you just gain sight into right away."},{"kind":"para","text":"You can enter the Way instantly, but you must trek further along if you want to learn it better."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I was younger, we used to go on motorcycle trips quite a bit with my family. We would go to specific camping spots we had been to hundreds of time. One of our favorite places to go was Dumont. This was a place full of sand dunes literally out in the middle of the desert. It's honestly kind of a magical place. If you were new there, you would probably be very confused about how to navigate that place. There are dunes as far as the eye can see. There are no roads, no bushes, no trails, just dunes. The winds blow a lot over there, and so the dunes are constantly shifting and shaping into different things. There is one particular dune there called \"Competition Hill.\" It's this rather large hill where people race to the top and test their off road vehicles to see how well they do in the sand and steep terrain. We would go there most of the time just to watch people racing. It's kind of in the middle of all the other dunes. Every time we went camping, we would always go there. How did we know how to get there? Honestly, I don't know. We would find specific dunes that looked a certain shape, or had a certain flat spot, and that's how we knew which direction to take. We never got lost somehow... ...We always found our place and we would take the same way every single time. The more we did it, the better we would recognize how to get there when we would go."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the way of Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"We learn how to navigate the more we are following Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"It might take some time getting there, but it will become sweeter and sweeter the more time we take to do it."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Knowing where you are going and how you are going to get there is a comforting thought."},{"kind":"para","text":"I love having direction."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't understand how people can do anything by a whim of the moment."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of pastor's and ministers that I know that just fly by the pants of their seat."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't have a schedule or a calendar, they just go wherever the day takes them, and so many people get lost in the background and forgotten because of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are in the way (being taught the way) are those who have direction and motive."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will have a relaxed and confident soul."},{"kind":"para","text":"A soul at peace."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should want more people to be like this."},{"kind":"para","text":"His \"seed\" shall inherit the Earth doesn't have to necessarily mean that he will have more kids, but rather that the more people who are in the way the more plentious we are in number."},{"kind":"para","text":"We become brothers in Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are in the family of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are all part of the same seed of Jesus when we are following Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't have to be related through biology, but we will be related through the blood of Christ."}]}]},{"start":14,"end":18,"title":"Forgiven","entries":[{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God's got a secret."},{"kind":"para","text":"What is that secret?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well if I told you, it wouldn't be a secret would it?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Actually, the secret has been revealed but people are too dull and ignorant to listen to it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They say, \"Wait, I want to know this secret! Tell me what it is!\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We say, \"Put your faith in Jesus Christ and you will know the secret.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The secret is simple, we come into the knowledge of all things when we have Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason I can know those two absolutes (as stated earlier) is because God has revealed that secret to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"I wouldn't have known that to be true any earlier in my life."},{"kind":"para","text":"I knew people were liars, but I didn't think EVERYONE was."},{"kind":"para","text":"I knew people were sinners, but I thought there were at least SOME good people."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord has revealed the secret fact to me that there is a whole spiritual battle happening behind the scenes, and scripture literally opens up how that's taking place."},{"kind":"para","text":"You cannot know that secret unless you are with Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"You may know it exists, but you will never understand it without Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"The tactics of spiritual warfare will be kept as a question mark until you trust in Christ for salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"When you are in the Way with the Lord, secrets are revealed."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, this may take time, but you will eventually learn things you didn't even know was a possibility before."},{"kind":"para","text":"Ten years of being saved (as of this writing) and I'm still learning new things through this book."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here's another secret;"},{"kind":"para","text":"We may not know the answer to something, and we may be in the middle of a very cruel and hectic trial, but focusing on the Lord gives us freedom from those pains."},{"kind":"para","text":"He gives us a path to freedom even in the middle of the desert and storm."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are going through something, may I suggest you keep your eyes on God."},{"kind":"para","text":"He WILL do something, even if your life is in the balance."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is faithful to His children, and does not just leave them in the wilderness."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It seems as if David thinks God is not turned towards him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He might think this way because of his own sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has turned His face away from David's sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"God, however, stays involved with the affairs of man."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will chasten, and He will correct, and He doesn't just turn away because you have fallen wayward."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has a heart for you, and you should want a heart for Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can develop a heart of love and care for the Lord, and we should be seeking with everything we can to do that."},{"kind":"para","text":"David has literally just said that all of His ways are mercy."},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course the Lord is going to have mercy on him."},{"kind":"para","text":"David is feeling afflicted and desolate, but God will not keep him there."},{"kind":"para","text":"God especially won't keep the beggar there."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will show mercy to those who are dropped to their knees in full leniency on Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those are the people He looks for the most in His soverign grace."}]},{"start":17,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"May I say, the greatest pain we have the chance to bear in this life is the pain of sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is heavy, and stressful."},{"kind":"para","text":"It weighs you down and makes you feel forgotten."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sin is good at making you feel isolated from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's good at making you feel as if you are a lost cause."},{"kind":"para","text":"David felt like a lost cause here."},{"kind":"para","text":"He felt as if God is not going to help him out ever again."},{"kind":"para","text":"King Saul might have felt this way too, and truth be told Saul was a lost cause because he never actually trusted the Lord for forgiveness and correction."},{"kind":"para","text":"He constantly bashed his way through life by his own means and selfishness, and just assumed that he was too far gone for the Lord to use anyway."},{"kind":"para","text":"Friend, I don't know if you need to hear this, but you are not too far gone from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you come to the Lord with this level of humility and dependancy, He WILL forgive you and set you free."},{"kind":"para","text":"You need to know that."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't matter what the preacher, or pastor might tell you about your sinful nature."},{"kind":"para","text":"Scripture says come to Him, and He will forgive you."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.","ref":"1 John 1:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"To him give all the prophets witness, that through his name whosoever believeth in him shall receive remission of sins.","ref":"Acts 10:43"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I, even I, am he that blotteth out thy transgressions for mine own sake, and will not remember thy sins.","ref":"Isaiah 43:25"},{"kind":"para","text":"Come to God asking for forgiveness, and (through Jesus Christ, who is the Way) He will grant it to you without any strings attached."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are people, however, who will not be forgiven."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are labeled in the next verses;"}]}]},{"start":19,"end":21,"title":"A Soul Keeper","entries":[{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The enemies of the Lord will not receive forgiveness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Is it because God will just not forgive certain people about certain things?"},{"kind":"para","text":"No."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's because they won't want forgiveness from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't seek to be forgiven, and so God will not seek to forgive them either."},{"kind":"para","text":"They may seem like they are doing well and staying on top for the time being, but God will not just let them slide by with their evil."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will always serve justice on mankind."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will always judge the evil of this world by His perfect standard of righteousness."},{"kind":"para","text":"His standard is perfect by the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the standard of judgement we should all be seeking for."},{"kind":"para","text":"Otherwise we will have justice systems like we do today (corrupt, and demeaning to the innocent)."}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is a good keeper of the soul."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what salvation is by the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's letting go of your own souls matter and trusting God with it through faith in Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's saying, \"I believe Jesus really died for me, and so I am trusting that you are not lying and you can do what you please with my soul."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's accepting that God can control your soul however He see's fit."},{"kind":"para","text":"If God see's fit to send me to Hell for all of eternity, who am I to argue with Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"If He see's fit to keep His promise of salvation through Christ, I have no room to argue."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am trusting Him to do what He knows is right."},{"kind":"para","text":"I, of course, know that God keeps His promises (His ways are mercy and truth), but ultimately He is the righteous judge who gets to make whatever decisions He wants to."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've entrusted Him with it."}]}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"title":"Redeem Us","entries":[{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has redeemed Israel."},{"kind":"para","text":"David has been redeemed, and Israel has been redeemed."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have to accept the redemption though."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have to place their trust in God's redemption (which (again) is Jesus Christ)."},{"kind":"para","text":"If they are not willing to accept it and put their trust in the form of redemption that God gave them, they must blame themselves for their demise."},{"kind":"para","text":"They can not blame the Lord for that."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has provided them a way which was a promise to them since the beginning of time."},{"kind":"para","text":"They must hold on to that \"Way\" and follow it with their hearts, minds, and souls."},{"kind":"para","text":"They must put everything they have into Christ and His salvation for them on the cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the redemption story."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a good story, and it's a true story, because God's Word is true, and evidenced by the Holy Spirit which reveals all secrets."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But God hath revealed them unto us by his Spirit: for the Spirit searcheth all things, yea, the deep things of God.","ref":"1 Corinthians 2:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"If you want to know the deep things of God, you must start at the cross of Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"Redemption starts there."},{"kind":"para","text":"Secrets are revealed after, as you are traveling along the Way of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Amen."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22}]},
    "26": {"chapter":26,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last chapter, we took a deep look about the Way of the Lord, the many sins of the world, the embodiment of meekness and truth, navigating with the right Spirits, knowing we are forgiven, trusting our soul in the only one who can keep it appropriately, and the desire for the Lord to redeem His people. It was a great chapter highlighting God's salvation story, and this chapter continues that vain a little deeper.","In this chapter, we see the integrity of a saved person. They can walk with the Lord in confidence, and have their lives examined because they know the salvation of the Lord personally. They are confident in God's grace and stay for them, and they are not willing to waiver no matter what kind of curveball the world tries to throw that them. If you have a hard time trusting the Lord, or you are often questioning your faith, this chapter is a good one to study."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"Examine The Spirit","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Asking God to judge you is a scary thought."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't know many people who would desire God's judgement."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are seeking for His mercy."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is a time to receive God's mercy, and it's the moment we take Christ to ourselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we do that, the judgement of God is placed on Jesus, and so when we are judged, we are righteous through Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"So this statement is two-fold."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can boldly ask the Lord to judge us because Christ has given us salvation, but it is CHRIST who ultimately had the right boldness to be judged by the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore being justified by faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ:","ref":"Romans 5:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are justified through Christ, and judgement is not our conclusion."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will be judged, don't get me wrong, but we are also justified because Christ is our covering for sin."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Being covered by Christ fixes every part of us."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are truly His, we will have righteousness, justification, proof, a new mind;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God.","ref":"Romans 12:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"a new Spirit;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will put my spirit within you, and cause you to walk in my statutes, and ye shall keep my judgments, and do them.","ref":"Ezekiel 36:27"},{"kind":"para","text":"and a new heart;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh.","ref":"Ezekiel 36:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have new life;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"\"Therefore if any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new.\" 2","ref":"Corinthians 5:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ completely changes us, so once again it's HIS boldness that allows us to ask God to \"examine\" us."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's also good to keep short accounts with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are only human afterall."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will make mistakes, and we will fall into sins, but the Lord will \"try the reigns\" and it is needful to see where we are lacking in some areas so we can strengthen and fix those areas."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are a constant work."},{"kind":"para","text":"I praise the Lord that Jesus was not."},{"kind":"para","text":"He completed the work, and He lived perfectly before the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the only reason that I would even have the desire that God would search me or examine me."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I'm going to be honest here."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are some days when I just feel too lazy to walk in the truth of God's Word."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are days when I don't even feel like reading, or praying, or thinking about scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"That seems to be my life though."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am sitting here today planning to write out commentary for two chapters of scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"It takes me about 6-10 hours depending on the depth of the chapter."},{"kind":"para","text":"Today, the chapter is short, but those are usually the ones that take the longest to write out."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am not even (currently) using these notes for any sort of Bible study."},{"kind":"para","text":"These are just personal."},{"kind":"para","text":"I always see God's \"lovingkindness\" but I'm not always walking in His truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am sure that I am not alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"David was not a man that always walked in God's truth either."},{"kind":"para","text":"There were days when he walked by the flesh."},{"kind":"para","text":"It got him into serious trouble."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"This I say then, Walk in the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfil the lust of the flesh. For the flesh lusteth against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh: and these are contrary the one to the other: so that ye cannot do the things that ye would.","ref":"Galatians 5:16-17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus though... He always walked in the truth of God's Word."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was constantly seeking after what pleased the Father."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how we should be viewing our life and faith stage."},{"kind":"para","text":"I may not always walk in the truth, but I am learning to walk a little more faithfully each passing day."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every day I'm learning to renew my joy, and renew my Spirit in walking with the Lord!"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus has given us that ability through His Spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has given us the ability to refresh ourselves in the Lord whenever we need it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Between you and me, I always need it."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is never a day when I feel like I'm good without God."},{"kind":"para","text":"I may not always walk in His truth, but I certainly don't stop walking with Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Let me put it in a different perspective."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't always walk in His truth, but I am always looking for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even without always walking in the truth, I still find the Lord nudging and pushing me forward."},{"kind":"para","text":"He always gets my attention again, and I still do what I have been called to do."},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems that I cannot help myself."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has put a Spirit within me so that even when I don't feel like doing something for the Lord, my Spirit somehow propels me into action anyway."},{"kind":"para","text":"I can't explain how it works, I just see it happen all the time."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't matter how much bitterness we might feel, if we have the Spirit of God we will continue forward in the work either way."},{"kind":"para","text":"He just makes it happen, and we must have our hearts prepared to change in a moments notice for the work of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I never regret going forward for the Lord, even if I start off as a bit bitter or calloused to it."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This, too, helps propel us forward."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we are surrounded by people who will encourage us in the Lord's work, it will help us not become sour to it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It becomes a passion, rather than a necessity."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord had twelve Apostles with Him for the work, and He calls them \"friends.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"They were helpful to encourage Him forward, and He encouraged them forward as well (actually, He encouraged them more than they encouraged Him, but that is only because they didn't have the Holy Spirit guiding them yet other than through Jesus Christ)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The jest of it is, they were all there to help serve with the Lord during easy seasons, and difficult stormy seasons."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only time they fled was when he was betrayed and arrested."},{"kind":"para","text":"They couldn't stick around and watch their Lord be mistreated and betrayed."},{"kind":"para","text":"I imagine the moment that Judas kissed Christ the disciples were all very confused and hurt."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was the only person that Jesus sat with who was \"vain\" and a \"disassembler.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Seriously, look at the kiss of Judas."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moment he kissed Christ, everyone disassembled."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ knew who he was the entire time, but never ratted him out for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"He waits, and He loves, and He pushes for salvation, but it just never clicks to Judas."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is quite sad."},{"kind":"para","text":"The other friends of Christ, however, were people who were not vain."},{"kind":"para","text":"They were not disassemblers."},{"kind":"para","text":"They were not looking to cause mischief or problems."},{"kind":"para","text":"They wanted to help the Lord on His mission, and they stuck by Him as faithfully as possible even through close calls and near disasters."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Who was it that Jesus sat with?"},{"kind":"para","text":"He sat with Sinners and Tax Collectors."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And it came to pass, as Jesus sat at meat in the house, behold, many publicans and sinners came and sat down with him and his disciples. And when the Pharisees saw it, they said unto his disciples, Why eateth your Master with publicans and sinners? But when Jesus heard that, he said unto them, They that be whole need not a physician, but they that are sick.","ref":"Matthew 9:10-12"},{"kind":"para","text":"They were the lowest of their current society."},{"kind":"para","text":"He loved the lost."},{"kind":"para","text":"He saw their spirit needed renewal so He chose to sit with them and renew them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those are the people that would actually accept His salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Pharisee's thought they were already too good, and so they wouldn't accept Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"It was the poor and needy that saw value in Christ, because they didn't have value in anything else."},{"kind":"para","text":"Nobody else bothered pouring value into them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ was the only one that did."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, the Pharisees were fools gold."},{"kind":"para","text":"They acted and looked like the real thing but they weren't."},{"kind":"para","text":"If Jesus sat with them than He WOULD be sitting with evil doers and the wicked."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knew who was genuine, though, and who was not."},{"kind":"para","text":"He made that distinction from the get go as He explained to them over and over again that one of His disciples was not really with them."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's saved for a later study."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we have the Lord, we have a boldness to allow God to examine us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be requiring it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even desiring it."},{"kind":"para","text":"We want to make sure we are in the right standing with the Lord, and the only way for that to happen is if God searches us and corrects us where we need to be corrected."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, many people see the correction, and instead of obeying their need to change, they fight against it and get upset with the Lord for trying to change them."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants you to live in holiness and righteousness, and that will not happen if you are not willing to accept His correction."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":11,"title":"Innocence By God","entries":[{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is only one who is innocent by the way."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded.","ref":"James 4:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"The term \"Wash your hands\" is a sacrificial ritual."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sacrificing to the Lord was not a very clean and easy thing to do."},{"kind":"para","text":"It required a little sacrifice."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus was that sacrifice for us, and so we don't need to make sacrifices like those of the Old Testament law."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can wash our hand in literal \"innocency\" because the Lord was our innocent sacrifice."},{"kind":"para","text":"There was no sin found in Him at all."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is why we are able to come to the altar of the Lord and plead for grace from Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will grant it through His Son."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is a great reason to \"publish with the voice of thanksgiving...\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is worthy of our praise by the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even if He didn't give His Son to die for us, He is still worthy."},{"kind":"para","text":"The fact that He has given this world salvation is even more of a reason we are assured that He is worthy."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has given us a source of freedom, and innocency though we are enslaved, and evil people."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is so good."},{"kind":"para","text":"He's too good."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are undeserving..."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Someone said, \"The people that are best fit for ministry are those that couldn't stay out of the church.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"I love the church."},{"kind":"para","text":"I love the congregation."},{"kind":"para","text":"I love to teach people."},{"kind":"para","text":"I love to help people."},{"kind":"para","text":"I love to reach people."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are so many aspects of the church that I love."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, most of the church has become political."},{"kind":"para","text":"That makes many people draw away from it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It has become mundane and necessary, rather than rejoiceful and desirous."},{"kind":"para","text":"I go to church to worship the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Serving and helping is all great and has it's place, but that is not the main focus of the church."},{"kind":"para","text":"A church that puts service as the main focus is a church that will run their congregation dry."},{"kind":"para","text":"The opposite is true true!"},{"kind":"para","text":"A church that puts being SERVED as their main focus is a church that will run their leadership dry."},{"kind":"para","text":"There has to be a nice balance, and I don't see there being one in many of the churches today."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have been in both situations now, and I think that church leaders need to be aware of this and harbor a community of balance between both of these."},{"kind":"para","text":"Actually, we see this in the family dynamic of David as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus did it right."},{"kind":"para","text":"He took care of the big things, and gave his disciples specific tasks that He knew they could handle."},{"kind":"para","text":"He trained them in it, and then positioned them to succeed, helping them along the way when they needed it."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how the leadership should be, but that is not usually how the leadership is."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that love the Lord's house are those that should be placed in prominent positions to serve, but they should also be those that are served as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Too much of one or the other will draw away from the ultimate goal of God's house which is spending time with the Lord."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus was placed in a tomb, but He did not stay there."},{"kind":"para","text":"His body and soul were taken to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is great news for all of us!"},{"kind":"para","text":"When we have Him, we will be WITH Him in eternity as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will not be gathered with the lost."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will be gathered with the saved!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Gather my saints together unto me; those that have made a covenant with me by sacrifice.","ref":"Psalm 50:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air: and so shall we ever be with the Lord.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 4:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have a people we will be gathered with, and those people are them that have trusted in Jesus Christ who is already gathered in eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you don't have Christ, you WILL be gathered with sinners and bloody men."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are mischievous men who take bribes."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are \"religious\" men."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are not men who are genuine about their following of the Lord."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord redeems us by the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Redeem\" means \"ransom\" or \"rescue.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord purchases us, and we are then rescued from an eternity away from Him in pain and torment."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will be spending our every moment with Him in paradise where there is no sin or pain."},{"kind":"para","text":"David says, \"be merciful to me.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how He redeems us."},{"kind":"para","text":"His mercy is our redemption."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom we have redemption through his blood, the forgiveness of sins, according to the riches of his grace;","ref":"Ephesians 1:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom we have redemption through his blood, even the forgiveness of sins:","ref":"Colossians 1:14"}]}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"title":"An Even Place","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I see a lot of self-proclaimed Christians who are very confused about what they are supposed to be doing, and how they are supposed to believe."},{"kind":"para","text":"There have been a few who question everything about their faith."},{"kind":"para","text":"They read something enticing online, or a friend says something that doesn't add up to their faith, and instead of addressing it through scripture, they just through their entire faith out and believe they are absolutely wrong."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is one thing for sure that we can place our foot on that is even and won't let you stumble, and that is that Christ died for you, and that is how He saved you."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you stumble over that, it is only because you don't truly believe it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Trusting in Christ is an absolute assurance of redemption."},{"kind":"para","text":"When you are on that foundation, everything else can be built on it."},{"kind":"para","text":"If it doesn't fit on that foundation, it is not meant to be there."},{"kind":"para","text":"If it is confusing, you don't need to use it."},{"kind":"para","text":"If it is frustrating, you don't need to be around it."},{"kind":"para","text":"If it is proofless, then you are not meant to hold it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is our steady foundation."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is our even place."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is where we must start."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must stem everything off from His sacrifice and resurrection for us."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the foundation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not our church."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not our faith."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not our ideas or theories."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not our traditions."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not our backgrounds."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not our teachers and leaders."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ alone is the starting point."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what we must hold onto."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might not know much of anything else, but it doesn't matter when we have the assurance of salvation as our forefront."},{"kind":"para","text":"I would be content with never learning anything ever again as long as I know Christ personally."},{"kind":"para","text":"Nothing else matters to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"I can know Christ, and that gives me reason to bless the Lord in His house with His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't care about the rest."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12}]},
    "27": {"chapter":27,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last chapter, David gives us some practical tools to build our walks. He tells us to examine the Spirit, being in the right standing with the Lord (constantly innocent in our way and conduct), and how the Lord judges on even ground. We have a bit of an edge to the unsaved though, because we have the cross of Christ. They do not, so their judgement will be worse than ours because we have an advocate.","In this chapter, we get a deeper look at that advocate. God is always looking out to save, and He's looking out to protect. Sometimes it seems as if the Lord is not going to help and provide as the days becoming darker, but (yet) He still does, and He is constantly watching to see how to serve His children to move them forward."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Confidence in Christ","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isn't He for all of us?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I think this Psalm is very deeply personal to the Christian who is searching to follow the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is a light for us."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have mentioned quite a bit already that the scriptures often refer to light."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't matter how dark the world seems to get, the Lord's light is always found somewhere eventually."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, it sometimes takes far too long to get to that point of seeing God's light, and really the only people to blame is ourselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the time of David, he needed God's light and salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Israel needed it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They had a lot of enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"David had a lot of enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"People that didn't even need to BE his enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knows that God's light triumphs over the darkness of this world, and so he is depending on that."},{"kind":"para","text":"During the time of Christ, the world was still in darkness, but His presence brought LIGHT."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people who loved their routines and their traditions and their religions didn't like that Jesus was pointing them out and speaking against them."},{"kind":"para","text":"They instantly had a problem when the light of the Lord was shining on them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ didn't fear anything, and feared no one."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was constantly following the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"God IS light and salvation for anyone that is searching through this lost dark world."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"During Christ's ministry, we see this happen quite a bit."},{"kind":"para","text":"They try and pin all sorts of things on Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"They ask Him double-sided questions in hopes that He will say something to slip up and they could call Him a blasphemer and a liar."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ never slipped though, and it only made them more angry with Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"All it did was just make themselves look like fools."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what ultimately happens to the prideful and wayward by the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"They try and trip up others, and they end up tripping themselves."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Lately it seems that there is a host encamped against our nation in the US."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have been making enemies with very powerful countries left and right."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, in our fine state of California, our leaders are making enemies with the churches."},{"kind":"para","text":"Down to the mayors of the cities, we are not good at peaceful resolution."},{"kind":"para","text":"The leaders in this state (alone) are prone to try and do anything and everything they can against the Lord and His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"David was experiencing a time in Israel's history (as I've said) where there were a lot of enemies around them."},{"kind":"para","text":"If it wasn't from the Philistines, it would be from another country, or even right in their own camps."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, David felt at peace in the middle of war."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was not afraid of the battle."},{"kind":"para","text":"Fighting and war seems scary, but God gives provision and comfort."},{"kind":"para","text":"He gives strength and boldness."},{"kind":"para","text":"I was asked recently about what I thought about being drafted into war in a foreign country. I said, \"At the stage that our country is currently at, I would not be for it. Our leadership is involved with wars they shouldn't be involved with. I would not like to fight those wars for them.\" Then they asked, \"Well what if they came to the borders of Florida?\" I said, \"Well that's a different situation, then I would have no problem fighting and protecting my country.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It's not because I am proud of my country by the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's because I have people I love here."},{"kind":"para","text":"I would want to do whatever it takes to protect them."},{"kind":"para","text":"If the fight comes to my doorstep, you bet your bottom dollar I will be at the frontlines."},{"kind":"para","text":"David had boldness in the middle of fighting because He knew the Lord was with him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He didn't have to go INTO the battle, the battle usually came to him."},{"kind":"para","text":"When the battle came to him, God always protected him, and provided for the people."},{"kind":"para","text":"This includes with Goliath where David takes his first victory."},{"kind":"para","text":"Same with Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"It might have seemed like Jesus kind of just gave up at the end."},{"kind":"para","text":"He allows His own death to happen."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't seem as if He actually cared about His friends and disciples."},{"kind":"para","text":"But He protected them every step of the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at how many times the disciples were in the middle of trouble throughout the gospel, and how many times Jesus stood up for them or calmed a storm."},{"kind":"para","text":"When Jesus was crucified, that was His ultimate way of standing up for His disciples."},{"kind":"para","text":"How?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Greater love hath no man than this, that a man lay down his life for his friends.","ref":"John 15:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"He gave His life for the world, and it is His friends who will receive that love."},{"kind":"para","text":"He gave His life for His disciples."},{"kind":"para","text":"They understood that when He rose again and showed Himself to them."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is why they were bold enough to stand up for the church moving forward."},{"kind":"para","text":"They gave their lives for Christ who gave His own life for them."},{"kind":"para","text":"They had no fear standing in the midst of war and having confidence in the Lord that whether they were going to live it would be for victory in Jesus, or whether they were going to die, it would be for victory in Jesus."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the end, glory to God!"}]}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"title":"The House of God","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"David didn't have a house for the Lord yet."},{"kind":"para","text":"It was a promise given to him through his lineage, but at the moment of this writing, he is speaking about a future hope."},{"kind":"para","text":"He, in fact, never gets to see the house of the Lord be built."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the New Covenant, the house of the Lord is the people!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Know ye not that ye are the temple of God, and that the Spirit of God dwelleth in you? If any man defile the temple of God, him shall God destroy; for the temple of God is holy, which temple ye are.","ref":"1 Corinthians 3:16-17"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are God's house!"},{"kind":"para","text":"So when we \"dwell in the house of the Lord all the days of my life...\" we are actually dwelling in our own bodies until our death."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are with the Lord every day from the moment we wake up to the moment we fall asleep."},{"kind":"para","text":"The time in between is a moment of refreshing our battery, but we are still with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are a Christian today, it should be your hearts desire to be with the Lord every waking moment of your life."},{"kind":"para","text":"We GET to behold the beauty of the Lord, and to enquire in His temple."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Enquire\" means \"to ask for information.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"That means we can come to God and literally speak to Him and He will give us answers and directions on what to do."},{"kind":"para","text":"People think Christians are crazy for praying to a being they can't even see or hear, and expecting Him to answer in some fashion or another, yet it's evidentially true that He actually DOES answer us."},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn't need to, but He wants to."},{"kind":"para","text":"It, honestly, baffles me whenever He answers my prayer."},{"kind":"para","text":"I feel so undeserving."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet we get to enquire of Him every day, and He literally just tells us to ask Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you:","ref":"Matthew 7:7"}]}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"title":"Protection From Trouble","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I have talked to many people about post-tribulation/pre- tribulation rapture and the differing viewpoints."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have never stood affirmatively on one side or the other and that seems to upset some people."},{"kind":"para","text":"The fact of the matter is, I could argue both sides as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Because we don't have enough absolute information on either side, I do not choose sides."},{"kind":"para","text":"But here is what I WILL say about it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn't matter which one happens, because God is able to hide us in the \"secret\" of His tabernacle, and set us upon a rock (that cannot be destroyed or broken)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The secret (by the way) is the place of sacrifice in the temple."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is where Christ is."},{"kind":"para","text":"So when we are hidden in Christ, we are protected no matter which form of rapture might happen."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are raptured up before the tribulation, GREAT, God has protected us."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are raptured up after the tribulation, GREAT, God has protected us."},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, God will protect us, and it is something He is still doing for us even right now!"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Notice the type of sacrifice David is mentioning here."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is sacrificing his joy!"},{"kind":"para","text":"That does not mean he is getting rid of it, it means that he is OFFERING it to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord loves a joyful giver;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Every man according as he purposeth in his heart, so let him give; not grudgingly, or of necessity: for God loveth a cheerful giver.","ref":"2 Corinthians 9:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"Singing praises with joy brings glory to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will protect, and He will guide, and that gives every single one of us explicit purpose to rejoice and sing to Him in victory and comfort!"}]}]},{"start":7,"end":13,"title":"The Hopeless Dead","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It seems that there has been a bit of a shift from what we have been reading in the first half of this Psalm."},{"kind":"para","text":"We were under the impression that David felt pretty victorious."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think that is the outward display of Christ by the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ was bold, and victorious even in the face of evil and terrible people trying to reject Him and destroy Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"But now we are getting the background thoughts of David, and I believe these were the thoughts of Christ too."},{"kind":"para","text":"Outwardly He displayed boldness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Inwardly, He continuously prayed for sustainability and continuance."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was 100% man mind you."},{"kind":"para","text":"His inward thoughts were on furthering protection, not just for Himself, but for the people around Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord had mercy on the Lord, even during the time of His crucifixion."},{"kind":"para","text":"He felt the full pain of the cross, absolutely, but the Lord was merciful to relieve that pain rather quickly."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe the Lord died faster than most people would on the cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is why they usually break the legs of those on the cross so they couldn't lift themselves up to breathe anymore."},{"kind":"para","text":"They didn't need to do that to Jesus though because He was already dead before they could."},{"kind":"para","text":"God extends that mercy to everyone else."},{"kind":"para","text":"The moment that Christ died, that was the access point to the mercy of God for all generations."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you want God's mercy, you must go through Christ's sacrifice."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This verse is gold!"},{"kind":"para","text":"If God tells you to seek His face, it is a wise person's duty to do just that."},{"kind":"para","text":"And when we go to seek the Lord's face, we should do it with everything we've got."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have not seen the face of the Lord yet, but I certainly have seen the grace of the Lord in my life."},{"kind":"para","text":"The more I seek His face, the more I am filled with grace!"},{"kind":"para","text":"The crazy part of this verse (here) is that it says his \"heart said\" that he will seek His face."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our hearts do not naturally seek after the Lord in anything."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The heart is deceitful above all things, and desperately wicked: who can know it?","ref":"Jeremiah 17:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded.","ref":"James 4:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"\"But the LORD said unto Samuel, Look not on his countenance, or on the height of his stature; because I have refused him: for the LORD seeth not as man seeth; for man looketh on the outward appearance, but the LORD looketh on the heart.\" 1","ref":"Samuel 16:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"David says, \"When the Lord asked me to seek His face, my HEART said that it would.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"That is not the natural man."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the man of Christ!"},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ was a man that had a heart for God."},{"kind":"para","text":"No matter what happened, His heart said, \"I will do this for the Lord.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"We will not have a heart to do that without the heart of Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we accept Christ, we have a renewed heart for the Lord!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh.","ref":"Ezekiel 36:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have Christ's heart for the things of eternity, rather than our old bitter and selfish heart of stone."},{"kind":"para","text":"God says to do it, it is wise for us to do it."},{"kind":"para","text":"You will not see the Lord's face by the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think that should be well understood right away."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said, Thou canst not see my face: for there shall no man see me, and live.","ref":"Exodus 33:20"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"No man hath seen God at any time; the only begotten Son, which is in the bosom of the Father, he hath declared him.","ref":"John 1:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"So why would God ask anyone to seek His face?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well, there will be a day when we will be in front of the Lord in judgement."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are seeking His face today, we will prepare ourselves for the moment we see Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are squandering that command, we will never see His face and live..."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we pass from this life, it is certain that we will all be in front of the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"We are confident, I say, and willing rather to be absent from the body, and to be present with the Lord.","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that have Christ will see God's face."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that do not, will be case into eternal torment."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will be in front of God in judgement, but they will not see His face."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will, instead, receive a second death."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they had hair as the hair of women, and their teeth were as the teeth of lions.","ref":"Revelation 9:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"\"You are either born twice and die once, or you are born once and die twice.\" D.L. Moody"},{"kind":"para","text":"Use this life to prepare yourself to face the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"You will eventually do it one day, and this life is the training ground for when that takes place."},{"kind":"para","text":"Seek His face today, and you will be ready to look at His face in eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"What a great moment for all of Christendom."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Sin causes God to turn away."},{"kind":"para","text":"There's nothing more heartbreaking to the Christian than to break the heart of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"God looks at the heart, but He also HAS a heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is ultimately what is happening when we sin, we are simply breaking God's heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"That should not be the desire of any man who is reading this today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Breaking God's heart is not something we should try and look for."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are a Christian today, you must understand that your sin breaks His heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, repentance turns God back towards you."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is a forgiving and merciful God who is desirous to maintain and keep His relationship open with His children."},{"kind":"para","text":"Praise the Lord He has given us access to His mercy."},{"kind":"para","text":"Praise God for Christ's sacrifice that allows us the gift of continually searching out the face of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"His salvation keeps His presence close."},{"kind":"para","text":"Without it, we would have a work ahead of us to grow connection to the Lord that would never succeed because even our thoughts are sinful."},{"kind":"para","text":"Praise God it does not depend upon what WE do in order to maintain our salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is GOD who is our salvation, not our works."},{"kind":"para","text":"David understands that, and Jesus PROVES it."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We sadly live in a world where fathers and mothers forsake their children."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now this doesn't always happen, but it happens more than I think society likes to admit."},{"kind":"para","text":"Children are growing up in rapid pace without authority figures."},{"kind":"para","text":"They (perhaps) LIVE with their parents, but they are not TRAINED by their parents."},{"kind":"para","text":"Society is the one training them."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord can take them forward if they would turn to Him, but that is not where society will usually lead them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Thankfully David knows the Lord, and so if his parents had ever decided to completely disown him, he still had family and motivation from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is his family."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is our family as well."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But as many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God, even to them that believe on his name:","ref":"John 1:12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, what manner of love the Father hath bestowed upon us, that we should be called the sons of God: therefore the world knoweth us not, because it knew him not.","ref":"1 John 3:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are part of the family of God the moment we accept Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are adopted into His kingdom."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Having predestinated us unto the adoption of children by Jesus Christ to himself, according to the good pleasure of his will,","ref":"Ephesians 1:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"To redeem them that were under the law, that we might receive the adoption of sons.","ref":"Galatians 4:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"We may be disowned by the world (and even the people who are supposed to love us the most), but the Lord will never forsake His own."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let your conversation be without covetousness; and be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.","ref":"Hebrews 13:5"}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"By the way, people are going to watch to see you fall."},{"kind":"para","text":"They probably won't have to wait long either."},{"kind":"para","text":"That does not mean their validation is what promotes your walk with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather, you must admit your faults and say, \"I am a sinful man. I know I am not worthy to be called a Christian let alone a leader in ministry. If there is no forgiveness for what I have done, I completely understand, because I do not deserve it.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The desire of all ministers, however, is that God would just keep them on a simple and easy path through life so there is no chance of falling or going the wrong way."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is usually not what happens though, but it's still a nice thought that David is praying for here."},{"kind":"para","text":"To Jesus, the plain path was His life."},{"kind":"para","text":"It was simple."},{"kind":"para","text":"He knew exactly what He was going to do, where He was going to do it, and why He needed it to be done."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not such simple creatures."},{"kind":"para","text":"We SHOULD be though."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should make it dumber, honestly."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will make it so much easier to just go in the right direction when we are not overcomplicating everything because we think it's too easy."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes the easiest route is the smartest one."},{"kind":"para","text":"Other times we might have to take a more complicated approach (only because it's the right thing to do, not because it's the better thing to do)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Doing what's right should always be easy is what I'm trying to get at."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, it's often the hardest thing to do, because people don't often agree with what you think is right (even though God literally says that it is the right thing)."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It's funny because the people during Christ's days were calling Jesus a \"false witness.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"They were trying to accuse Him of blasphemy and heresy, when it was pretty obvious that it was the religionists that were guilty of that."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus (God in the flesh) cannot blaspheme or lie."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is not possible for Him to do that."},{"kind":"para","text":"David was worried about being given to his enemies due to his own sin, but Christ was given to the enemy due to OUR sins."},{"kind":"para","text":"They were cruel, and they were liars, murderers, and false witnesses."},{"kind":"para","text":"They hated Christ so much that they actually broke their own law that they tried to accuse Christ of breaking."},{"kind":"para","text":"For some reason it is okay for them to do it, but not okay for us."},{"kind":"para","text":"One time my dad and I were leaving a McDonalds to head towards a jobsite (I worked in construction). When we left the parking lot, my dad was putting his seatbelt on at the same time. As soon as he got on the freeway, a cop pulled him over. The cop noted that he didn't have his seatbelt all the way on before he left his parking space. My dad said, \"I put it on, I was just in motion when I did it, is this really worth all of this time and effort spent? I have to get to work.\" The cop said, \"It's a danger and it's against the law so I will have to write you a ticket.\" \"Okay, what's the ticket for exactly.\" my dad asked. \"For not wearing your seatbelt.\" the cop responded. \"But I AM wearing my seatbelt, just because I put it on a little late doesn't make it illegal. Show me the law that says I have to put my seatbelt on before I leave my parking spot.\" My dad replied. \"It's officers discretion\" the cop said. My dad ended up taking the ticket, and as we watched the cop drive past us, the cop put his seatbelt on while the car was in motion..."},{"kind":"para","text":"He just broke his own law."},{"kind":"para","text":"By the way, there was no \"officers discretion\" law that stated you can get a ticket for putting your seatbelt on while the car is in motion."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was just being a dirty cop, and a jerk."},{"kind":"para","text":"The religionists of Christ's day were being just as arrogant and prideful."},{"kind":"para","text":"Except their arrogancy ultimately leads to Christ's death even though He was completely innocent."},{"kind":"para","text":"This world is unjust in every turn, but the Lord is always just."},{"kind":"para","text":"The unjust rulers will not go unpunished, that is a promise."},{"kind":"para","text":"Until then, there will sadly be many casualities of innocent people."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not because the Lord doesn't care (He certainly does. If He didn't care, He wouldn't have allowed His son to die on the cross)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather He allows these things to happen because He will have final judgement for them."},{"kind":"para","text":"The innocent people will be taken care of by the Lord, even if they are not taken care of by the world..."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God's goodness is always somewhere to be found."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not in the land of the living by the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are in the land of the dead."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"We are travelling through the land of the dead on our way to the land of the living.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, I think that is what provides the believer with so much hope and necessity to continue forward."},{"kind":"para","text":"They know there is goodness in the land that they are traveling to."},{"kind":"para","text":"There's nothing good here."},{"kind":"para","text":"We would faint if this is all we have."},{"kind":"para","text":"But I'm so glad God gives us glimmers of hope for this living land."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm so glad He reminds us every once and a while that there is something better awaiting us."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes we forget about it, and God will have to grab ahold of us, and show us some grace and compassion so we see the bigger picture."},{"kind":"para","text":"May we remember God's goodness in this dead land."}]}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"title":"Wait on the Lord","entries":[{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Another golden verse."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes that is what we need."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think I need to write a book on this because we are living in a society that is very fast paced."},{"kind":"para","text":"That was a theme I used at a teen camp we did one year."},{"kind":"para","text":"I preached on three topics about \"waiting\" on the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems that everything is telling us to go go go, but the Lord tells us to sit and wait."},{"kind":"para","text":"There should be seasons where that is all we can do."},{"kind":"para","text":"I hope you get a chance to wait on God."},{"kind":"para","text":"I hope the Lord provides you with that opportunity."},{"kind":"para","text":"Tone back a little bit, and sit with God."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what we should all be doing anyway."},{"kind":"para","text":"We get so caught up on moving forward, and getting ahead, that we forsake the quiet peace and tender presence of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are rushing to seek His face, rather than just waiting on Him to tell us HOW to do it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Ministry workers are the most guilty of this rushed lifestyle."},{"kind":"para","text":"All it does is cause bitterness and drag."},{"kind":"para","text":"We suddenly become used up and empty, and then depression sets in and we don't know what to do anymore."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has given us sign after sign to step back and wait, and we do not take that seriously."},{"kind":"para","text":"I hope we will take a moment for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus took plenty of moments to sit and wait on God."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what kept Him doing ministry with joy."},{"kind":"para","text":"He had a renewed compassion for people every time He took a moment to be with the Lord and be refreshed."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what we all need to do if we want to love others properly."},{"kind":"para","text":"Take a moment to wait on Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Be encouraged by Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Have your heart STRENGTHENED by Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then it is responsible to move forward by Him."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14}]},
    "28": {"chapter":28,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last chapter, David spoken about how we should have confidence in our salvation, keeping our eyes and hearts set on the house of God (the presence of God), how God will protect us from trouble that comes into our lives, the importance of seeking the Lord in the land of the living, and the necessity to WAIT on the Lord in every season of life.","In this chapter, we still see the necessity to hold Christ. The world will try and sway you into holding onto everything EXCEPT Christ, but scripture makes it clear that nothing is more stable and more worthy than holding onto the Lord of all creation. He is solid, and trustworthy. There is no one else that we can trust to hold onto except for Him."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Hold Christ","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We need the Lord's voice and presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"I had lived a life without the Lord, and it was quite lonely."},{"kind":"para","text":"Depression and anxiety was my theme, and because of it I hated life."},{"kind":"para","text":"I cried unto God quite a few times in life before I was a believer."},{"kind":"para","text":"I never heard Him answer me."},{"kind":"para","text":"Looking back, He was always answering me but I was just too ignorant and selfish to notice."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord had always been trying to get my attention and I was always rejecting it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ relied on the Lord's voice and guidance through His entire life and ministry."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even in the very end we see Him praying to the Lord about letting the cup of suffering pass from Him, yet the Lord answers what must be done."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus knew that He would have to suffer that death."},{"kind":"para","text":"He had already suffered it."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was there before it took place."},{"kind":"para","text":"He felt the pain throughout history."},{"kind":"para","text":"As soon as the first sin was committed, Christ bore the pain of the cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the tribulation period, they will only be able to rely on the Lord's voice."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is all we must rely on today."},{"kind":"para","text":"If the tribulation happened tomorrow in an instant, would you be able to lean on the voice of the Lord alone to get you through it?"},{"kind":"para","text":"If the rapture didn't happen until later (or you missed the rapture and turned to Christ after the tribulation had commenced) would you lean on God?"},{"kind":"para","text":"In those days, it will be all you have to lean on."},{"kind":"para","text":"You won't have anything else to keep you going, so you will have to find His voice and leading."},{"kind":"para","text":"Otherwise, without Him, you are heading for \"the pit\" (which is the grave and eternal hell fire)."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"A child of God should be reaching for God through every season."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no direction to cling to but up towards His \"holy oracle.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Oracle\" means \"The holy of holies.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It is the place in the temple that the sacrifice was made."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what we are reaching toward."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are reaching towards the sacrifice of the Lord (which is Jesus Christ)."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the only one that can keep our heads above water when the storm comes."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the only one that keeps us afloat."},{"kind":"para","text":"He can get us through."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are in a painful place today, reach for the holy oracle."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is there and willing to pull you close."},{"kind":"para","text":"Embrace Him like your life depends on it, because it certainly does."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":5,"title":"The Works of the Wicked","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked in this world are an enticing bunch."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is very easy for any of us (even the strongest Christians among us) to be swayed into sin and wicked living."},{"kind":"para","text":"Quite recently a pastor that I have enjoyed studying with throughout the years wrote a letter of resignation from his post. He has been a pastor for forty years or so. It took many people by surprise. I don't know what the problem was, but he wrote in his letter that he was struggling with some sort of sin that has caused him to step down from his pastorate. To everyone on the outside, it seemed that he was a great example of a holy man, but there was something that had taken ahold of him somewhere that swayed him into a wicked lifestyle."},{"kind":"para","text":"You, reading this today, can fall into that same trap."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must be very careful."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the end times, there will be a lot of people who are swayed away from the God of the Bible."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some of them were never really pursuing God to begin with, while others were just beginning to seek, or were close to salvation before the anti-Christ makes it difficult to live without honoring him."},{"kind":"para","text":"The anti-Christ will make it so that if you don't turn away from the Lord, you will not have an easy time living on this Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"You say, \"Well now I don't think that will happen to me, I am a strong Christian and no one can sway me.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Just look at COVID."},{"kind":"para","text":"People were willing to get the shot just so they can get free meals from local restaurants, or so they could keep their jobs."},{"kind":"para","text":"They weren't even allowed to buy groceries in some areas without the shot."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even then they had to get boosters and all sorts of things to keep up to date with the ability to live a normal life in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"It still isn't normal today."},{"kind":"para","text":"There were many Christians who were quick to give up church and even their own faith so they could live in comfort in this world through these vaccines and government mandates."},{"kind":"para","text":"It would not be hard for Satan to control and sway people (even people of \"faith\")."},{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked will entice you in this world, and they will tell you how much easier it is to just simply cave to the government authority, and they will try and justify not following the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are doing that now, and it will just become common language in the future."},{"kind":"para","text":"May we learn to stand strong, though, and search out the Lord with everything we have."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You have probably heard the saying, \"Give them their just deserts\" before.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It comes from David here."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is saying that the wicked deserve what they are getting because it's what they asked for."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a treat to them, and they will eat it like a treat, but it will just make them sick."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what desert does to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"It sounds good in the moment, and so I engorge myself with it, and then regret ever taking that first bite after I am finished."},{"kind":"para","text":"I feel more sick because I had too much of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what will happen to the wicked of this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will get what they ask for, and they won't feel better about life."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will just feel sick."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will literally give them what they want."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Is it because God wants to hurt them and take all of their chances of salvation away from them?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course not!"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have studied extensively already throughout scripture that God is a God of second, third, fourth... hundredth chances."},{"kind":"para","text":"He gives too many chances if I could be honest."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are all undeserving of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"No, rather the reason they will get what they ask for is because God knows they won't take any more chances from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"So He just lets them have what they want."},{"kind":"para","text":"David says it in the next verse:"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They don't care about the Lord and they never will."},{"kind":"para","text":"I hate to say this, and I'm not one for bad news, but there are going to be some people on this Earth who are simply just lost causes."},{"kind":"para","text":"This does not mean we should just roll over and give up on those we claim to love because we don't know if they are a lost cause or not."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather this should give us MORE urgency because we really DON'T know if they are a lost cause or not."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be pleading with their soul, and pleading with the Lord if we truly love them like we say we do."},{"kind":"para","text":"God wants to give them a chance, but He will only do that if they are willing to actually TAKE His salvation upon themselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"He, ultimately, knows who will be saved and who won't be."},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't know."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord purposely doesn't let us know so we can have urgency for EVERY soul, not just to the ones WE deem are worth our pleading."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will see in the last days that there will be a great wicked city that is built up."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord will allow them to build their city, but HE will not be the builder of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be the power of the people that builds it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be the power of the Lord that tears it down."},{"kind":"para","text":"If God does not build it, it will not last."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":7,"title":"The Lord Helps","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The world does not understand this verse."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't understand that God would listen and answer."},{"kind":"para","text":"To the world, they write it off as a fluke, or as a happenstance, and not as a providence from the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't think God is really paying attention or actually really cares."},{"kind":"para","text":"It must be so miserable to have no hope for a miracle that they would so desire to see come true."},{"kind":"para","text":"It must be miserable to see a loved one in the hospital dying from some sort of disease and think, \"They have nothing ahead of them in their eternity, and there is no hope for them on this Earth.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"It is a true loss to the Atheist."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Christian knows there is a hope for every soul."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether it's Heaven through Jesus Christ, or Hell through rejection of Him, that is up to the individual person."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, I would rather my family end up in eternal torment than to believe that they just disappear for all of eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"It makes everything in this life seem so useless and depressing."},{"kind":"para","text":"If I believe there is a Hell, then it should burden me to think that there are family members going there."},{"kind":"para","text":"If I don't believe that, then I have no burden for my family at all, and the love I have for them is nothing more than shallow and superficial."},{"kind":"para","text":"I could never really love anybody without the burden of eternity resting on my conscience."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Praise the Lord for strength."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don't get me wrong, I often feel very defeated, but I usually can find strength for the day through the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even through a difficult problem in life, I have found that praying with a burden, and relying on the Lord always provides me with boldness and strength to do the right thing and the best thing for the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He always provides clarity and direction."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is always there to help when we need it, and it brings us into a Spirit of rejoicing and praise!"},{"kind":"para","text":"We can praise Him even in the most bleak circumstances that comes our way."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is always there to provide for us if we are willing to just beg and wait for Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"We don't even necessarily need to beg Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"We just need to plead with Him, and then trust He will do what HE wants with the situation."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must trust that HE know's what is best, even if it doesn't look like something we are going to enjoy."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must trust Him wholeheartedly if we are going to find Him as a help."},{"kind":"para","text":"Otherwise we will grow bitter towards the Lord thinking we know better than what He is actually giving us."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"title":"Saved For Ever","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Who are the \"anointed?\""},{"kind":"para","text":"The ones that accept the Lord as their salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Who accepts the Lord's salvation?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The one's in which God chooses."},{"kind":"para","text":"Who does God choose?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The one's that will trust His saving strength."},{"kind":"para","text":"You are just as anointed as any other man of God today."},{"kind":"para","text":"You are chosen like any other if you are willing to turn to God's saving strength."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has proven His strength through Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what Christ came here for."},{"kind":"para","text":"He came here to save the whole world that would desire to turn to Him for salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must reject our strength, and trust HIS strength if we are going to have salvation though."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will save those that trust Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is a guarantee by me, by Jesus, by the prophets, by the Apostles, and by David:"}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once saved, always saved."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom ye also trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation: in whom also after that ye believed, ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise,","ref":"Ephesians 1:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"God will not take back what He has freely given to you."},{"kind":"para","text":"He does not save by accident."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't understand those false religionists who think or preach a message about \"losing\" your salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"If God made an accident by saving you, then He is either not perfect, or not Holy and Just."},{"kind":"para","text":"He saves those with pristine accuracy though, and anyone that is saved today is because He has accepted you with no stipulations attached."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even if you have accepted Him and continue in sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you have truly accepted Him today, you are saved."},{"kind":"para","text":"Period."},{"kind":"para","text":"No one can take that away from you, not even the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"He won't take it away."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a gift to you \"for ever.\""},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I give unto them eternal life; and they shall never perish, neither shall any man pluck them out of my hand. My Father, which gave them me, is greater than all; and no man is able to pluck them out of my Father's hand.","ref":"John 10:28-29"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the gifts and calling of God are without repentance.","ref":"Romans 11:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"A good barometer to test your salvation status should be your desire to sin though."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you have no conviction about your continued sin, then it is likely that you don't love the Lord like you think you do."},{"kind":"para","text":"You should love God enough that you feel bad for breaking His heart with your sin..."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9}]},
  },
};
